],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T22:09:54-08:00","id":831504,"title":"","content":"I like that the new Character creation rules allow for the 5-dot contracts at creation now, provided they're in-seeming.<br /> <br /> That was possibly one of my biggest bug-bears with 1E that it was difficult to have an Elemental that could turn into Ice at creation or whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1462,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","user":"Xenesis","date":". 02-17-2016, 01:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T23:44:23-08:00","id":831540,"title":"","content":"I love, <i>love</i> that people are seeing what I've been seeing for so damn long.<br /> <br /> Now someone invite me to their playtest, I don't have a game going on and I haven't played Changeling in ages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T23:55:41-08:00","id":831544,"title":"","content":"wow, this just totally made my day. I was eating when I first saw this and literally dropped my fork. I really like the new contracts (vainglory is as glorious as it should be), the embracing the wyrd rules are great, I love how dropping the mask interacts with contracts too. The extended lifespan from having high wyrd is great, way better than the 1e version of it, especially with Forever and a Day. The fading magic rules are also fantastic, I love that you included a way for changelings to drop their template mechanically, rather than just making it a fully narrative event.<br /> <br /> I am really looking forward to seeing the goblin vows and pledge rules now, given how well everything else has been reworked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T23:55:48-08:00","id":831545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks#post831430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a lot of content. Thought y'all might be interested in poking around it.<br /> <br /> Because I love you.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-the-lost-tinkering-and-toying/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-th...ng-and-toying/</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I love you too :O","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T00:07:40-08:00","id":831554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=831544#post831544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am really looking forward to seeing the goblin vows and pledge rules now, given how well everything else has been reworked.</div> </div> </div> </div>Enjoy Pledges. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2K8R3qXyDyoZEgzZ0U0V1M0Wk0/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2K8R3qXyDyoZEgzZ0U0V1M0Wk0/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2K8R3qXyDyoZEgzZ0U0V1M0Wk0/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2K8R3qXyDyoZEgzZ0U0V1M0Wk0/view?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T00:08:20-08:00","id":831556,"title":"","content":"It looks great, and I'm eager to see the finished book.<br /> <br /> Changelings definitely received a power bump like vampires and werewolves in their second editions.<br /> <br /> I do have a few questions and comments:<br /> <br /> 1. The iron explanation and distinctions definitely still need some work to avoid confusion and arguments, particularly any differentiation from steel if that is the intent. While I understand that most people don't have usable steel swords and similar archaic weapons, items like steel pipes, crowbars, hunting and work knives and axes, shotgun slugs and shot, arrow broadheads, etc. are common, and items like steel chains and police handcuffs that seriously impact changelings inherent escape capabilities are ubiquitous.<br /> <br /> 2. If you simultaneously Embrace the Wyrd and scour your Mask, does the use of contracts still benefit from the Exceptional Success bonus?<br /> <br /> 3. I believe Reticent is a fairly harsh and long lasting Condition and a little inconsistent with claims that Harvesting doesn't actually harm the subject and is not necessarily predatory.<br /> <br /> 4. Does Clarity provide a bonus to resist all magic and supernatural effects or only those that affect a changeling's perception?<br /> <br /> 5. For Kenning. what constitutes the &quot;presence of magic&quot; in an area? Is this like Mage 2e's Peripheral Mage Sight which only detects 'active' supernatural effects like the use of Vampire Disciplines, Werewolf Gifts, and Mage spells, or does Kenning also automatically attempt to detect the mere presence of anything supernatural in nature or origin like the mere presence of a vampire or werewolf? If the latter, are mages without active spells considered inherently supernatural?<br /> <br /> 6. The Character Creation spoiler twice lists Experience costs for Morality. Is this a placeholder for Clarity?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T00:10:09-08:00","id":831557,"title":"","content":"I was about to say, it seems like we're missing pledges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T00:15:11-08:00","id":831558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=831556#post831556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 6. The Character Creation spoiler twice lists Experience costs for Morality. Is this a placeholder for Clarity?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Some of this stuff will get a clarification later on. But this, yes, it was a placeholder when we were still in discussion about anchors and integrity analogues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T00:44:34-08:00","id":831567,"title":"","content":"Copied/reworked from my comments, just so it's here, and a bit more:<ul><li>I think Dreamwalking should use Dream Form rules like other gamelines it's been mentioned for, at least when mentioning non-changelings. A universal baseline would be nice for crossover, or even just for being better able to transfer between games. As it is, it seems very, very difficult to handle a situation where both are involved.</li> <li>Character creation seems all good, except the template document mentions a free specialty but the character creation doesn\u2019t mention that at all, unless I missed it?</li> <li>Really like that you built into the core that other supernatural senses can beat the mask by default, rather than using the somewhat difficult mask piercing system from 1e. Mask strengthening does imply that only fae can use the clash of wills, though, is that intentional?</li> <li>I love the mechanics for scouring away the Mask and having that enhance your fae side a bit in the form of contract bonuses, as well as causing you some hardships with gates and implementing the Bewitched condition (which I also love). I do think the distance on the drawbacks is a little high though.</li> <li>The scar bit is a nifty, flavorful tidbit, I like that.</li> <li>I like that cold iron has more of a bite on Changelings now, doing agg to them in addition to true fae.</li> <li>Caging a Dream is awesome, simply put, and well made to not be an instant I Win.</li> <li>Embracing the Wyrd seems a little potent, but it\u2019s hard to say for sure since it does have a drawback and likely needs to be seen in play for me to be sure.</li> <li>Incite Bedlam is much cooler, but I think it should come into play earlier than Wyrd 6; that always felt like an unneeded prerequisite.</li> <li>The Reticent condition seems like it\u2019s a bit too potent of a drawback to characters targeted by a harvest; it hardly seems like nobody\u2019s harmed if they\u2019re losing all willpower and keeping it off, especially since it lasts for so long. Almost makes them worse for a community than Vampires (at least high humanity rarely-kill vamps). Too many changelings? Suddenly have a town of zombies...</li> <li>Clarity\u2019s benefit against all magic seems to be a bit high to me. I think it might be better if you use the same perception chart and have that modify the willpower bonus (so, Clarity 6 gives +4 or -3).</li> <li>By contrast, I do love kenning being reflexive, usable by all, and costless if you\u2019re at Clarity 5+.</li> <li>I went through merits and Contracts too. Only thing that lept out (other than liking the majority of them a lot) for merits is that Rigid Mask is a bit much as an auto-win against non-supernatural attempts, at least for the cost. Contracts I'm going back and forth about, mostly that their power levels don't always seem to match the dot rating, but that's the sorta thing I'd have to playtest.</li> </ul><br /> As a note, I do want to try all of this out. I need to see if I can convince the ST for the Victorian Lost game we\u2019re starting up soon to let us use these rules, so I can give some actual playtest feedback, instead of just blabbing about my at-a-glance opinion &gt;_&gt;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T01:27:23-08:00","id":831588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=831567#post831567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]Incite Bedlam is much cooler, but I think it should come into play earlier than Wyrd 6; that always felt like an unneeded prerequisite.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll confess in my 6 years of CTL, I've never seen Incite Bedlam in play for precisely that reason, that no one tends to get to more than Wyrd 4-5 before the end of our Chronicles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T01:38:39-08:00","id":831590,"title":"","content":"Cool! Thanks for sharing.<br /> <br /> So far I'm just skimming but I do have a question. If you were playing the bad faerie from Sleeping Beauty, how would you curse SB to prick her finger and die? It looks like Tying The Knots of Fate is the Contract you want, but that one explicitly says you can't specify the outcome - no &quot;and die&quot;?<br /> <br /> I'm glad to see that the Mirror Contracts are in there. I'm not sure if anyone's figured it out yet, but I have a thing for magic mirrors.<br /> <br /> The new Hidden Reality looks awesome. It should probably give a contested dicepool for the Fairest version though, the guard you modify might be a player charachter.<br /> <br /> I'm not too keen on the definition of iron. Under the old rules, you had to intentionally acquire iron. That meant that a Changeling with an iron weapon is making an important statement, and a Hunter had to do research and identify their target. When every melee weapon is iron by default you loose that. My suggestion would be to use a more narrative definition rather than a chemical one. If a metallurgist would call it iron (including things like &quot;pig iron&quot;) then it counts. If they call it something else, like steel, then it doesn't count. You say you don't know anyone with a steel sword; but I'd wager your friendship circle contains few Changelings or monster hunters.<br /> <br /> I'd really like a contract that synergises with Caging a Dream; so that nobody can notice you escape until they look at where you're not with their own eyes. That wriggling sack they're carrying turns out to actually be full of twigs.<br /> <br /> Oathbreaker Condition is awesome.<br /> <br /> I think I prefer the new Bargains system over the old get magic stuff from the Wyrd system (Pity Demon doesn't have it too). But how do you Ensorcell someone in 2E?<br /> <br /> The new Hollow Merit is exceptionally awesome, but I do wish it had an equivalent of the Hollow Doors Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 02-17-2016, 04:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T01:58:32-08:00","id":831602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=831590#post831590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not too keen on the definition of iron. Under the old rules, you had to intentionally acquire iron. That meant that a Changeling with an iron weapon is making an important statement, and a Hunter had to do research and identify their target. When every melee weapon is iron by default you loose that. My suggestion would be to use a more narrative definition rather than a chemical one. If a metallurgist would call it iron (including things like &quot;pig iron&quot;) then it counts. If they call it something else, like steel, then it doesn't count. You say you don't know anyone with a steel sword; but I'd wager your friendship circle contains few Changelings or monster hunters.</div> </div> </div> </div>A metallurgist (and a great many other people) would make little distinction between iron and steel, except to note that steel is basically iron with fewer impurities. That's precisely why in a lot of fantasy literature the fae are affected by steel, a ubiquitous substance in the modern world.<br /> <br /> The differentiation of &quot;cold iron&quot; as being wrought by hand without magic or mass-production is far easier to understand narratively or mythologically than any apparent difference between iron and steel.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T02:01:52-08:00","id":831604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=831588#post831588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll confess in my 6 years of CTL, I've never seen Incite Bedlam in play for precisely that reason, that no one tends to get to more than Wyrd 4-5 before the end of our Chronicles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, same here.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, just noticed pledges were put up too! I do like them, but sort of miss the open ended building block nature of 1e pledges. I know the whole 'free stuff' thing got out of hand really quickly, though, and I'm glad to see that toned down. Still, the way the systems are rolled up is nice, taking a lot of stuff that was optional or added later in 1e (unwitting pledges becoming sealings, for instance), and making it all nice and easy by comparison to how it used to be while still being flavorful.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T02:05:18-08:00","id":831605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=831588#post831588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll confess in my 6 years of CTL, I've never seen Incite Bedlam in play for precisely that reason, that no one tends to get to more than Wyrd 4-5 before the end of our Chronicles.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I'll be changing this. Maybe Wyrd 3~. Not sure yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T02:06:35-08:00","id":831609,"title":"","content":"I'm liking a lot of what I'm seeing, though I'm not through it all. In the Mask and Mein part, why does the section immediately after that say 'Masque' instead of Mask? I think it'd be better to go with Mask, to make sure you're differentiating it from that other product line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/287-wildfire","name":"Wildfire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T02:33:25-08:00","id":831617,"title":"","content":"All right.<br /> First off: David A Hill is an awesome guy, and for this, he deserves a holiday dedicated to himself. (DaveB also deserves one, but it should be darker and scarier. Like Halloween. But that's neither here nor there.)<br /> <br /> Secondly, I have a few things I'd like to comment about some of the Contracts! In general, they are just... amazing. I love them. But some of them sparked questions in me, especially the catches. I'll try to list them here.<br /> <br /> Blessing of Perfection is the one that I have the most issues with. The Catch hinges on two rather rare things happening at once. That you do this for someone you have just met, will not happen often. Doing something in exchange for a small favour, is also not going to happen very often. Now, this Catch hinges on you doing something with an object that belongs to someone you just met, AND that you do it in exchange for a small favour. Either one or the other is rare enough, I'd say.<br /> Second nitpick: Why does the Catch only work to alleviate half of the uses for the Contract? There is no way to fulfil the Catch if one uses it to boost oneself.<br /> Third nitpick: Exceptional on four successes? I thought de rigueur was to have it on three? (This one, I admit is whiny, but shouldn't the game try to be consistent?)<br /> <br /> Mirror Walk, I don't have as much a problem with, as I'm unsure as to how it works exactly. Do you have to know that there is a reflective surface you aim at? Can you 'scan' for reflective surfaces near where you want to go?<br /> <br /> Game Master's Table lacks an Exceptional effect. Does this mean to say that there isn't one, or did it accidentally get cut?<br /> <br /> With Portents and Visions, once again the Catch confuses me. Does the Catch mean a picture of the target AS a child, or does it require a picture the target MADE as a child? (Also, how does this apply to things that were born adult? I got the impression that Oneiroi just spawn fully grown out of dreams. Same with Huntsmen, True Fae, et cetera. I have no problem with them being un-Catchable, I am just curious.<br /> <br /> Hidden Reality. Now... This is a Catch I think is rather pointless. Isn't one of the big things with Changelings that they can't be confined? Or does it simply mean that this grants them more options to escape? In which case, it's not pointless, and I am stupid.<br /> <br /> Finally, Chrysalis. I simply don't understand how the Catch works. It might again be just me who is stupid, but perhaps the phrasing could use some stupid-proofing?<br /> <br /> <br /> Apart from these things, I simply loved everything that was given out. It's simply glorious. Thank you David for doing this. And of course, thank you all writers who contributed. (You can't let David get ALL the glory for this, can you?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T03:10:31-08:00","id":831626,"title":"","content":"Couple of other things that jump out at me as I skim:<br /> - The new Pledge system seems fantastic - simple enough, but broad and rewarding. And I love Sealings, because they enable the concept of <i>watch your words around the fae</i> and the Wyrd as an indiscriminatory binding force in a way that 1e didn't.<br /> - Others have mentioned it, but Reticent seems very punishing. The consequences are somewhat dissonant from the relatively innocuous description of Harvesting, and turn the viability and moral quality of the act on its head. I'm, hmmm, not sure what to feel about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 02-17-2016, 06:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T03:24:19-08:00","id":831628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=831448#post831448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still looking at a final wording. But, honestly? I'm not too concerned. I don't know anyone that owns a steel sword. I can't remember the last time I saw one that wasn't in a locked display case.</div> </div> </div> </div>(holds hand up)<br /> <br /> Yeah, I own a sword.<br /> <br /> He didn't work on Changeling, but Malcolm Sheppard actually does longsword fighting as a martial art, too. He's pretty good at it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{