lineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T04:35:57-08:00","id":831653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=831649#post831649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Middle Ages were frightening <b>Dark Era</b> for the changelings. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> All this Iron all around them as steel...<br /> <br /> What an <i>Iron</i>y. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I do not think different ages presenting different challenges to a kind of supernatural is a serious issue. It is a bit like vampires having to worry less about blazing torches in the modern day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T04:59:00-08:00","id":831666,"title":"","content":"<b>Thoughts on Changeling 2ED Playtest rules</b><br /><br /> My little compilation of question and comments on shown rules. More to come in next post packages. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Character Creation:</b><ul><li>(After checking with rest of files) <b>Virtue and Vice are changed in to Mask and Mien archetypes, yes?</b> Mask is Virtue replacement, Mien of Vice one?</li> <li><b>Long Term Aspirations</b> <i>should</i> grant Beat after each game session the lead problems for character until resolution.</li> <li>Morality(?) \u2013 Probably Clarity should be in text \u2013 will be buy able back with Experience?</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T05:18:55-08:00","id":831679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=831666#post831666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Thoughts on Changeling 2ED Playtest rules</b><br /><br /> My little compilation of question and comments on shown rules. More to come in next post packages. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Character Creation:</b><ul><li>(After checking with rest of files) <b>Virtue and Vice are changed in to Mask and Mien archetypes, yes?</b> Mask is Virtue replacement, Mien of Vice one?</li> <li><b>Long Term Aspirations</b> <i>should</i> grant Beat after each game session the lead problems for character until resolution.</li> <li>Morality(?) \u2013 Probably Clarity should be in text \u2013 will be buy able back with Experience?</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>[*] I'm fairly certain both are replaced by both. Just like for Vampires and Werewolves.[*] That's how I run it at least.[*] Nope. The Clarity preview document states rather clearly that breaking point success, Seeming Blessings, and a few powers are the only ways to raise it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T05:23:14-08:00","id":831681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=831679#post831679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*] I'm fairly certain both are replaced by both. Just like for Vampires and Werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves Bone is Virtue replacement and Blood is of Vice, it clearly stated in the text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T05:44:33-08:00","id":831685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=831681#post831681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Werewolves Bone is Virtue replacement and Blood is of Vice, it clearly stated in the text.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Where does it say? Because I can only find this:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Your character possesses traits called Blood and Bone.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">They reflect a core dichotomy of the Uratha condition. A<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Blood archetype reflects your character\u2019s behavior and identity<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">on the hunt, when claws are out, and lives are on the line. A<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Bone archetype reflects your character\u2019s sense of self-identity.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">It\u2019s who she is behind the instincts, fur, and fury.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> And this:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Anchors keep Uratha grounded. They\u2019re concepts, philosophies, people, places, and things that help her find herself<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">when lost. <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Bold\"><b>Werewolf: The Forsaken </b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">characters have three<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Anchors: Blood, Bone, and Touchstones.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Blood and Bone act as a dichotomy. Blood is the visceral, hot instinct brought on from deep within. Bone is the<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">personal firmament that identifies the fleshy human under<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">the fur and claws.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> If you mean that you use Bone instead of Virtue in Social Interaction, well of course! You are off the hunt. Using Blood would be seriously odd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T05:57:55-08:00","id":831692,"title":"","content":"I thought Mein was virtue and Mask is Vice, simply because it makes acting like your true self in an important situation worth more while you get tempted to just do mask a lot in the same way you're tempted to do vice a lot because it's an easy way to regain your willpower.<br /> <br /> Edit: Do you pick an element when you take the Cloak of the Elements Contract or do you pick it when you use the contract?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 02-17-2016, 09:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T06:19:51-08:00","id":831696,"title":"","content":"This is incredible. I haven't had time to do more than a quick read but I really like everything I've seen. One thing that immediately jumped out to me was the Beast affinity for Might of the Terrible Brute. One complaint I had with 1e was that it was basically impossible for dex based melee to compete with strength because all the contracts were strength based. I am so pleased to see this.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm very impressed with the Merits. They maintain the flavor and general concept from Rites of Spring but with new mechanics that make me want to use them, which was generally not the case previously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T06:34:15-08:00","id":831703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=831443#post831443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The definition of iron has abit of an issue, since steel swords and steel daggers meet the definition of iron given. Unless that was intentional.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is as it should be. Faerie's power waned with advent of the iron age and now resurges with the ubiquity of plastics and other polymers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T06:36:45-08:00","id":831704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=831685#post831685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you mean that you use Bone instead of Virtue in Social Interaction, well of course! You are off the hunt. Using Blood would be seriously odd.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean main concept and pointing of their change in Gifts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WtF 2ED, p. 86</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When your character makes a clearly bad choice in the heat of the moment in accordance with her Blood archetype, she regains a spent Willpower point. If she takes it a step further, submitting to Kuruth or calling a hunt on a whim in accordance with her Blood archetype, she refreshes all her spent Willpower points.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does sound a lot of like Vice definition - from Wolf-Blooded rules later (<b>WtF</b> 2ED, page 90):<br /> &quot;Vice is a point of vulnerability or weakness within her.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WtF 2ED, p. 86</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When your character forces down her rage, and takes action with what she fundamentally knows as true, if it\u2019s in accordance with her Bone archetype, she regains a Willpower point. When she stands her ground and lets her rational mind interfere with the hunt, or cause conflict within the pack, she refreshes all her spent Willpower points.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does sound a lot o like Virtue definition -<br /> &quot;Virtue is something fundamental within the character which reaffirms her inherent strength and integrity.&quot;<br /> <br /> And <i>Dream Hunter</i> Gibbous Moon Facet ( <b>WtF</b>, page. 118 ) has connection of those:<br /> <br /> &quot;The Cahalith hunts through the dream for fragmentary thought-beasts and figments, discovering one of the following about the prey: roughly where the prey is in the physical world, <b>his Blood and Bone (or Vice and Virtue or other equivalent traits)</b>, any steps he is taking to try to protect himself from the hunt, an impression of his immediate surroundings.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T06:40:01-08:00","id":831707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=831556#post831556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. The iron explanation and distinctions definitely still need some work to avoid confusion and arguments, particularly any differentiation from steel if that is the intent. While I understand that most people don't have usable steel swords and similar archaic weapons, items like steel pipes, crowbars, hunting and work knives and axes, shotgun slugs and shot, arrow broadheads, etc. are common, and items like steel chains and police handcuffs that seriously impact changelings inherent escape capabilities are ubiquitous.</div> </div> </div> </div>I might not worry about this. Iron and steel are very difficult to differentiate since pure iron is harder to make than any of its many ferrous alloys (e.g., wrought iron, steel, etc.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":". 02-17-2016, 09:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T06:48:57-08:00","id":831714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=831628#post831628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(holds hand up)<br /> Yeah, I own a sword.<br /> He didn't work on Changeling, but Malcolm Sheppard actually does longsword fighting as a martial art, too. He's pretty good at it.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair Dave, I suspect you and Malcolm are nerds like me who spent much of your teenage years playing D&amp;D and Vampire: the Masquerade. The average person doesn't own a sword. Given the tone of the Chronicles of Darkness setting I expect that nerds like us (and I'm including everyone on these and other boards) are even rarer there than in our own world. So very, very few people <i>in situ</i> probably have access to steel in a form that they might think to employ against a Changeling.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Ultimately, let us not fret too much about the iron rules. If the final text provides some permutations of them in the storyteller chapter that might be good (e.g. only cold-wrought steel -- aka cold iron, etc.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T07:04:17-08:00","id":831718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=831666#post831666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Thoughts on Changeling 2ED Playtest rules</b><br /><br /> My little compilation of question and comments on shown rules. More to come in next post packages. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Character Creation:</b><ul><li>(After checking with rest of files) <b>Virtue and Vice are changed in to Mask and Mien archetypes, yes?</b> Mask is Virtue replacement, Mien of Vice one?</li> <li><b>Long Term Aspirations</b> <i>should</i> grant Beat after each game session the lead problems for character until resolution.</li> <li>Morality(?) \u2013 Probably Clarity should be in text \u2013 will be buy able back with Experience?</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Clarity will not be purchasable with Experiences. It can only be gained through play. <br /> <br /> Mask and Mein are the replacements, yes. Which is which isn't too important. <br /> <br /> And long-term aspirations should be that wya. I'll be sure to note it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T07:05:11-08:00","id":831719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=831692#post831692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Do you pick an element when you take the Cloak of the Elements Contract or do you pick it when you use the contract?</div> </div> </div> </div>When you purchase the Contract. If you have Fire Cloak, that's what you've got.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T07:17:24-08:00","id":831726,"title":"","content":"Glad to hear those comments, <b>DaveH</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=831718#post831718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mask and Mein are the replacements, yes. Which is which isn't too important.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is whole &quot;Virtue helps in Social Maneuvering&quot; thing in general new <b>CoD </b>rules. It <i>is</i> one of important mechanics for social interactions.<br /> <br /> I'm mainly <b>Mage</b> ST and like to dwell in to Mind Arcanum powers and related phenomena. When going with 2ED <b>Changeling</b> characters in crossover scenarios I will need to mark what is &quot;Virtue-like&quot; and what is more &quot;Vice-like&quot; from Mask and Mein archetypes, just to judge how powers will act on them.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure, but there are also many other things like those in <b>CoD</b> gamelines - For example, Underworld's touch on mind of those that inside so when Lost will come to Great Below it would be easier to point how they interplay with &quot;Vice and Virtues are reversed in mechanics&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-17-2016, 10:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T07:20:17-08:00","id":831727,"title":"","content":"never had a chance to play/ST Changeling, but I reeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeally want to right now.... :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T07:39:32-08:00","id":831731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=831554#post831554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Enjoy Pledges.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2K8R3qXyDyoZEgzZ0U0V1M0Wk0/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2K...ew?usp=sharing</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You beautiful bastard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T07:40:29-08:00","id":831732,"title":"","content":"Making a character right now. But the merits Touchstone and Exotic Airs are nowhere to be seem. T_T","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":7210,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","user":"Horodrigo","date":". 02-17-2016, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T08:04:11-08:00","id":831742,"title":"","content":"So I just finished reading Pledges and that is AWESOME. Though I will miss the old pledge system, I hated how it was a mix of hard rules and wildly non-specific systems. This one is absolutely drowning in flavour and I love it.<br /> <br /> But I'll miss giving myself +3 brawl and some merits to go along with it out of nowhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T08:05:15-08:00","id":831743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=831703#post831703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is as it should be. Faerie's power waned with advent of the iron age and now resurges with the ubiquity of plastics and other polymers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, based on how the ban was worded, plastics are bound to become new iron. Woe to the changeling daring to use a plastic cup. Or a keyboard. Or a toilet seat.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T08:35:03-08:00","id":831760,"title":"","content":"This is absolutely awesome! I'm going to start brushing off my setting notebooks and putting some finishing touches onto things and try to get a game going with my mates. Looks like some great stuff MachineIV! I especially like that the Thorn and Bramble Contracts lived on. Always my absolute favorite ones. I do have a few little comments for the Contracts though! Nothing major.<ul><li>Cloak of the Elements<ul><li>Do the armor values and damage stack when an Elemental has multiple versions active?</li> <li>For immaterial elements that can't cause damage (Darkness) do you think the Contract should instead reduce penalties caused by sed element?</li> </ul></li> <li>Creeping Dread<ul><li>The Fairest power seems super out of place. Maybe swap the Fairest and Beast powers around with Mirror Walk and let Beasts force someone to run away from themselves?</li> </ul></li> <li>Fang &amp; Talon<ul><li>The mode of transportation power is a bit unclear how it works with birds for flight, and burrowing animals. But, that one feels just to be due to this being a rough copy than any issues.</li> </ul></li> <li>Inanimate Communication<ul><li>Does the Darkling Shadow-Copies work as 100% true copies? If one copied a thumb drive, would it contain all the same information for example?</li> </ul></li> <li>Changing Hours<ul><li>Freeze the Clock: Ah yeah! This Contract. This Contract has always been a bit... tricky. Making an Immovable Object is a weirdly powerful tool. But, the big thing is no duration is given for the effect.</li> <li>The Fairest sub-power really needs a big blurb explaining what happens when you de-age a person. That one I can see being a big confusing.</li> </ul></li> <li>Mirror Walk<ul><li>The Beast version of this seems really out of place. Maybe swap it with the Fairest Creeping Dread? The mechanics of the effect also seem strange. Dramatic Failures are pretty much constantly the 'something terrible happens' bit, and having a power that specifically circumvents that seems weird.</li> </ul></li> <li>Game Master's Table<ul><li>Nothing at all to do with mechanics. The original version of it had a really nice bit of fluff explaining why a Changeling may chose to use different games depending on the situation which was very cool. It'd be brilliant if that could make it in again.</li> </ul></li> </ul>But, the stuff still looks brilliant! Looking forward to seeing the Court Contract stuff. Unless I've managed to miss it somehow which is quite possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T08:47:06-08:00","id":831767,"title":"","content":"Thank you. I'm looking forward to this game so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10751-belac93","name":"Belac93","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10751_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T08:51:38-08:00","id":831772,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Freehold Creation</b></span><ul><li><b>Rebuilding a Broken Bulwar -</b><i>&quot;</i><i>When a Bulwark breaks, the freehold can rebuild it at the next time the ritual would normally be performed. It should never be taken lightly or done too easily, even if the Bulwark ritual occurs frequently. The more quickly and easily the ritual is, the harder their enemies will strike when the opportunity presents itself.&quot;</i></li> </ul><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Should not this be the other way around?</b> When True Fae are satisfied with Tale of Sheherezada Courts should the be less aggressive if story is not told this particular time \u2013 only that leave it on two, three days and you are never sure if Gentry did not use the time to send Huntsmen or other forces. On the other hand \u2013 if you have only one ritual a year it can hell break everything. Ritual <b>must</b> succeed, or you will need to wait whole year without defense of Bulwark \u2013 and True Fae can attack any time in this year period! One WIDE open defense problem against many smaller ones, but eating day to day time of Freehold members<b>. </b></div><ul><li><b>Approaches</b> \u2013 <i>I do not get logic of this. </i><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> If Approaches highlight the things members of particular Court are great one \u2013 <b>WHY Huntsman will challenges them at these ways?</b> Why Huntsman start occult duel with Autumn courtier when he has much more probability on the physical contest footing with him ( and probably classical Chase scene to catch Autumn Courtier ). Particularly, as Courtiers with Mantle 4+ make Huntsman to first goes for Personal Approach of changeling. <b>WHY Huntsman need to abide this rules when she can just break the rules and not try to get Yearning? </b></li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-17-2016, 12:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T08:54:30-08:00","id":831774,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Core Template Rules</b></span><ul><li><b>Mask &amp; Mien</b> - Is <i>Bewitched (Condition)</i> new version of ensorcellement of mortals? <b>Are Ensorcelled using this Condition for modeling their powers of seeing past the Mask?</b></li> <li><b>Iron Bane </b>\u2013 <b>Actual rules works more or less like DaveH posted a month ago on forum?</b></li> </ul><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/808613-2ed-changeling-weakeness?p=808794#post808794\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...794#post808794</a><br /> <br /> <i>\u2018Because &quot;cold iron&quot; is a really subjective term, and would largely reflect things that aren't by any means practical tools or weapons. So, if it's iron enough that people think of it as iron, it's iron, and it counts. Cast iron, wrought iron, cold iron, dramatic irony, if it's iron, it's iron. (\u2026) So, iron, that which is perceived to be iron (by who, I have to ask), cuts through fae magic. Contracts, Tokens, Hedgespun Artifacts, the like-Iron cuts through it.<br /> <br /> Cold Iron is defined as iron that has been shaped by hand - no machines beyond simple ones, no magic to shape or transform it. Cold Iron does aggravated damage to faeries. Strangers, Huntsmen, Hobgoblins, and Changelings, they all burn under cold iron's caress. Should a fairy touch cold iron, they subtract their Wyrd from all dice pools.\u2019</i><br /> <br /> <b>So does not this point to </b><u>not work</u><b> with Steel, as thought generally use \u201cSteel =/= Iron\u201d in language does not miss this Bane? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </b></div><ul><li><b>Caging the Dream</b> - <i>This ability to escape applies to all grapples (see p. XX) with non-supernatural attackers. She must use a Clash of Wills against supernatural attackers.</i></li> </ul><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> <b>So does this mean that if werewolf goes over changeling with his jaws, werewolf use his Grapple dicepool Strength + Brawl with bonus from Form and changeling is rolling Wyrd and\u2026 what? Larceny? Dexterity? Some Contract?</b></div><ul><li><b>Embracing the Wyrd \u2013 Do I get it right that character that is still under Mask seems dream-like but still mortal looking for those around him? </b>He may seem a bit taller and more intimidating, but more or less looks still as the normal Mask version of himself?</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-17-2016, 12:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T08:58:01-08:00","id":831778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=831726#post831726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Glad to hear those comments, <b>DaveH</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> There is whole &quot;Virtue helps in Social Maneuvering&quot; thing in general new <b>CoD </b>rules. It <i>is</i> one of important mechanics for social interactions.<br /> <br /> I'm mainly <b>Mage</b> ST and like to dwell in to Mind Arcanum powers and related phenomena. When going with 2ED <b>Changeling</b> characters in crossover scenarios I will need to mark what is &quot;Virtue-like&quot; and what is more &quot;Vice-like&quot; from Mask and Mein archetypes, just to judge how powers will act on them.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure, but there are also many other things like those in <b>CoD</b> gamelines - For example, Underworld's touch on mind of those that inside so when Lost will come to Great Below it would be easier to point how they interplay with &quot;Vice and Virtues are reversed in mechanics&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know. Reversing the mechanics in Changeling will have absolutely 0 effect. They are functionally identical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T09:04:37-08:00","id":831786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=831772#post831772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Approaches</b> \u2013 <i>I do not get logic of this. </i><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> If Approaches highlight the things members of particular Court are great one \u2013 <b>WHY Huntsman will challenges them at these ways?</b> Why Huntsman start occult duel with Autumn courtier when he has much more probability on the physical contest footing with him ( and probably classical Chase scene to catch Autumn Courtier ). Particularly, as Courtiers with Mantle 4+ make Huntsman to first goes for Personal Approach of changeling. <b>WHY Huntsman need to abide this rules when she can just break the rules and not try to get Yearning? </b></div> </div> </div> </div>The Huntsman does not have to obey by Court Approaches. They just <i>really really want to</i>, because they use Yearning for all their abilities, and a Huntsman that runs out of Yearning suffers <b>untold excruciating pain</b>, &quot;dies&quot; and then is reformed 2 weeks later to start all over again. A Huntsman will do <i>anything</i> to avoid running out of Yearning, even if that means challenging a Summer courtier to a sword duel. And no, a Huntsman can't really just &quot;not spend Yearning.&quot; A Huntsman that doesn't use their abilities is never going to get to their prey.<br /> <br /> I think Personal Approaches might <i>have</i> to be obeyed, I don't remember. But IIRC Court Approaches are optional but really, really appealing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T09:22:10-08:00","id":831803,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Wyrd Table</b></span><ul><li><b>Incite Bedlam - </b>I concours that Incite Bedlam should start earlier, other ways it will not be seen in most Changeling games -<b> Maybe Wyrd 3 will be best place to start it? And then next usage per next 2 Wyrd dots \u2013 so \u201cTwice per chapter\u201d at Wyrd 5, \u201cOnce per session\u201d on Wyrd 7, with Wyrd 9 and 10 without changes?</b></li> <li><b>Frailties \u2013 I\u2019m not sure if they should not start at Wyrd 1</b> \u2013 it has logic that character take back one of this from the time of Durance and what his overall narrative in Arcadia remake him. And each new Frailties after next 2 Wyrd dots. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></li> <li><b>Goblin Fruits \u2013 Changeling can have simply up to Wyrd dots of Goblin Fruits with herself? </b></li> <li><b>Pledges \u2013 Same as Goblin Fruits? Character can have up to Wyrd dots of Pledges on herself active at once?</b></li> <li><b>Glamour Addiction \u2013 I like idea, but, once again \u2013 writing it as starting from the Wyrd 6+ makes it non-existent problem in most of run games where majority ( if not all ) of characters are Wyrd 5 and lower. Also, this rule:</b></li> </ul><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><i>\u200b\u201cAdditionally, a changeling at 0 Glamour begins to suffer from both physical deprivation, as though starving, as well as suffering the effects of the Condition. No matter how much she eats or drinks, she cannot gain nourishment until she possesses at least 1 point of Glamour. This penalty applies to any changeling, not just the most powerful.\u201d \u2013 </i><br /> <b><b>Should be on start of the Addiction paragraph. </b>I want to know rules concerning all changelings first hand, not from middle of text block. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></b></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T09:40:09-08:00","id":831826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=831448#post831448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm still looking at a final wording. But, honestly? I'm not too concerned. I don't know anyone that owns a steel sword. I can't remember the last time I saw one that wasn't in a locked display case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, hey, missed this. I also own a steel sword!<br /> <br /> I don't know why anymore, but I got it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T09:41:05-08:00","id":831827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=831774#post831774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Core Template Rules</b></span><ul><li><b>Iron Bane </b>\u2013 <b>Actual rules works more or less like DaveH posted a month ago on forum?</b></li> </ul><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/808613-2ed-changeling-weakeness?p=808794#post808794\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...794#post808794</a><br /> <br /> <i>\u2018Because &quot;cold iron&quot; is a really subjective term, and would largely reflect things that aren't by any means practical tools or weapons. So, if it's iron enough that people think of it as iron, it's iron, and it counts. Cast iron, wrought iron, cold iron, dramatic irony, if it's iron, it's iron. (\u2026) So, iron, that which is perceived to be iron (by who, I have to ask), cuts through fae magic. Contracts, Tokens, Hedgespun Artifacts, the like-Iron cuts through it.<br /> <br /> Cold Iron is defined as iron that has been shaped by hand - no machines beyond simple ones, no magic to shape or transform it. Cold Iron does aggravated damage to faeries. Strangers, Huntsmen, Hobgoblins, and Changelings, they all burn under cold iron's caress. Should a fairy touch cold iron, they subtract their Wyrd from all dice pools.\u2019</i><br /> <br /> <b>So does not this point to </b><u>not work</u><b> with Steel, as thought generally use \u201cSteel =/= Iron\u201d in language does not miss this Bane? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </b></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, cold iron refers specifically to hand-forged steel quenched in one of the following three substances -- ice, snow, or ice-water. You can look these up.<br /> <br /> These represent the rarest of rare hand-forged steel blades and the very few swordsmiths I know don't forge swords this way because it's labor intensive (although one gets really well-bonded high-carbon steel though because of the very rapid cooling).<br /> <br /> You might be able to find handforged Japanese swords that are actually forged this way but they go for thousands of dollars (and more usually you'll find tons of swords that purport to be made this way but are simply hand-forged and quenched in (not ice-cold) water or (far more likely) are actually cast. &quot;Fakes&quot; abound and I wouldn't be above letting players find &quot;cold iron&quot; weapons only to discover the hard way that they're actually cast steel and no better than wrought iron alloys against faerie magics. False advertising is a thing.<br /> <br /> Also steel == iron because no one makes pure iron for anything. (The steel making process is literally replacing one impurity with a different one kind of like ethanol out competing methanol after you've ingested both.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":". 02-17-2016, 12:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T09:45:42-08:00","id":831828,"title":"","content":"I already posted in another thread how I'll be handling cold iron (and iron in general). Iron is mankind's labour. Steel is fit for nobility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T09:47:30-08:00","id":831832,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar70_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"70\" data-vbnamecard=\"70\">MachineIV</a> Read through the rules, really good stuff. I'm especially excited for the dream / dreamscape rules. Although now I'm doubly disappointed that we didn't get similar rules for nightmares and the primordial dream in Beast. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T10:05:41-08:00","id":831841,"title":"","content":"Having trouble parsing either of the seeming affinity bonuses for Light-Shy.<br /> <br /> Also, Night's Subtle Distractions and Light-Shy seem to have more mechanical overlap than should be present on two Contracts of the same rating with nominally different conceptual bases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 02-17-2016, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T10:26:31-08:00","id":831855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=831774#post831774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li><b>Embracing the Wyrd \u2013 Do I get it right that character that is still under Mask seems dream-like but still mortal looking for those around him? </b>He may seem a bit taller and more intimidating, but more or less looks still as the normal Mask version of himself?</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Embracing the Wyrd with the Mask up:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://youtu.be/lKaw5SjeHx0\" data-code=\"lKaw5SjeHx0\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/lKaw5SjeHx0/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> Embracing the Wyrd and dropping the Mask:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://youtu.be/spHEw2n9LwE\" data-code=\"spHEw2n9LwE\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/spHEw2n9LwE/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T10:30:32-08:00","id":831862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=831841#post831841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having trouble parsing either of the seeming affinity bonuses for Light-Shy.<br /> <br /> Also, Night's Subtle Distractions and Light-Shy seem to have more mechanical overlap than should be present on two Contracts of the same rating with nominally different conceptual bases.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Darkling bonus for Light-Shy seems very on-point, IMO. The Wizened one, I feel, is evoking the whole &quot;the staff are invisible to the people they're serving&quot; feel.<br /> <br /> Light-Shy and Night's Subtle Distractions are overlapping a fair bit, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T10:39:12-08:00","id":831866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=831827#post831827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Actually, cold iron refers specifically to hand-forged steel quenched in one of the following three substances -- ice, snow, or ice-water. You can look these up.<br /> <br /> These represent the rarest of rare hand-forged steel blades and the very few swordsmiths I know don't forge swords this way because it's labor intensive (although one gets really well-bonded high-carbon steel though because of the very rapid cooling).<br /> <br /> You might be able to find handforged Japanese swords that are actually forged this way but they go for thousands of dollars (and more usually you'll find tons of swords that purport to be made this way but are simply hand-forged and quenched in (not ice-cold) water or (far more likely) are actually cast. &quot;Fakes&quot; abound and I wouldn't be above letting players find &quot;cold iron&quot; weapons only to discover the hard way that they're actually cast steel and no better than wrought iron alloys against faerie magics. False advertising is a thing.<br /> <br /> Also steel == iron because no one makes pure iron for anything. (The steel making process is literally replacing one impurity with a different one kind of like ethanol out competing methanol after you've ingested both.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iron_in_folklore\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Horseshoe_shaped_wind_chime_with_bells.jpg/960px-Horseshoe_shaped_wind_chime_with_bells.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iron_in_folklore\" target=\"_blank\"> Iron in folklore - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iron_in_folklore\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iron_in_folklore </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Against faeries, though, it has always just meant &quot;Iron&quot;. Any backtracking on that in roleplaying games is only for game balance purposes. It's like saying &quot;cold, hard steel&quot; as an expression.<br /> <br /> Now, those game balance purposes might be perfectly desirable in a roleplaying game about playing people who have been warped by the Gentry into faeries, but &quot;cold iron&quot; doesn't mean a specific Japanese forging method. It just means Iron.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T11:21:28-08:00","id":831896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=831540#post831540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love, <i>love</i> that people are seeing what I've been seeing for so damn long.<br /> <br /> Now someone invite me to their playtest, I don't have a game going on and I haven't played Changeling in ages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anyone up for a forum game then? I may have ideas. Evil, evil ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T11:23:58-08:00","id":831900,"title":"","content":"Do they involve a high school?[/sarcasm]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T11:27:09-08:00","id":831908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=831772#post831772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Rebuilding a Broken Bulwar -</b>[I]&quot;<i>When a Bulwark breaks, the freehold can rebuild it at the next time the ritual would normally be performed. It should never be taken lightly or done too easily, even if the Bulwark ritual occurs frequently. The more quickly and easily the ritual is, the harder their enemies will strike when the opportunity presents itself.&quot;</i><br /> <b>Should not this be the other way around?</b> When True Fae are satisfied with Tale of Sheherezada Courts should the be less aggressive if story is not told this particular time \u2013 only that leave it on two, three days and you are never sure if Gentry did not use the time to send Huntsmen or other forces. On the other hand \u2013 if you have only one ritual a year it can hell break everything. Ritual <b>must</b> succeed, or you will need to wait whole year without defense of Bulwark \u2013 and True Fae can attack any time in this year period! One WIDE open defense problem against many smaller ones, but eating day to day time of Freehold members.</div> </div> </div> </div>The easier the Bulwark is to restore, the smaller the window of opportunity to strike at a vulnerable Freehold. When promptly fixing the Bulwark is neither possible or simple, the Others and their servitors have greater allowance and time to prepare for devasting incursions, and there is less urgency driving them.<br /> <br /> On a different topic, I really like how Embracing The Wyrd feels (the Tolkien examples where characters suddenly become more threatening and loom terrible and great are on point!) and I think the benefits scale appropriately with your supernatural might. And I finally get what was said about the power of dropping the Mask. That the significance of the act has the repercussions it does in regards to Hedgegates and your visibility in the Wyrd feels extremely fitting without making me think that it's always going to be too risky. I asked myself several times why I would ever want to drop the mask in 1e, given how impractical and lacking in an outright advantage it was, but in 2e? I can see many situations where it would be useful and a risk worth taking, and there's a lot more substance in it, both mechanical and narrative.<br /> <br /> Speaking of, I find it interesting how some Contracts seem to<i> tempt you</i> to drop the mask to grasp their full power, because doing so allows you to achieve some permanent advantage. It tells of that magic leaving a mark, transforming you the more you take, rewarding you with an extension of its effect. That's effin' cool and speaks volumes of the transfigurating influence of the Wyrd on Changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 02-17-2016, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T11:27:56-08:00","id":831909,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Glamour</b></span><ul><li><b>Harvesting from Emotions</b> \u2013 I <i>really </i>like those rules. I was going more on the idea of that Harvested lose on <i>point</i> of Willpower, not all of them \u2013 but this is much more profound and powerful. With Reticent Condition, changelings are now somehow \u201cpsychic predators\u201d, using tricks of their True Fae once masters. <i>I love this!</i> &lt;3</li> </ul><ul><li><b>Harvesting from Emotions</b> - <b>Does Harvesting in this way also rep all of victims Willpower?</b> Cause it sounds it should be a bit more like one <i>point</i> in this example, as they are not so \u201cpalpable\u201d. They are just dreams, not \u201cliving\u201d emotions. <b>Or maybe up to point of Willpower for each Harvestered Glamour point in dreams?</b></li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Clarity</b></span><br /> <br /> As I mentioned it in recent topic, just after showing of new rules <b>\u2013 <i>I still need to highlight that each Trigger should have two versions, Common and Specific. Common would leave penalty like -1 and Specific like -3.</i> </b>Common would be general events and typical life complications \u2013 Common Trigger could \u201cromantic relations\u201d for character that lost a husband to True Fae in Durance. Then going to romcom with friends will be Common Trigger for character. Specific Trigger would be \u201cSeeing lost husband\u201d, when player and Storyteller assumes that it\u2019s totally changed person after Durance and plays of Gentry.<br /> <br /> <b>EACH Trigger for any changeling should have those Common and Specific versions so players would need to have highly specialized and very general ones!</b> In that way Storyteller will not be a dick for putting characters with Specific only ones over very extreme world coincidence so Clarity would be tested for super snowflake characters. Or the one with high Common like that could go down in Clarity five times quicker with general worded Trigger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-17-2016, 02:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T11:29:29-08:00","id":831911,"title":"","content":"@Yolf:I know, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T11:35:32-08:00","id":831915,"title":"","content":"I do have one question regarding the mask-stripped contract bonus: Assuming the mask still doesn't exist in the hedge (add frankly it would be absurd if it did) do contracts get a bonus there too? It does seem thematic for fae magic to just flat-out work better in fae realms, but just to be sure...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"li