div> </div>I did not find the <b>Touchstone</b> merit either. Can someone please explain to me how they work with this splat(bonus and stuff)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T15:28:48-08:00","id":832121,"title":"","content":"I wonder what the odds are of some sort of merit (or style merits) that increases ones ability at Pledgecrafting to somewhat resemble the 1E version? At first I was wholly glad it was gone, but I believe there is some merit (hah) in using lower-case &quot;c&quot; contracts to place yourself in the Role of a Narrative, and thus receive bonuses according to Role you are now in. As an example, promising someone you'll be their Guardian, and then getting physical skills and/or merits. Just an idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T15:29:48-08:00","id":832123,"title":"","content":"Goblin vows still give a little of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T15:41:19-08:00","id":832131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As I mentioned it in recent topic, just after showing of new rules <b>\u2013 <i>I still need to highlight that each Trigger should have two versions, Common and Specific. Common would leave penalty like -1 and Specific like -3.</i> </b>Common would be general events and typical life complications \u2013 Common Trigger could \u201cromantic relations\u201d for character that lost a husband to True Fae in Durance. Then going to romcom with friends will be Common Trigger for character. Specific Trigger would be \u201cSeeing lost husband\u201d, when player and Storyteller assumes that it\u2019s totally changed person after Durance and plays of Gentry.<br /> <br /> <b>EACH Trigger for any changeling should have those Common and Specific versions so players would need to have highly specialized and very general ones!</b> In that way Storyteller will not be a dick for putting characters with Specific only ones over very extreme world coincidence so Clarity would be tested for super snowflake characters. Or the one with high Common like that could go down in Clarity five times quicker with general worded Trigger. </div> </div> </div>No. Each trigger already has at least two versions. Having only two would not stop a storyteller from being a dick if the storyteller is a dick, especially since the player has input on whether something actually would count as a breaking point for their character. Also the &quot;seeing lost husband&quot; is ridiculously specific. What if they found the wedding ring? Why wouldn't that trigger anything beyond the Common, which would happen upon finding any wedding ring. The current system allows for you and your storyteller to work out what actually matters to your changeling and it's so tightly restricted as your &quot;Two-Trigger&quot; method which weakens roleplaying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T15:45:55-08:00","id":832135,"title":"","content":"Does Fae Mount follow the same rules as Hollow (that is, you can have more than five dots, but the merit is not considered higher than that if such things are counted) or is the Merit actually limited to five dots?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T16:35:54-08:00","id":832171,"title":"","content":"I <i>think</i> it's a five dot limit. I dunno, there was some questioning about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T16:41:34-08:00","id":832173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=832171#post832171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I <i>think</i> it's a five dot limit. I dunno, there was some questioning about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think right now, I'm in favor of a 5-dot limit. But I don't think it's a huge deal either way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T16:48:48-08:00","id":832182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=831909#post831909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I mentioned it in recent topic, just after showing of new rules <b>\u2013 <i>I still need to highlight that each Trigger should have two versions, Common and Specific. Common would leave penalty like -1 and Specific like -3.</i> </b>Common would be general events and typical life complications \u2013 Common Trigger could \u201cromantic relations\u201d for character that lost a husband to True Fae in Durance. Then going to romcom with friends will be Common Trigger for character. Specific Trigger would be \u201cSeeing lost husband\u201d, when player and Storyteller assumes that it\u2019s totally changed person after Durance and plays of Gentry.<br /> <br /> <b>EACH Trigger for any changeling should have those Common and Specific versions so players would need to have highly specialized and very general ones!</b> In that way Storyteller will not be a dick for putting characters with Specific only ones over very extreme world coincidence so Clarity would be tested for super snowflake characters. Or the one with high Common like that could go down in Clarity five times quicker with general worded Trigger.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I explained when you brought it up before, each Trigger <i>already has</i> a specific expression and a general expression, the way it's written now. You just don't get varying penalties for the specific or general version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T17:10:09-08:00","id":832194,"title":"","content":"1. One of my players said he wants his fae mount to be a balloon animal horse and I cannot figureout if he is being sincere or not.<br /> 2. My character concept is lucky that he wasn't big on his Court so I don't have to worry about only having universal contract clauses :P<br /> 3. ... and now I'm going to be stuck spending the next few hours trying to figureout how precisely his contracts alter his mein.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T17:11:23-08:00","id":832195,"title":"","content":"I feel like I'm missing something, but Dropping the Mask vs. Embracing the Wyrd feel narratively like slightly different flavours of the same thing...or more that Embracing Wyrd is basically a souped up version of Dropping the Mask. Like, I'm not sure whether you'd want to roll those two into a single mechanic, or if there's a reason for separating them?<br /> <br /> Also, is there any actual mechanical benefit for dropping your mask when Embracing Wyrd - do you still get the contract bonus? The text seems to suggest no, but I'm not sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member"