thing that exists&quot; due to a lucky strike by a Huntsman or <i>especially </i>Thief of Reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's reasonable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T19:19:12-08:00","id":832254,"title":"","content":"Ooh, saving grace of agency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T20:20:37-08:00","id":832296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=831862#post831862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Darkling bonus for Light-Shy seems very on-point, IMO. The Wizened one, I feel, is evoking the whole &quot;the staff are invisible to the people they're serving&quot; feel.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't doubt they're fitting, I'm saying that the Darkling bonus references &quot;the target&quot; on a user-affecting Contract and I can think of very few circumstances in which one would have to remain motionless for longer than a scene and spending singular extra points of Glamour would be unacceptable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T20:30:15-08:00","id":832298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=832296#post832296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't doubt they're fitting, I'm saying that the Darkling bonus references &quot;the target&quot; on a user-affecting Contract and I can think of very few circumstances in which one would have to remain motionless for longer than a scene and spending singular extra points of Glamour would be unacceptable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think for Darkling, &quot;the target&quot; refers to &quot;Additionally, witnesses suffer her Wyrd as a penalty to all rolls to notice her.&quot; Since the effect is the same, I think Darkling extends the duration to a week. &quot;Target&quot; is a poor choice of words, though, yes.<br /> <br /> The Wizened bonus would make sense if Light-Shy ended upon being successfully spotted, so Wizened can basically just extend the contract for as long as they needed. Otherwise yes, the Wizened bonus feels odd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T22:41:22-08:00","id":832333,"title":"","content":"You know, I used to think changelings of 2e were going to be infinitely varied just with Kith + Seeming, especially with kith saying how you can modify them. Then I found out Dual-Kith was being kept and changelings become varied to an even greater infinity... and then I saw the contract rules and how they now alter your changeling's identity.... the level of customization when it comes to meins is ridiculous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T23:14:43-08:00","id":832344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=832182#post832182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I explained when you brought it up before, each Trigger <i>already has</i> a specific expression and a general expression, the way it's written now. You just don't get varying penalties for the specific or general version.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you point me to the explicit rules on two versions of Trigger? I try to read mechanics carefully and still did not see those to versions in text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T23:25:12-08:00","id":832347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=832344#post832344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could you point me to the explicit rules on two versions of Trigger? I try to read mechanics carefully and still did not see those to versions in text.</div> </div> </div> </div>Last paragraphs of the &quot;Crafting Triggers&quot; and &quot;Triggers in Play&quot; sections.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T23:27:14-08:00","id":832350,"title":"","content":"I love the Reticent condition as it is. Taking a character's willpower but giving her the +3 resistance is pretty interesting. <br /> <br /> I imagine a city controlled by changelings has gone all &quot;Equilibrium&quot; due to all the emotion feeding. The people are emotionless, but can't be as easily manipulated by emotion oriented advertising or propaganda as easily. And the way I am reading it, it could be used against attempts by supernatural creatures as wells like Angels or Vampires. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8619-aforgeforthoughts","name":"AForgeForThoughts","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T23:38:00-08:00","id":832356,"title":"","content":"Finally read through all the bits that weren't previously spoiled, though my allergies + beta language are making actual comprehension hard.<br /> <br /> Hostile Oaths make me sad. I wish it wasn't so completely absolute. I don't care how hard it is: there's got to be a way of breaking that other than zeroing at least one participant's Wyrd. I get that, mechanically, two reconciled changelings could simply <i>not</i> mess with each other, but &quot;undying enmity&quot; still makes me sad. I can't see a way to do it satisfactorily though. I'm going to noodle on that.<br /> <br /> I like the general sense I'm getting from the Dreamwalking stuff, but... there's an implication in the text that a Changeling who infiltrates a Dream Bastion without a pre-established agreement <i>isn't</i> committing an act of violation. They totally are. Parleying with someone's subconscious isn't consensual. I'd like it made more clear that that's an unethical thing to do, even if many Changelings nevertheless have no qualms about doing it. It's certainly <i>more</i> ethical than what Huntsmen and Gentry do, but it's in the <i>middle</i> of the spectrum, not on the saintly end of it.<br /> <br /> I'm also rather sad that Changelings who have a restful sleep disappear from their beds at night. It's a profound gulf in intimacy there, and it is filled with melancholy. Not to mention how creepy it is if you have casual one-night stands with mortals and they wake up in the middle of the night, conclude you've taken off, except all your stuff is still there... which... makes me wonder how many Changelings dare to sleep naked.<br /> <br /> Lastly, trying to puzzle out the cosmology of dreams here. There seems to be an unnamed dreamspace that acts as a conduit of sorts between the mortal world and the Hedge (so a dream is less a &quot;gateway&quot; and more a tunnel?). A mortal dreamer basically opens up the conduit from one end, and the Hedge naturally creates the other endpoint in return. A Changeling who dreams is basically <i>digging</i>, so there's no &quot;other end&quot; and waking up means just walking back up the hole. Bastions, in this sense, actually kinda feel like scars created in response to the &quot;wounds&quot; where a dream is like a needle that pulls some Hedgestuff out. And Hedge Gates are basically bypasses around the dreamspace that blow it so wide open there's no Bastion formed in response. Am I understanding what's going on here correctly? I feel like I am not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T23:40:39-08:00","id":832358,"title":"","content":"About <b>Clarity Triggers</b>...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=832347#post832347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last paragraphs of the &quot;Crafting Triggers&quot; and &quot;Triggers in Play&quot; sections.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, you mean this?<br /> <br /> <i>Triggers should ideally be simultaneously specific and broad. If your character lost his husband in the abduction, that husband could be his second trigger. However, the very concept of marriage might be the trigger\u2019s broader expression. So, while confronting his lost love could trigger a breaking point, so could being invited to a wedding, or passing by bachelorette party on his way to the club. </i><br /> <br /> Maybe it's me not being Native Speaker, but could not be refrain more directly in final text?<br /> <br /> Now it sounds like the Trigger could be ( not is in all variant ) as:<br /> <br /> A. Confronting lost love,<br /> OR<br /> B. Being invited to a wedding<br /> OR<br /> C. Passing by bachelorette party.<br /> <br /> It's just reads like it must be chosen like A, B or C and <i><b>only</b></i> one of it.<br /> <br /> <i>When dealing with the general application of a trigger, the player should receive full authority on when it does or does not apply. However, if a character faces the specific trigger (in our example, if he confronts his former husband), that\u2019s a definite breaking point.</i><br /> <br /> <b>This rule should be hashed out in to &quot;Crafting Triggers&quot; section, it clearly points that Trigger should be both Common and Specific - it only lost in &quot;examples&quot; part of text.</b><br /> <br /> <b>I would also encourage to mark Triggers as something like &quot;Lost Love - Confronting the husband&quot; on the char sheets, to make situation a more clear on both players and ST sides.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-18-2016, 02:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T23:51:51-08:00","id":832364,"title":"","content":"How is the following not direct:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Triggers should ideally be simultaneously specific and broad.</i> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T23:55:14-08:00","id":832365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=832222#post832222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It hasn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that isn't what I asked to be said at <i>all</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T23:57:41-08:00","id":832366,"title":"","content":"Sorry. Here, have a sneak peek at Goblin Vow as an apology!<br /> <br /> [REDACTED]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T23:58:41-08:00","id":832367,"title":"","content":"Having read through all of the new content, I have to say, I love it. I can tell a lot of work has been put into it all and I would just like to say thank you for allowing us to check it out.<br /> <br /> There were a few things I would love to have been explained a bit elaborately, and most of it is in the dream walking section. i felt it was a bit confusing. the dream intensity roll is kind of wrapped up into the roll of remembering the dream, and had to read it a couple of times to notice it was the roll to determine intensity, and would have loved more information on entering dreams and leaving dreams. <br /> <br /> can a changeling that vanishes from the mortal world when they sleep exit through the hedge, or do they always reemerge where they fell asleep? can they vanish when they fall unconscious? will the skein be referenced or mentioned at all?<br /> <br /> and lastly the pledge crafting in 1e was one of the main reasons I loved changeling, and im upset to see it go, but im not going to throw this system out before i get a chance to play around with it in my group.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T00:24:07-08:00","id":832372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=832364#post832364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is the following not direct:<br /> <i>Triggers should ideally be simultaneously specific and broad.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>It's convulent and not direct - its &quot;narrative speaking&quot;, not &quot;rules speaking&quot; mode. I posted lower the arguement that each of proposed variants sounds as discrete Trigger from what you choose <b>one</b>, <i>not</i> that they <i><b>all</b></i> should be trated as parts of the same Trigger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T00:52:26-08:00","id":832383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=832366#post832366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry. Here, have a sneak peek at Goblin Vow as an apology!<br /> <br /> [REDACTED]</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And then everything turned out okay!<br /> <br /> But seriously, the fact that I've got a 194 page PDF full of preview material and I'm still this amped to see more speaks volumes to me about how great this game is going to be.<br /> <br /> You lot are doing great work!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T01:57:21-08:00","id":832394,"title":"","content":"I have a quick question about Huntsmen (and Hobs, Gentry, and other fully fae). How easily can they break a Seeling?<br /> <br /> If a Changeling manages to trick a Huntsmen into agreeing to perform a really ardous task. &quot;Could you fetch my bag from the locker&quot;, &quot;yes&quot;, &quot;oh you thought I meant that locker. No, it's in Davy Jones' locker. Somewhere in the Pacific I think.&quot;; then wins the Contested roll needed to Seal a Huntsman.<br /> <br /> Has the Changeling effectively defeated the Huntsman, and forced it to waste it's time on Earth searching the ocean for the bag? Or can the Huntsman just say it's only one point of Lethal damage. I'm breaking this deal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T06:44:21-08:00","id":832481,"title":"","content":"I think the easiest way to deal with steel vs. Iron is to say that the True Fae have a side deal with Steel that makes it not count as Iron.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T06:47:50-08:00","id":832484,"title":"","content":"Steel is for Nobility, Iron is for commoners. That's why Iron pichforks are so deadly to Gentry! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T06:57:47-08:00","id":832492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=831950#post831950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks. I actually thought you picked the element when you activated the relevant Contracts, which would obviously make the Contract far more versatile and powerful. It should definitely be clarified in the Contracts descriptions.<br /> <br /> It might also be nice to permit the purchase of additional elements for the Contracts in a manner similar to purchasing additional Seeming bonuses.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's a good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T07:08:44-08:00","id":832501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=832372#post832372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's convulent and not direct - its &amp;quot;narrative speaking&amp;quot;, not &amp;quot;rules speaking&amp;quot; mode. I posted lower the arguement that each of proposed variants sounds as discrete Trigger from what you choose <b>one</b>, <i>not</i> that they <i><b>all</b></i> should be trated as parts of the same Trigger.</div> </div> </div> </div>You pick one specific thing (like &quot;confronting the lost husband&quot;) that is your Trigger. Any time that specific thing happens, that's a Breaking Point. Any time something happens that isn't the specific thing, but is still related to the root of the Trigger, the player can decide for themselves if it should be a Breaking Point or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T07:32:26-08:00","id":832511,"title":"","content":"Okay, I've now read some of the chunks and here's a few of my initial impressions.<br /> <br /> 1. The Reticent Condition is interesting. I like it, but at the same time, I've got a few concerns and thoughts on it. First, I think I'd like it better if the Condition was gained whenever a target lost the last of their Willpower to being harvested, with one Willpower lost for each point of Glamour taken, rather than automatically losing all Willpower if they are harvested at all. The loss of all Willpower makes it hard to argue that changelings aren't harming people by feeding from them, which may be the intent, which is fine. It also takes the teeth out of any mortal opponents they may have, though, including hunters, as only a truly emotionless being would be able to hold on to their Willpower long enough to make use of it. If they've got the Merit that allows them to feed on other supernatural beings, would they also be able to cripple their Willpower as easily?<br /> <br /> 2. I'm not quite clear on this. When they drop the Mask, are all Contracts automatically an exceptional success, or is it only that the roll is counted as an exceptional success if the roll is successful, but failure is still possible? I worry a bit about this, as a Fairest with the Changeling Hours Contract has a fairly easy way to permanently remove any threat against herself by freezing them in time permanently.<br /> <br /> 3. Using Mask and Mien as the Virtue and Vice replacements seems like it could get confusing, given that the two terms are also used for other major parts of the character.<br /> <br /> 4. Glamour addiction seems pretty interesting. When it says that they must harvest it by their preferred method, does that mean their preferred method in the moment, or does each character have a certain way that they need to do so? For example, if an Autumn Courtier likes to scare people and feed on their immediate terror, is that the only way that he could stave off deprivation, or would goblin fruits do the trick just as well?<br /> <br /> That's it for now, but I'm sure more will follow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T09:40:51-08:00","id":832560,"title":"","content":"Some thoughts on Contracts:<br /> <br /> The various mechanics for buying different contracts (some are stand-alone, some have a dot range with multiple possible effects, plus a couple different seeming extras) seems unnecessarily complicated. Perhaps the explanation could be simplified by saying: You buy the basic contract for X dots and it does Y. For one additional dot, you can buy or more of the following extra effects: &lt;list of effects, noting that some are free / automatic for a given seeming.)<br /> <br /> For Bite of the Wooden Fang, it seems like a Contract that only applies to weapons should use Weaponry, not Brawl?<br /> <br /> Also, for a 5 dot Contract, the drawback on Red Rage seems far too brutal. I think a better time limiting mechanic might be to change it so the bonuses are equal to your Wyrd and the duration is the number of successes rolled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6556-lostlost","name":"LostLost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T09:47:15-08:00","id":832564,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how Reticient would even work with werewolves. They ain't ever running out of Angry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T09:49:55-08:00","id":832565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=832394#post832394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a quick question about Huntsmen (and Hobs, Gentry, and other fully fae). How easily can they break a Seeling?<br /> <br /> If a Changeling manages to trick a Huntsmen into agreeing to perform a really ardous task. &quot;Could you fetch my bag from the locker&quot;, &quot;yes&quot;, &quot;oh you thought I meant that locker. No, it's in Davy Jones' locker. Somewhere in the Pacific I think.&quot;; then wins the Contested roll needed to Seal a Huntsman.<br /> <br /> Has the Changeling effectively defeated the Huntsman, and forced it to waste it's time on Earth searching the ocean for the bag? Or can the Huntsman just say it's only one point of Lethal damage. I'm breaking this deal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Huntsman could also just... not try to do it and it won't take <i>any</i> consequences, if I'm reading it right. The trick with a Huntsman would be that you'd seal it for promising to do something it <i>has</i> to do anyways, like successfully capturing a changeling, or fulfilling an Approach, and then something else afterwards, like, I dunno, &quot;And then I'll give him a chance to run.&quot; Then the Huntsman would be breaking the seal by failing to do so, or handing the changeling over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T10:11:29-08:00","id":832574,"title":"","content":"Edit: Nevermind I found it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T10:52:49-08:00","id":832592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=832564#post832564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how Reticient would even work with werewolves. They ain't ever running out of Angry.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd likely give any Frenzy-ing Splat a +3 to resist Frenzies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T10:54:31-08:00","id":832594,"title":"","content":"Okay, here are my initial thoughts on the Contracts. For the most part, I like them, and the touch of making each one favor a couple Seemings is a nice one. I look forward to seeing what the favored Contracts will be like for the Grimms and the chance-based ones (which I'm going to call Madcaps as a placeholder until their name is revealed). I do wonder, though, if Loyalists have any favored Contracts or whether they always gain only the basic version without additional cost. On to a few specific Contracts:<br /> <br /> I noticed that the Game Master\u2019s Table Contract lacks an exceptional success effect. Might I suggest that the exceptional success gives the expanded information that the success effect lacked (ie: whether the warrior is killed or captured, or the fact that the bridge needs to be taken by stealth)?<br /> <br /> With Cloak of the Bear\u2019s Massive Form, does a Beast gain an additional two forms every time they purchase a new form, or only when they first purchase the Contract? Is it required that they be close enough to touch the animal they are changing into, or just close enough to touch any of the animals that they have available to them? For example, if they have a squirrel and a bear form, can they use the Catch if they are being attacked by a bear to turn into a squirrel for escape, or would using the Catch only allow them to become a bear to fight back? For that matter, how specific is the animal species required to be in order to make use of the Catch? If a changeling has a polar bear form, would a grizzly bear allow them to invoke the Catch since they are both bears, or would it need to be another polar bear?<br /> <br /> The Red Rage of Terrible Revenge\u2019s 1 lethal damage per turn seems pretty brutal to the character invoking it, given that the ones they\u2019re facing will probably be adding to that damage, making the use of that power a pretty quick way to incapacitate the character. Would making the damage per turn bashing rather than lethal, at least on an exceptional success, render the Contract too useful?<br /> <br /> Tying the Knots of Fate looks pretty good, but the limit of the event needing to occur within the next month seems to be especially limiting for trying to bless or curse an infant. Perhaps you could make it so that the time frame that the event could occur within could take place at a far later time or in response to specific triggers if an exceptional success is rolled, thus making it possible to give the infant a blessing or curse that could take effect later in life. I think the power could also stand to have a couple examples listed in the text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T11:49:24-08:00","id":832630,"title":"","content":"Name: Halaza <br /> <br /> Gender: Male <br /> Seeming: Darkling <br /> Kith: Hunterheart <br /> Court: Ivory<br /> <br /> Merits:<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Ivory Court Mantle, \u2022\u2022\u2022 hollow (\u2022\u2022 size, \u2022 luxery), \u2022\u2022\u2022 Hedge Beast Companion (Tiger: Skinmask \u2022\u2022\u2022, Pathfinder \u2022, Double Jointed \u2022\u2022, Alternate Identity (Rathika), Alternate Identity (Sarah) \u2022\u2022, Eiditic Memory \u2022\u2022, Striking Looks \u2022\u2022 (beautiful \u2022\u2022), \u2022 Goblin Vow (Mithra), \u2022\u2022\u2022 Retainer: Melanie (Heirodule/Priestess).<br /> <br /> Attributes: Str \u2022\u2022\u2022, Dex \u2022\u2022, Sta \u2022\u2022, Int \u2022\u2022, Wits \u2022\u2022, Resolve \u2022\u2022, Manip \u2022\u2022, Pres \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Comp \u2022\u2022. <br /> <br /> Contracts: Control Elements (fire) \u2022\u2022\u2022, Boon of the Scuttling Spider \u2022\u2022.<br /> <br /> Clarity \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022(Archtype Deity, virtue Anwering Prayers, Vice exploiting Faithful)<br /> <br /> Wyrd \u2022<br /> <br /> Skills/Specialties: Athetics \u2022\u2022\u2022 (BDSM), Brawl \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Stealth \u2022\u2022, Larcany \u2022, Occult \u2022\u2022 (Gods), Investigate \u2022\u2022, Expression \u2022, Subltefudge \u2022\u2022, Intimidation \u2022\u2022\u2022, Persausion \u2022 (Worshippers)<br /> <br /> Oaths: Freehold, Court of Ivory, Motley, (Bargain) Melanie, (Personal Oath) Falicidae.<br /> <br /> The Temple of Shadow Vices<br /> <br /> The Temple is a massive Hollow that functions as a Temple dedicated to Halaza, God of Vice.<br /> <br /> Its made up of A massive courtyard, a Banquet Hall, a Fully Stocked Kitchen, A communal worship area, a dungeon, a countless living Quarters.<br /> <br /> Every room is equipted with an Altar of Halaza which when prayed at can grant ones prayers to a limited degree. The Altars can create projections made from prayer and shadows which can't leave the Temple (the projections function like holodeck characters/objects, they're not &quot;real&quot;, and only do what they're &quot;programmed&quot; to do, if attacked or damaged they disappear into shadows hadows).<br /> <br /> The Temple is made of Polished Black Onyx, with gold engraved images. A massive statue of Halaza is the the communal room, with glowing eyes that follow your movements.<br /> <br /> The rooms are lit only by eternal torches.<br /> <br /> The living quarters have comfortible beds and bathrooms.<br /> <br /> The door to the Temple is the back door at the Whiskey A-Go-Go stripclub.<br /> <br /> Halaza is a Darkling Hunterheart who prefers into hunt from darkness and who has a God complex. As a Mitrae of the Ivory Halaza is greedy for worship and power.<br /> <br /> Halaza enjoys awing others with his ability to summon fire and darkness.<br /> <br /> Halaza appears as a more animalistic verision of a Cenobite, bald with sharp animal teeth of polished ivory jutting from his skull, eyes. His greed for power manifests via his mantle as golden mancles, collars, and chains on those who end up in range of his mantle him, but they do not impede anyone in any way.<br /> <br /> When Halaza attacks someone using brawl, those he touches are actually damaged by his shadow, which lashes out in varous forms at the target. This is the manifestation of his Kith Blessing, and it includes his gaze, which causes sadows to caress the onlookers, making giving them the insensate condition (either pleasurable or terrofying depending on wheather it is meant to be punishment or reward).<br /> <br /> When attacking, Halaza prefers to use Boon of the Scuttling Spider and attack from darkness at a weird angle.<br /> <br /> Felicidy is a Tiger Hedge Beast Companion who enjoyed using Skinmask to interact with humanity and serves Halaza. <br /> <br /> She has two alternate Indentities, one Rathika was a former Priestess of Halaza who betrayed him to a Loyalist and was eaten by Felicidy as a result, who assumed her identity. The other was an Australian hunter named Sarah, with a stripper cover, who tied to hunt Felicidy and was eaten instead. Felicidy assumed her identity as well.<br /> <br /> Felicidy acts as a spy and assassin for Halaza.<br /> <br /> Melanie, a green eyes red head is Halaza's current Priestess and Hierodule. An Escort who grew jaded, wishing to experience something new, Melanie was recruited by the Cult of Mithra to serve Halaza.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 02-18-2016, 03:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T17:13:39-08:00","id":832848,"title":"","content":"After having set aside time to carefully read over Glamour, I have to agree with everyone saying Reticent is too harsh and frankly, easily exploitable (especially with Exotic Airs). I'm already houseruling it in my playtest game as draining 1 Willpower per Glamour the changeling obtains, and the condition lasting only until the end of the scene (though it reaches its full duration, as described in the text, if the changeling &quot;sucks the victim dry&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T17:26:21-08:00","id":832860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=832848#post832848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After having set aside time to carefully read over Glamour, I have to agree with everyone saying Reticent is too harsh and frankly, easily exploitable (especially with Exotic Airs). I'm already houseruling it in my playtest game as draining 1 Willpower per Glamour the changeling obtains, and the condition lasting only until the end of the scene (though it reaches its full duration, as described in the text, if the changeling &quot;sucks the victim dry&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>I hate, hate, hate &quot;end of scene&quot; Conditions. It kind of ruins one of the best aspects of Conditions.<br /> <br /> I'll look at Reticent. Although I'd prefer to see how it worked in play for people. I'm not hugely concerned about abuse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T17:39:12-08:00","id":832870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=832860#post832860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll look at Reticent. Although I'd prefer to see how it worked in play for people. I'm not hugely concerned about abuse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do feel that having it be the <i>higher</i> of a week and twice Wyrd days is a bit much for what the Condition does, particularly given it's objectively harsher than Soul-Shocked and demonstrably easier to inflict.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T17:41:22-08:00","id":832874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=832860#post832860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hate, hate, hate &quot;end of scene&quot; Conditions. It kind of ruins one of the best aspects of Conditions.<br /> <br /> I'll look at Reticent. Although I'd prefer to see how it worked in play for people. I'm not hugely concerned about abuse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually tend to default to &quot;end of scene&quot; Conditions whenever they don't give reliable Beats, especially when they're this ridiculously harsh. What's the point otherwise? Having a really punishing condition for days and days that cripples your ability to regain willpower and only gives you one measly Beat at the end, assuming you Resolve it at all? If it gave reliable Beats, like Addicted (especially since Addicted gives you Deprived, for even more Beats), it would be a completely different story.<br /> <br /> I genuinely cannot see how Reticent lasting from one week to <i>20 freaking days</i> is going to improve my stories in any way. What's more, I haven't done the math yet, but with the baseline of 1 week, a Freehold with 100 Changelings that each harvest Glamour from a random person once a day is going to have an ongoing 700 Reticent people in their town/city, if not more. That's very, very noticeable. Throw in some Changelings with Wyrd 4+ and you're looking at dozens and dozens more people with that condition, lasting even longer.<br /> <br /> I am not really going to use it as-is on my playtest, sorry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":10056,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","user":"ShadowKnight1224","date":". 02-18-2016, 08:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T17:45:18-08:00","id":832878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=832860#post832860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hate, hate, hate &quot;end of scene&quot; Conditions. It kind of ruins one of the best aspects of Conditions.<br /> <br /> I'll look at Reticent. Although I'd prefer to see how it worked in play for people. I'm not hugely concerned about abuse.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> David, don't be shy, tell us how you really feel about Conditions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I think a primary problems with Reticent is no so much that it's objectively too powerful or punishing a Condition, but that's it's sufficiently severe and/or long-lasting to be inconsistent with the earlier text's unequivocal claim that such Harvesting doesn't damage the target and is not inherently predatory. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T17:47:25-08:00","id":832880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=832874#post832874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I genuinely cannot see how Reticent lasting from one week to <i>20 freaking days</i> is going to improve my stories in any way.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the effect doesn't last, nobody will bother even attempting to resolve it. It's a problem I've run into with some of the Disciplines in Requiem. If there's an easy way to just ignore it and let it go away, it'll have zero impact in play.<br /> <br /> I might shorten the time when I get some active notes from play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T17:52:31-08:00","id":832885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=832874#post832874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I genuinely cannot see how Reticent lasting from one week to <i>20 freaking days</i> is going to improve my stories in any way. What's more, I haven't done the math yet, but with the baseline of 1 week, a Freehold with 100 Changelings that each harvest Glamour from a random person once a day is going to have an ongoing 700 Reticent people in their town/city, if not more. That's very, very noticeable. Throw in some Changelings with Wyrd 4+ and you're looking at dozens and dozens more people with that condition, lasting even longer.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually a fantastic side-effect, as far as I'm concerned. My group's first response to Reticent was &quot;damn, that's dark&quot; quickly followed by a general &quot;good, the quick and easy way of gaining Glamour has a drawback now&quot;. In the Changeling games I've played, the only times someone didn't get their Glamour from sucking on Emotions was when they ate Goblin Fruit, and that was a complete by-product. That said, obviously everything isn't for everyone, but I absolutely LOVE this Condition. Being a psychic vampire now feels. .like being a psychic vampire. Rather that a guilt-free &quot;the world's population is my battery&quot; approach. <br /> <br /> I could see a concern, perhaps, in a cross-splat game though. On the other hand, I'm rather in lock-step with the Developer's &quot;so what&quot; approach, and also I can imagine some pretty serious repercussions to being found out as &quot;that guy who puts the whammy on randoms and supernaturals, drains them of their will, and makes a frozen trainwreck out of their emotions&quot;. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T17:53:00-08:00","id":832886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=832860#post832860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll look at Reticent. Although I'd prefer to see how it worked in play for people. I'm not hugely concerned about abuse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think part of it is that there's some mood whiplash compared to 1E in terms of harvesting Glamour. 1E harvesting was mechanically harmless and 2E the condition induced is about as bad (if not worse) as losing their soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T17:56:58-08:00","id":832890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=832880#post832880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the effect doesn't last, nobody will bother even attempting to resolve it. It's a problem I've run into with some of the Disciplines in Requiem. If there's an easy way to just ignore it and let it go away, it'll have zero impact in play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to beat a dead horse, but if the Condition is intentionally long-lasting and not particularly easy to resolve (among other reasons), it's hard understand how emotion harvesting can not be considered damaging or predatory. The flavor text is just not consistent with the mechanics.<br /> <br /> However, if Reticent stays as is, any arguments about whether Changelings are truly &quot;monsters&quot; will certainly be far less contentious in light of their primary means of procuring supernatural sustenance.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T17:58:03-08:00","id":832891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=832874#post832874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's more, I haven't done the math yet, but with the baseline of 1 week, a Freehold with 100 Changelings that each harvest Glamour from a random person once a day is going to have an ongoing 700 Reticent people in their town/city, if not more. That's very, very noticeable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should imagine so, because that's an enormous freehold full of very wasteful changelings.<br /> <br /> Supernatural communities in a locale don't tend to break even halfway into the triple digits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T17:59:06-08:00","id":832892,"title":"","content":"As if harvesting emotions shouldn't be damaging or predatory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T18:01:32-08:00","id":832894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=832511#post832511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. I'm not quite clear on this. When they drop the Mask, are all Contracts automatically an exceptional success, or is it only that the roll is counted as an exceptional success if the roll is successful, but failure is still possible? I worry a bit about this, as a Fairest with the Changeling Hours Contract has a fairly easy way to permanently remove any threat against herself by freezing them in time permanently.</div> </div> </div> </div>The intent is that failure is still possible. It's just that if you succeed on the Contract use, it counts as an exceptional success instead of a normal success.<br /> <br /> And yes, dropping the Mask and Embracing the Wyrd are pretty potent if you use them together. I'll see what David thinks after playtest, but we might be able to fold some aspects of them together. Also, it occurs to me that I think a changeling out of Glamour should count as having their Mask dropped until they gain a single point. It makes the scene more tense and makes many changelings loathe to use that last bit of their power, which can be great for drama.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T18:02:56-08:00","id":832896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=832880#post832880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the effect doesn't last, nobody will bother even attempting to resolve it. It's a problem I've run into with some of the Disciplines in Requiem. If there's an easy way to just ignore it and let it go away, it'll have zero impact in play.<br /> <br /> I might shorten the time when I get some active notes from play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but hear me out:<br /> <br /> <i>The Reticent condition isn't sufficiently interesting, narrative-wise, to justify this</i>. If it was something like Addicted or something that would call the character to <i>do</i> something narratively interesting, I'd change my tune. But Reticent is a <i>passive</i> condition, it makes the character <i>less</i> like themselves, it makes them <i>do less</i>. They cannot regain Willpower, indulging in Vice is useless (and I assume they aren't inclined to), and only doing something truly significant Virtue-wise or emotion-wise is enough to resolve the condition. But again, given the description (&quot;but a dull reflection of her normal self&quot;), they probably aren't even inclined to do so.<br /> <br /> Not to mention the <i>target</i> of this Condition. Not changelings, not Fetches, not Huntsmen, not the True Fae, but the mortals that the changeling interacts with. If they're random people, this condition is only narratively relevant when the cases start to pile up in the Changeling's usual haunts... and even then there's nothing he can really do about it other than feel bad and try to change his feeding habits (which, in fact, if we're being realistic, is the sort of thing that more experienced changelings advise newer changelings about, outright negating this possibility in the first place). If they're not random people, and the changeling does feed on a close mortal and they witness what they've done to them, what's the narrative pull here? The changeling letting the condition fade or resolve on its own is anticlimactic. Only when the changeling tries to fix what they did and get the victim to experience a strong emotion to break out of it does it feel narratively relevant. But even then you get a very &quot;mortals are just playthings to the fae&quot; vibe. Which, okay, it's vaguely thematic, but it just feels so niche, considering most changelings will probably experience this whole thing only a handful of times.<br /> <br /> I think &quot;emotionally deadened&quot; is just a bad idea, concept-wise. It doesn't drive the character narratively, it strays a bit too close to Vampire with the whole &quot;look at the terrible things you do to pursue your thirst for <s>blood</s> Glamour!&quot;, it's applied on the wrong character in the first place (because honestly, the main draw of an &quot;emotionally dead&quot; condition is witnessing the PoV of the character experiencing it, since they are outwardly inexpressive), and it's overall just <i>boring</i> in gameplay. I'd much prefer something that tampered with the character's emotions in a way that resulted in an active character, like a mini-incite-bedlam that's completely out of the changeling's control, or the character being unnaturally fascinated with the changeling, leading them to stick their noses where they shouldn't, or something that just shakes things up and gives the ST interesting possibilities for things to happen.<br /> <br /> If you want to keep Reticent, I'd much rather see it on the players themselves, perhaps on a dramatic failure in a Harvest Glamour roll?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":10056,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","user":"ShadowKnight1224","date":". 02-18-2016, 09:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T18:08:04-08:00","id":832898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=832892#post832892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As if harvesting emotions shouldn't be damaging or predatory.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree, but that's the problem.<br /> <br /> It's not the fiction implying that Changelings don't view emotion harvesting as predatory or don't care about its effects, but rather the actual explanatory fluff describing the mechanics stating as a fact that it's not harmful or inherently predatory.<br /> <br /> I personally would be more than satisfied if emotion harvesting was clearly understood to be damaging to its targets like vampire feeding, although that would certainly change the tone and perceptions of changelings and their society and culture, both in and out of character. They would quickly and readily go from abuse survivors to victimizers (sadly closer to realty than many other tropes).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":".  typo 02-18-2016, 11:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T18:08:53-08:00","id":832900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=832892#post832892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As if harvesting emotions shouldn't be damaging or predatory.</div> </div> </div> </div>I might be in the minority here, but I genuinely don't think that passively harvesting the emotions in a location (like a party, a funeral, a bar fight or a sports match) should be harmful to anybody.<br /> <br /> Perhaps it might be useful to have two different types of emotion harvesting: ambient and personal. Personal harvesting should have side effects, but it should have the advantage of giving you a large amount of Glamour in a very short amount of time, making Changelings akin to emotional vampires. Ambient harvesting should be safe, but it should take <i>a lot </i>of time to get you a decent amount of Glamour (and might be better for changelings that conserve their Glamour and are merely staving off addiction or keeping themselves topped off).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T18:11:44-08:00","id":832904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=832898#post832898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I agree, but that's the problem.<br /> <br /> It's not the fiction implying that Changelings don't view emotion harvesting a predatory or don't care about its effects, but rather the actual explanatory fluff describing the mechanics stating as a fact that it's not harmful or inherently predatory.<br /> <br /> I personally would be more than satisfied if emotion harvesting was clearly understood to be damaging to its targets like vampire feeding, although that would certainly change the tone and perceptions of changelings and their society and culture, both in and out of character. They would quickly and readily go from abuse survivors to victimizers (sadly closer to realty than many other tropes).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll make sure the descriptions line up more with the reality of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T18:26:21-08:00","id":832913,"title":"","content":"I'm going to look at Reticent. Although, I do want there to be a drain/cost involved. <br /> <br /> I think part of the confusion here is the line where Willpower is apparent in the game world. Like, it clearly reflects in events that occur in-game. But it's not something that's easy to measure. This isn't someone being suicidal or whatever; they're just... less effective, less motivated, less fulfilled. All abstract stuff that could be chalked up to a lot of things. This isn't health level loss, which is pretty clear and objective.<br /> <br /> This will definitely be clearer, and looked at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T18:31:21-08:00","id":832917,"title":"","content":"Thank you for being willing to look at it again! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T18:33:28-08:00","id":832920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=832917#post832917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for being willing to look at it again! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Of course. That's the whole reason I'm doing this. <br /> <br /> I hope that people understand that in the end, even if I disagree with their notes, I appreciate them and are considering them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T18:36:40-08:00","id":832923,"title":"","content":"Yeah, no worries. Besides, that's what houseruling is for. If I end up disagreeing with the final version of Reticent (or its equivalent), I can easily just say, for example, that it gets replaced by the Obsessed condition instead.<br /> <br /> Either way, I just wanted to appreciate the awesome atmosphere we have, with the two-way feedback and open communication. It hasn't been my experience with other companies. So thanks for that!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T19:17:36-08:00","id":832951,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if Reticent makes the tactic of &quot;Get a beast to use nightmares on someone, and get the changeling to feed on that fear&quot; more ethical than it was with 1e glamour feeding rules or less....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T19:38:11-08:00","id":832959,"title":"","content":"Half of what's weird to me about Reticent and emotional harvesting is the totality of it. That's not the right word, but bear with me. There isn't a still unhealthy but less violent/predatory option like you can try to focus on subtle and consensual-ish feedings as a vampire. Feeding off strong emotion was messy in 1E because emotions didn't just disappear after you stirred them up, and they had effects on people. Now, with negative emotions you've riled it up, it actually becomes a cheat out of consequences. If you fill a mortal with fear, rage, jealousy, sorrow, and then feed off them - the consequence is deleted*.<br /> <br /> So the other half is that really this takes the emotional vampirism of 1E and inverts it; it's dark to feed off positive emotion and potentially cathartic to feed off of negatives. I'm not sold on that switch, but it's not irredeemable by any means.<br /> <br /> EDIT: * I know this is not entirely a fair description. Rhetorical flourish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","user":"Nicias","date":". 02-18-2016, 10:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T19:43:45-08:00","id":832960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=832951#post832951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure if Reticent makes the tactic of &quot;Get a beast to use nightmares on someone, and get the changeling to feed on that fear&quot; more ethical than it was with 1e glamour feeding rules or less....</div> </div> </div> </div>Ethics be complicated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T19:50:46-08:00","id":832967,"title":"","content":"I agree with those concerned about reticent. I just don't feel like it adds anything to the game.<br /> <br /> Perhaps if only happened when you get an exceptional success or a dramatic failure on a harvest, and convert it to hours instead of days. So its a risk, but not a certainty, it makes it more interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T20:06:51-08:00","id":832971,"title":"","content":"My other area of concern is Pledges. I understand hitting them with the nerf stick, but this goes too far.<br /> <br /> In 1e it was this dymamic, if broken system and a major part of the changeling experience.<br /> <br /> Now outside of pledging a court for the free mantle dot, a freehold, and maybe a motley, and a single bargain, it doesn't seem worthwhile to even bother with the mechanic.<br /> <br /> Oaths used to be this exciting if risky thing you could do, a powerful deal, and more flexible.<br /> <br /> I'd personally have prefered something more like the original, but a Changeling was limited to gaining one merit from his pledges, with the exception of the mantle merit for joining a court, and each mortal or none fae splat could only get one merit from dealing with Changelings.<br /> <br /> Or maybe make it so an oath can only have so many points in it.<br /> <br /> Sealings just seem like a way for Changelings to be annoying to mortals.<br /> <br /> Almost everything else I love.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T20:13:44-08:00","id":832974,"title":"","content":"I spoke up against the <i>extent</i> of Reticent, but personally, Harvesting <i>should </i>be damaging or costly to the target somehow. In hindsight, 1e was the strange one for Harvesting incurring no negative effects on the harvested. So I like that it has a more tangible drawback and that Changelings are actually draining someone's emotions. There's much more responsibility and questionable moral quality with it, and the decison to obtain glamour in that way becomes more personal and significant for Changelings.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I totally back the concept of Reticent, but I appreciate that you're looking over the consequences and description of Harvesting, David. Even if that was the entire point of sharing all this material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 02-18-2016, 11:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T20:18:42-08:00","id":832976,"title":"","content":"Yeah I agree that harvesting emotions should have consequences, just nowhere near as bad as they are now. Something like removing a WP per success and then maybe giving the effects of the condition for a day or so if you completely drain their willpower with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T20:19:09-08:00","id":832978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=832974#post832974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I spoke up against the <i>extent</i> of Reticent, but personally, Harvesting <i>should </i>be damaging or costly to the target somehow. In hindsight, 1e was the strange one for Harvesting incurring no negative effects on the harvested. So I like that it has a more tangible drawback and that Changelings are actually draining someone's emotions. There's much more responsibility and questionable moral quality with it, and the decison to obtain glamour in that way becomes more personal and significant for Changelings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe &quot;just&quot; draining Willpower to provide Glamour, with harvesting beyond that/rolling a dramatic failure inflicting Reticent? Losing Willpower is pretty serious, and definitely harmful (if that person later goes out and gets mugged, and didn't have Willpower reserves...), but it isn't quite as severe. Might make a decent house rule, even.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T20:25:50-08:00","id":832983,"title":"","content":"Least I seem too negative, I LOVE the changes to Seemings, Kiths, Oneiromancy, Clarity, Contracts, Courts, Court Mantle, Court Goodwill, Hedge Beast Companions, Fae Touched (except life span), Hollows, Embracing the Wyrd, Dropping the Mask, Huntsmen.<br /> <br /> Making cobble thought a inherient part of oniemancy and making it less broken, and on top of that making it a part of hedgespinning is really cool.<br /> <br /> I also love the Toronto Court (PS I noticed in the Court Goodwill merit, that an example was goodwill Ruby Court \u2022\u2022\u2022, so it sounds like its a living court again, instead of a former court).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T20:28:03-08:00","id":832984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=832976#post832976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I agree that harvesting emotions should have consequences, just nowhere near as bad as they are now. Something like removing a WP per success and then maybe giving the effects of the condition for a day or so if you completely drain their willpower with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This would be a good change. You could even make the condition harsher since it only lasts for a day. Time is not the only lever you have to force characters to deal with conditions. A short-lasting but really annoying (or even crippling) Condition can be just as effective as a longer-lasting but milder one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T20:30:54-08:00","id":832985,"title":"","content":"I'd almost feel like I'd prefer a complete about face in the opposite direction. Like, harvesting induces huge spikes in emotion. Kinda like Bedlam on a singular person scale...a game I played in introduced this as a story arc and it was pretty interesting to play around with...harvesting would inspire huge surges of emotion, be it rage, sadness or whatever and it let to some interesting and unpredictable scenes.<br /> <br /> I mean, I'm trying to gather up a small group to give it a shot and I'll run with it as is, but I'm not sure how it'll go with Reticent as is.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=832971#post832971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My other area of concern is Pledges. I understand hitting them with the nerf stick, but this goes too far.<br /> <br /> In 1e it was this dymamic, if broken system and a major part of the changeling experience.<br /> <br /> Now outside of pledging a court for the free mantle dot, a freehold, and maybe a motley, and a single bargain, it doesn't seem worthwhile to even bother with the mechanic.<br /> <br /> Oaths used to be this exciting if risky thing you could do, a powerful deal, and more flexible.<br /> <br /> I'd personally have prefered something more like the original, but a Changeling was limited to gaining one merit from his pledges, with the exception of the mantle merit for joining a court, and each mortal or none fae splat could only get one merit from dealing with Changelings.<br /> <br /> Or maybe make it so an oath can only have so many points in it.<br /> <br /> Sealings just seem like a way for Changelings to be annoying to mortals.<br /> <br /> Almost everything else I love.</div> </div> </div> </div>The new pledge mechanics feel how I'd almost always see them used in play - you'd do a handwavy pledge with a basic idea and benefit and just run with it for the session. The Pledge accounting would only ever come out when something long-term and semi-permanent like Freehold pledges would come into play. So I like them! A few things aren't clear, but I assume that's mostly just drafting and refining.<br /> <br /> Although, I am not really sure why you'd actually want to make a Duel Pledge under the new system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1462,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","user":"Xenesis","date":". 02-18-2016, 11:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T20:44:51-08:00","id":832990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=832978#post832978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe &quot;just&quot; draining Willpower to provide Glamour, with harvesting beyond that/rolling a dramatic failure inflicting Reticent? Losing Willpower is pretty serious, and definitely harmful (if that person later goes out and gets mugged, and didn't have Willpower reserves...), but it isn't quite as severe. Might make a decent house rule, even.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see that. And I had alternate proposals on the effects of Harvesting swimming in my head, but I fear diminishing the role of Reticent too much. Maybe changing the duration to the lowest of the two possible ones could factor in it? I think there's a thin line to work with in the process of making it significant but not too punishing. I don't know what I'd find ideal at this time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 02-18-2016, 11:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T20:45:18-08:00","id":832991,"title":"","content":"I'm intrigued by the idea of Oaths being 'forever' in some way, marking the Changeling. However, I also don't think that what we've seen of Pledges so far makes the 1e mechanics invalid, they just expand on them. We just haven't seen enough of them yet.<br /> <br /> I'll jump on the bandwagon for the love of 1e Pledges though; writing Pledges, establishing benefits, drawbacks, time limits, etc is a joy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T22:50:34-08:00","id":833053,"title":"","content":"Character Creation, when applying the template: Do Changelings get any bonuses similar to Kindred getting a Favored Attribute dot or Uratha getting an Auspice Skill dot?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T22:54:18-08:00","id":833055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amaterasu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=833053#post833053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Character Creation, when applying the template: Do Changelings get any bonuses similar to Kindred getting a Favored Attribute dot or Uratha getting an Auspice Skill dot?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's mention of an extra specialty, but I'm not sure if that's accidentally grandfathered in from 1E or it's intentional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1462,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","user":"Xenesis","date":". 02-19-2016, 01:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T23:16:35-08:00","id":833066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amaterasu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=833053#post833053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Character Creation, when applying the template: Do Changelings get any bonuses similar to Kindred getting a Favored Attribute dot or Uratha getting an Auspice Skill dot?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they don't currently receiving anything like that, although the changeling template bonuses are pretty powerful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T23:25:43-08:00","id":833070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=833055#post833055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's mention of an extra specialty, but I'm not sure if that's accidentally grandfathered in from 1E or it's intentional.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I believe that's a holdover from 1E, although if D-Rock still wants it in, we can keep it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T23:27:25-08:00","id":833071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=833066#post833066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, they don't currently receiving anything like that, although the changeling template bonuses are pretty powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, we considered a Specialty, and it was up for discussion for a while. But I don't think we're going for it because it adds a little extra complexity to character creation, and I don't think it adds much to the experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T00:33:04-08:00","id":833089,"title":"","content":"Just realized I overlooked something about Riddle-Kith and wanted to check since there's no Duration listed: is the second clause of the Cost meant to imply that you can render the Contract indefinite contingent upon the temporary suppression of a single dot of Clarity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T01:28:40-08:00","id":833112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=833089#post833089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just realized I overlooked something about Riddle-Kith and wanted to check since there's no Duration listed: is the second clause of the Cost meant to imply that you can render the Contract indefinite contingent upon the temporary suppression of a single dot of Clarity?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that was the intention, so at least for now, let's run with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T01:32:51-08:00","id":833115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=833089#post833089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just realized I overlooked something about Riddle-Kith and wanted to check since there's no Duration listed: is the second clause of the Cost meant to imply that you can render the Contract indefinite contingent upon the temporary suppression of a single dot of Clarity?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say it &quot;implies&quot; that so much as it &quot;outright states it in black and white&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T02:12:13-08:00","id":833126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=832971#post832971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My other area of concern is Pledges. I understand hitting them with the nerf stick, but this goes too far.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this, in actual faerie tales a single pledge is a really big deal, and often the entire story is based on one single pledge. For example, Bearskin or Rumplestiltskin. However I like the core of the new system more than 1E, it just needs stronger effects.<br /> <br /> Sealings especially seem almost pointless, the only practical benefit they have is that you can lie about them being stronger than they are; but in that case why even bother spending the Glamour. You can lie without using the Sealing power. My suggestion would be to up the penalties, base the standard penalties on 1E Medial pledge penalties, the stronger penalties on the 1E Greater penalties; and all Fae beings also gaining a weaker version of the Oathbreaker Condition.<br /> <br /> Oaths are fine, but I'd replace all the &quot;once per chapter&quot; with once per Session or in some cases once per scene.<br /> <br /> As for Bargains. The problem here is that Hunstman trying to find the Changeling happens off screen. A Huntsman is likely to turn up at a dramatically appropriate moment (I would argue that they should turn up at dramatically apropriate moments). Storytellers are unlikely to roll the Hunstman's Investigation to decide when they show up, which makes the penalty pointless. Perhaps an alternative would be the ability to slip into the Bargain's role once per Session/Chapter. You grab your shoe making tools, get to work, and for the next hour or so no fae being can disturb you. You're not Bob, you're &quot;the shoemaker&quot; and &quot;the shoemaker&quot; does not have friends or enemies, just shoes. And while you're busy making shoes you're planning or your allies are coming to your aid.<br /> <br /> I would also like to see more types of Bargains than just the anti-Huntsman one. For example a Bargain that gives you a Merit or a new Contracts while you're working on it. Take the fairy tale The Three Spinning Women; they asked the would-be-Queen to call them her aunts in exchange. Why would a faerie want to be a Queen's aunt? Status Merit? New Identity Merit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T02:38:12-08:00","id":833128,"title":"","content":"I think/hope that some of these problems will be alleviated when the release Goblin Vows, or at least that's the impression I got from Arc's reply to my previous comment on Pledges.<br /> <br /> Also, yeah, as far as Reticent goes, draining a Willpower per success and applying Reticent if you over-drain (maybe with a duration of a number of days equal to the amount you over-drained?) is a good idea. It also sort of mirrors nicely with Vampire -- you can slurp and will do a little damage regardless, but if you slurp too much, you start fucking with people pretty hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T04:52:42-08:00","id":833158,"title":"","content":"Till I have sick days and time for Character Creation, I just went to Playtests\u2026<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Merits</b></span><ul><li><b><i>Enchanting Performance</i></b><i> \u2022-\u2022\u2022\u2022, Style </i></li> </ul><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b><i>Prerequisites:</i></b><i> Presence \u2022\u2022\u2022, Expression \u2022\u2022\u2022 </i><br /> <i>(\u2026)</i></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><i>\u2022 </i><b><i>Harpy:</i></b><i> Your character knows how to aim an audience for maximum humiliation. At least, to make a target perceive things that way. He can use Expression as Hard Leverage and adds her Wyrd to the roll to do so. </i><br /> <br /> <i>\u2022\u2022 <b>Siren: </b>When your character has successfully opened a Door using performance (Expression, Craft) he may spend a Glamour to open another Door immediately.</i></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>If this style Merit make possible to open Doors with Crafts on <i>Siren</i>, so it should be possible to use it with <i>Harpy</i> and <i>Muse</i> Manuver. </b>Then in <b>Prerequisites</b> should also be \u201cExpression \u2022\u2022\u2022 or Crafts \u2022\u2022\u2022\u201d. I would rather go with this interpretation as myself think about Crafts using character that this Style would be perfect for. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div><ul><li><b><i>Faerie Favor \u2022\u2022\u2022</i></b> - <b>Does I get it right that Sanctity of Merits applys and once \u201ccashed\u201d for Favor, character can choose other Merit in it\u2019s place?</b></li> </ul><ul><li><b><i>Rigid Mask (\u2022\u2022)</i> - Does it not a bit over the top that intentionally dropping your character\u2019s Mask causes a level of lethal damage?</b> Wanted to take this Merit for my Darkling, but getting this high damage is a bit too much, especially as from time to time I would want him to expose his Mien. <b>Maybe 1 Bashing, or at most Wyrd/2 Bashing for dropping the Mask?</b></li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-19-2016, 07:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T06:07:52-08:00","id":833198,"title":"","content":"1 lethal isn't all that much, especially if you're packing a goblin fruit or two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T09:12:21-08:00","id":833328,"title":"","content":"Just had a thought, but if you use cobble thought to draw out a &quot;living&quot; creature, say the pony in the example, which ends up a lifeless husk, could you use hedgespinning to turn that pony into a hedgespun robot?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 02-19-2016, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T09:59:41-08:00","id":833359,"title":"","content":"My car only has six horse power, but one of them can break the sound barrier.<br /> <br /> *drives off in his car, his engine screeching the tune of My Little Pony*<br /> <br /> Maaaybe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T10:33:34-08:00","id":833373,"title":"","content":"But first you'd need to learn to trust again, otherwise you couldn't gather enough magic of friendship to make your automation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T13:13:19-08:00","id":833469,"title":"","content":"Crossposting from elsewhere:<br /> <br /> A comment on harvesting:<br /> <br /> Instead of making it innately predatory to get the involvement you want, why not make the depth of feeling mean more than an equipment bonus?<br /> <br /> One of the big falling-down points of 1e is that there isn't that much point to embrace fae behaviour. You can feed off fear by telling a spooky campfire story as easily as you can actually being the stuff of spooky campfire stories; the only difference is a few bonus dice.<br /> <br /> Why not take a hint from Beast? Why not make it so that Changelings can feed from Glamour from a source of a given strength, but only up to a point. A few come-hither looks from across the bar net you a few Glamour, but it doesn't matter how much or how often you do it; you won't get any deep emotion and, thus, deep power from such an act. It's a quick charge-up, and nothing more. Meanwhile, if you drive an artist mad with obsessive desire for you, acting as his unearthly muse, you can regain far more Glamour from supping at his mad fervor while he makes you immortal on canvas.<br /> <br /> This encourages fae behaviours and makes groups like the Scarecrow Ministry suddenly make sense, but, just as valuable, it also adds incentives to Hedge-diving and making pledges. Deals with mortals and goblin fruit could provide Glamour beyond what &quot;cheap feeding&quot; offers, and thus let Changelings who aren't willing to dedicate themselves to their fae side find an alternative that also provides adventure hooks.<br /> <br /> If you really want, you can even require that the most powerful emotions have to center on the Changeling for best feeding.<br /> <br /> This way, Hunters might still track down Changelings for the lives they ruin (the Autumn Court alone must have to beat them off with both hands), but doing so is manifestly the Lost's choice and not a natural function of their feeding, all while also not getting rid of the world-building element of feeding. It also makes that +1 success a Court gives you even more valuable.<br /> <br /> (And, yes, I realize, this is similar to Satiety, but a good idea's a good idea)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T13:19:00-08:00","id":833474,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna throw in a vote to stay as far away from Beast as possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T13:24:18-08:00","id":833479,"title":"","content":"Hey, a good idea's a good idea, regardless of who has it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T13:26:08-08:00","id":833481,"title":"","content":"Not that I agree on the Satiety levels idea, but why stay away from Beast? They have a lot of interesting parallels. Beast can't answer Changeling problems anymore than Demon can, but it can certainly inform them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T13:29:25-08:00","id":833485,"title":"","content":"I'm regretting bringing up Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T13:32:40-08:00","id":833487,"title":"","content":"The main point is trying to keep gamelines as distinct as possible, in both theme and mood (not just aesthetics).<br /> <br /> Other than that, it's personal preference. Beast touches on themes that I would rather not see in Changeling. The idea of the victim turning predator or abused turned abuser should IMO be optional, like Becoming The Nightmare, instead of incorporated in the text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T13:44:37-08:00","id":833494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=833487#post833487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main point is trying to keep gamelines as distinct as possible, in both theme and mood (not just aesthetics).<br /> <br /> Other than that, it's personal preference. Beast touches on themes that I would rather not see in Changeling. The idea of the victim turning predator or abused turned abuser should IMO be optional, like Becoming The Nightmare, instead of incorporated in the text.</div> </div> </div> </div>.... what he said actually didn't do &quot;victim turning predator or abused turned abuser&quot; at all... So I'm confused.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T13:48:39-08:00","id":833497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=833494#post833494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.... what he said actually didn't do &amp;quot;victim turning predator or abused turned abuser&amp;quot; at all... So I'm confused.</div> </div> </div> </div>He referenced Beast's Hunger mechanic, which evoke Primordial fears and are generally not pleasant for the victim. That, in the context for changeling harvesting having negative consequences for mortals and the predatory theme of Beasts, I don't feel comfortable with the blend of both themes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T13:49:23-08:00","id":833499,"title":"","content":"Well, setting aside that &quot;becoming your abuser&quot; was outright written into the text of first edition (the example of the man-eating troll, anyone?) and that your experiences with the fae have made you like them, a part of the point is that it isn't necessary. It's entirely optional.<br /> <br /> The benefits of adding this feature are obvious:<br /> <br /> -Changelings could and would still feed generally on emotions, meaning it maintains the world-building element without having you leave a trail of drained victims behind you.<br /> -Joining a Court becomes even more important, since it effectively raises the max you can get from a given feeding tier, and thus further encourages player behaviour.<br /> -Deeper feeding encourages more fae behaviours. These aren't necessary, but they <i>are</i> rewarded, allowing groups like the Scarecrow Ministry to not seem like pointless assholes.<br /> -Feeding more deeply doesn't inherently create victims either, but it often can. Feeding deeply becomes about emotional extremes, and those extremes aren't innately good; a theme that 1e tried to get across as well. Deep desire can bring you deepest joy, just as it can drive you into maddening obsession, and painful sorrow can be exceptionally cathartic.<br /> -It gives characters more incentive to form deals with mortals. The income of glamour gained by performing tasks for mortals was pitiful. Now, that small trickle would have meaning.<br /> -It gives characters more incentive to Hedge-dive. Again, being able to restore Glamour without being tied to the limitations of feeding depth is important.<br /> -It gives characters more incentive to feed from dreams, since they are able to provide stronger emotions for fewer consequences.<br /> -It gives more meaning to the Glamour tithe paid to Court leaders.<br /> -Deep feeding encourages fae behaviours that just... Aren't encouraged otherwise.<br /> <br /> If you feel that this reasoning is incorrect, or that you just plain don't like adding feeding tiers because you feel it doesn't help the game, thumbs up. I'd prefer it if you didn't reflexively say no to something just because it might be mechanically similar, though; any more than one might get rid of Death Rage and the Beast from Werewolf or Vampire just because one is too similar to the other. Mechanical similarity isn't the same as thematic similarity, and it isn't the same in terms of impact on gameplay or player experience.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=833497#post833497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He referenced Beast's Hunger mechanic, which evoke Primordial fears and are generally not pleasant for the victim. That, in the context for changeling harvesting having negative consequences for mortals and the predatory theme of Beasts, I don't feel comfortable with the blend of both themes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I referenced it because it contains a useful feature: Tiering of reward. I then used, as references of how it might work in play, come-hither stares as opposed to the rapturous adoration of a muse. The point isn't to make Changeling behaviour innately predatory, it's actually to do the opposite: To make any predation involved a definite choice on the Changeling's part. Predation, after all, is already entirely possible and exists in a bunch of the 1e material already. The example feeding method of Summer Courtiers is picking a fight with random schmucks, and the Winter Court of Miami sits at the centre of the drug trade because it thrives on the misery of the addicted and vulnerable.<br /> <br /> More than that, though, it also serves as a bunch of other features, and, on top of it, reminds players that emotions are <i>powerful</i>. The rawest, most powerful sources of magic aren't the quickie one-night-stands but the truest love that echoes down the ages; not the momentary sorrow of a dropped ice-cream but a child crying for the parent who won't come home. There needs to be some representation of that fact; that there's a quantitative and qualitative difference between the Changeling who gets high giving out candy and one that ruins lives. The sort of creature that would produce those most powerful emotions is a monster, and, quite honestly, I'd like it if there was a reason for monstrous Changelings to exist beyond &quot;They're jerks&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2855,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","user":"Axelgear","date":". 02-19-2016, 05:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T13:54:33-08:00","id":833502,"title":"","content":"My problem was less with the mechanics and more with the theme and mood change it might evoke. Putting too much attention on the Glamour harvesting shifts things a bit too close to Vampire/Beast feeding.<br /> <br /> But that's just me. I liked that Changelings were harmless to mortals when harvesting. It made them substantially, thematically and ontologically different from the predators of the CofD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T13:55:22-08:00","id":833503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=833497#post833497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He referenced Beast's Hunger mechanic, which evoke Primordial fears and are generally not pleasant for the victim. That, in the context for changeling harvesting having negative consequences for mortals and the predatory theme of Beasts, I don't feel comfortable with the blend of both themes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, and in many ways, such a severe Reticent Condition leaves a victim <i>worse </i>off than if he had just been gnawed on by a Horror. You may have bad dreams for a while if a Tyrant utterly humiliates you to go high-Satiety, but with this? Being fed on by a changeling looks a lot like the changeling sending you through a depressive episode. That's kinda harsh, even from a purely rules perspective (it's a <i>very </i>potent debuff against anyone not on a <i>subset </i>of social interactions, and you just need to piss someone off enough to give off Anger Glamour to inflict it).<br /> <br /> I do like the idea of Reticent as a whole, it's just that it should be, yanno, the end of Willpower drain rather than the beginning, or much easier to cure and shorter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 02-19-2016, 05:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T14:01:53-08:00","id":833505,"title":"","content":"Maybe the Reticent Condition could become inflicted if a Changeling takes more points of Glamour than a target's current Willpower? With the option of each Glamour taken=Willpower lost. I like the Condition, but I don't like that it's immediately applied to a target; I feel like it should be the effect of over-harvesting, rather than something that always happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T14:09:24-08:00","id":833511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=833502#post833502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My problem was less with the mechanics and more with the theme and mood change it might evoke. Putting too much attention on the Glamour harvesting shifts things a bit too close to Vampire/Beast feeding.<br /> <br /> But that's just me. I liked that Changelings were harmless to mortals when harvesting. It made them substantially, thematically and ontologically different from the predators of the CofD.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair. I honestly was happy to leave Changeling feeding as it was in 1e. I asked Hill about it on 4chan, though, and he said he wanted to make it more complicated. I'd rather see complications arise as a result of Changeling <i>choice</i>, rather than their innate nature. Reticent, as it stands, makes Changelings more psychically vampiric than actual psychic vampires; it's horrifying. Even just stealing Willpower implies that Changelings are in some way parasitic, and I don't really like that.<br /> <br /> Having Changelings be innately harmless gets my thumbs up, but they should probably have reasons to be harmful if they so choose. That way, you get built-in story ideas. Plus, adding tiered feeding helps make them more into the beings of myth and legend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T14:35:02-08:00","id":833530,"title":"","content":"My problem with the idea that changelings are harmless to mortals is that it ignores how much emotions can fuck someone up. It's not as blatant as, say, drinking blood, but it can be problematic.<br /> <br /> You ever have the one friend who will do anything to scare you, regardless of the fact you don't want to be scared? His argument is probably that in the end, so long as it doesn't physically hurt you, nothing bad is actually happening, but in reality the person being scared is now being trained to anticipate stress all the time where it's not due- it sets them in an anxious position. It can be really fucked up how this can work as a long term effect. Even if it's just one really big scare, this can mess with a person.<br /> <br /> Or what about desire? I remember in middle school, there were these two girls who got off on making people flustered and embarrased by acting sensuously around people and teasing them but never giving them. No one is actually hurt, but I remember some people, particularly the deeply religious kids they loved go after particularly, starting having self loathing problems and little break downs because they were lost in how to feel and what to do about it, or if even anything was wrong.<br /> <br /> And these are just two minor examples of how pulling someone along emotionally can be problematic. I have some examples of people doing this, both deliberately and not, that have much more horrifying results.<br /> <br /> Changelings play with people's emotions, and that's not a light affair, particularly coming from supernatural creatures. If anything, Reticent is softer than anything I would have done in regards to feeding on emotions, because it at least creates a rest period after a high, rather than leaving victims in an unstable, uncertain place of increased vulnerability. It always <i>bothered</i> me that we treated eating emotions as though it was no big deal, that there were no consequences, because other people forcing you into an emotional state just isn't a thing. It's part of the reason I like the drug metaphor going on with Glamour, extended by the Overdose optional rules in the Storytelling Chapter, because at least that encourages players to chase the idea into an unhealthy place, both for themselves and the victims.<br /> <br /> But yeah, no, I <i>don't</i> want changelings to be harmless. I want consequences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T14:47:31-08:00","id":833536,"title":"","content":"The problem with Reticent is that it doesn't do what you're asking, Arcane. The consequences of fanning people's emotions should be the natural consequences of fanning people's emotions. You don't need a supernatural consequence to make that hurt more. If anything, Reticent's emotional draining <i>hurts</i> that angle: Instead of exemplifying emotion's power to take you on a rollercoaster of psychic torment, it leaves you internally dead. It negates, instead of exemplifying.<br /> <br /> The solution should be to give Changelings <i>more</i> reason to play with people's emotions, and then let them deal with the natural fall-out. not to have feeding itself be harmful. The muse who drives her artist lover to mad excess should see what it does to him; see how he forgets personal hygeine and sleep in favour of sitting at his easel for days on end; how he stops leaving his studio except to see her; how he stands outside her house at night, crying for her to come to him because he cannot think of anything but her. When he finally hangs himself because she can't deal with this and spurns him, she should feel the horror of the act as if she tied the rope herself.<br /> <br /> <i>That</i> should be the consequence for playing with people's emotions and treating human beings like they're batteries; the natural consequences of strong emotions. Emotions with all the force of a hurricane, and all the devastation of a forest fire. The high drama and low melancholy of a Byron play.<br /> <br /> At present, though, Changelings have no need or reason to produce that sort of feeling. A Changeling can just hang out in a club all night and feed to their heart's content, and never devastate any lives in their passing. Reticent not only doesn't change that to what you're after, it actively makes it <i>worse</i> by taking away the very capacity to toy with emotions that so often fills these stories and that you, yourself, are trying to create.<br /> <br /> Reticent may be softer than what you'd have done, but I hope that what you'd have done would actually encourage strong and powerful emotions to drive the drama, rather than deaden them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T14:53:20-08:00","id":833538,"title":"","content":"I'm not arguing that, but I'm also not the guy behind it, and I get the logic and narrative ideas of Reticent.<br /> <br /> I'm not making a case for or against Reticent right now. I'm arguing against the idea that emotional feeding shouldn't have a consequence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T14:58:26-08:00","id":833541,"title":"","content":"That's fair. If we're in agreement on that, could I get your opinion on my suggestion? See any holes in it? And, if it's not untoward given your work on the book, I'm curious what your take would be, though I understand if professionalism precludes it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T15:05:18-08:00","id":833546,"title":"","content":"Yeah, manipulating people's emotions for sustenance has always had unfortunate implications, but I'd rather the consequences were more nuanced. Right now it doesn't seem to much matter how much glamour you gain or what you did to get it. Reticent happens from even the smallest feeding, which discourages attempts at low impact feeding since the impact is gonna be the same no matter what. Vampires have a really direct metric of how much harm they do, measured in lethal damage, and it's directly proportional to how much they choose to take. <br /> <br /> In first edition there were no mechanical penalties attached to the feeding itself, and I liked that because it encouraged me to think carefully about whether I wanted to induce strong negative emotions or spend the extra time and energy finding a naturally occurring source. As a Summer Courtier it was often tempting to take the easy road and start a fight to harvest anger, but I never did that because it meant somebody else had a bad day and that might create ripples and escalate conflicts. I was always keenly aware that being nice to people endangered my glamour supply, and that raising the general quality of life around me made my life harder in some ways.<br /> <br /> With these rules, if harvesting glamour is going to turn somebody into a shell of themselves for a week at minimum, it seems better to push for really powerful experiences, maximizing my glamour intake (and delaying time to next harvest) since they're not going to feel it either way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T15:16:33-08:00","id":833553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=833538#post833538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not arguing that, but I'm also not the guy behind it, and I get the logic and narrative ideas of Reticent.<br /> <br /> I'm not making a case for or against Reticent right now. I'm arguing against the idea that emotional feeding shouldn't have a consequence.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So long as the fluff actually recognizes the consequences of emotion harvesting, I personally like a significant negative impact on the targets of such feeding.<br /> <br /> I believe it would strongly emphasize an abused now becoming the abuser theme, and certainly demonstrate how changelings are indeed truly &quot;monsters&quot; in the CofD.<br /> <br /> However, turning changelings so obviously and unequivocally into &quot;emotional vampires&quot; might step on the proverbial toes of other gamelines like Vampire a little too much, and I don't get the impression that David intended to strongly emphasize such themes in the new edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T15:25:18-08:00","id":833555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=833553#post833553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So long as the fluff actually recognizes the consequences of emotion harvesting, I personally like a significant negative impact on the targets of such feeding.<br /> <br /> I believe it would strongly emphasize an abused now becoming the abuser theme, and certainly demonstrate how changelings are indeed truly &quot;monsters&quot; in the CofD.<br /> <br /> However, turning changelings so obviously and unequivocally into &quot;emotional vampires&quot; might step on the proverbial toes of other gamelines like Vampire a little too much, and I don't get the impression that David intended to strongly emphasize such themes in the new edition.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Branford has the right idea. Repeatedly inflaming someone's emotions should have obvious long-term negative effects. A little nibble here and there isn't harmful, maybe even sometimes helpful if those emotions were something the subject needed, but feeling anger, sorrow, desire, or fear all the time, just from the Seasonal Courts alone? That isn't healthy.<br /> <br /> I get the sense that maybe Axelgear's idea should be an option. It's not the core method of Glamour feeding, but it should be a tempting option when you need to actively milk someone for the stuff. Maybe a changeling can &quot;play Lenean Sidhe&quot;, not dulling emotions by taking them but choosing to inflame them to unhealthy levels instead. That provides a Glamor spigot far more rich and reliable than goblin fruits or dreams...at the cost of driving someone to increasing insanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T15:26:14-08:00","id":833556,"title":"","content":"It does work quite well as the consequence of a True Fae feeding though. Maybe you could make it optional. You can either sip surface emotions for a quick, safe fix, or you can nearly rip out people's souls for a hefty bonus.<br /> <br /> True Fae, being utterly sociopathic, generally go for the later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T15:32:12-08:00","id":833558,"title":"","content":"I still throw my hat on the idea that emotional vampires is not the most fitting consequence. I'll still vote for an excess of emotion (or an unintended emotion or circumstance) over emotional deadening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T15:48:03-08:00","id":833562,"title":"","content":"Personally, I prefer the flavour of glamour feeding as it's presented in the 2e changeling template &quot;This is not necessarily a predatory act (although changelings can prey on their victims to elicit Glamour of the appropriate \u201cflavor\u201d), in that it does not require actually harming the subject. Instead, it's as if the subject creates a vapor cloud of emotional energy in which the changeling immerses herself, breathing it in, tasting it, allowing it to fill her lungs and her mind and her heart.&quot;<br /> over the predatory condition that conflicts with that flavour. Especially since I've never really seen changelings as predators before + now with glamour addiction all changelings Need to feed on glamour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 02-19-2016, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T16:26:09-08:00","id":833573,"title":"","content":"Maybe I haven't read far enough, but. Caging a dream... can you chase someone through that portal? how long is it open for? or is it more like nightcrawler &quot;poof&quot; I'm now in Faerie?<br /> <br /> If this is still an &quot;open for debate thing&quot; my feeling is it should be an open portal that you could be followed, and I don't actually like the using it to get out of grapple. might be more of an interesting thing to give bonus dies to you to break grapple as both you and your grappler pop arrive in faerie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":4046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","user":"xenoterracide","date":". 02-19-2016, 07:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T16:47:33-08:00","id":833586,"title":"","content":"I'll toss out opinions and ideas on emotion eating after I go and look over some stuff.<br /> <br /> Caging a Dream's Portal Mechanics involve some kind of liminal barrier that can be 'traversed'-the commons being doors and archways, but I have a fondness for mirrors and windows. It remains open for a time(I think it's based on Wyrd?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T17:20:57-08:00","id":833602,"title":"","content":"Out of curiosity, what do Dream Bastions look like, anyway?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T17:30:32-08:00","id":833604,"title":"","content":"Rather like anything. I've visualized them as giant flowers, snow statues, and and glass cliffs faces.<br /> <br /> I imagine there's more specific forms, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T17:39:36-08:00","id":833610,"title":"","content":"I just want to say I LOVE the way dream interaction is being used in Changeling 2e!<br /> <br /> I was a bit curious about actually entering dreams though. When a changeling falls asleep he has the option of dissapearing from the world and going physically into his own dream. She can go to the hedge and find someone's dream bastion and insert herself that way (assuming you can find the right person's dream). There was also a contract that takes you instantly through a person's dream and into the hedge.<br /> <br /> Are there other ways to enter someone's dream for changelings? Can you enter a person's dream by touching their sleeping body in the real world as if going through a bastion? I didn't see anything about that, but I may have missed it.<br /> <br /> Once again, awesome work, and I can't wait to hold the actual book in my hands!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1092-tribute-of-a-dark-heart","name":"Tribute of a Dark Heart","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1092_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T18:21:30-08:00","id":833627,"title":"","content":"<b>Should we not move Emotional Harvesting mechanics and philosophy discussion away into <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/833620-harvesting-glamour-in-2ed\">separate topic</a>?</b><br /> <br /> I like to participate in it, but it\u2019s a bit too much with normal <b>Playtestable Chunks </b>overload.<br /> <br /> <br /> So to asses some things now from rest of Playtests Files\u2026 <b>Pledges</b><ul><li><b>Sealing</b> \u2013 <b>As I understand, character can have any number of Sealings, she just need to pay in Glamour, yes? </b>No roof top limitation here on instances?</li> <li><b>Oaths</b> \u2013 <b>Do I get it right that character can have any number of Oaths also? </b>Wording seems implaying that any time I can make Oath \u2013 for motley, freehold, personal or any other long term dedication \u2013 I just can have my Oath on this.</li> <li><b>Oathbreaker Conditon</b> \u2013 <b>The penalty of -1 on Social rolls with changelings is automatic? </b>So that other Lost just see your Mien and understand on Wyrd level \u201cOh, he broke the Oath, I see it on him\u201d? Or it\u2019s more a gossip things \u2013 \u201cYou heard, this new Darkling in town broke an Oath. \u2013 Typical Darkling\u201d?</li> <li><b>Motley Oaths </b>\u2013 <b>We have <i>all </i>listed game effects or only one is chosen with the creation of Motley?</b></li> <li><b>Ensorcelled mortals</b> <b>\u2013 What happen to them? </b>In 1ED it was specific Plegde. Now I do not see this. Fae-Touched and Fetches are Minor Templates and bit more powerfull than mortal seeing changeling for what it is.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T18:24:03-08:00","id":833631,"title":"","content":"Unless I was misunderstanding the Wyrd Advantages section, you can only have as many pledges as your current Wyrd. I don't know whether that applies to sealings or not (because it'd make them functionally difficult to use at Wryd less than 3-4).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T18:33:48-08:00","id":833634,"title":"","content":"FYI, I'm probably going to fuss with harvesting and stuff on Monday. I hate to say not to waste too much time, but the conversation's getting a bit bogged down, and I have some ideas for what I want to do with it already with the feedback given. I definitely can't address every single concern or comment, but I've got some ideas I think people will dig.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T18:38:17-08:00","id":833637,"title":"","content":"Okay, so let me start on the subject of Reticent itse-Actually, no, let me explain something about myself first, because I'm sure a question has cropped up in people's mind, and I want people to understand why somethings works the way I do.<br /> <br /> Namely, why is it I sometimes seem like I have no idea what's going on in the new texts.<br /> <br /> There's a couple of factors into this, but there are too many for me to talk about in a short deviance, so we'll hit the big one. Namely, I remember stuff better when I make the point of reading it in big chunks. If I read something small bit by small bit over time, I tend to forget each bit and it's connection to everything else, and thus it fades away. If it's all one cohesive block in my head, it sits better.<br /> <br /> This is a problem when you're following stuff in an RPG project, because stuff by necessity has to come in small bit by small bit, and there's not always time to just have big sit down reads for this stuff. For relevance, I came in around the time the writers were wondering where their redlines were, which means most of the first drafts were done. I read and understood the first draft version of the game. As redlines and second drafts started making their way in, though, while I've been reading them, it's been piecemeal, so it hasn't been sitting well. The same thing happened with Beast as a playtester, which is why when we got the PDF for that, I made damn sure to read it all the way through again.<br /> <br /> So, in case you were wondering, that's why.<br /> <br /> NOW let's talk about Reticent.<br /> <br /> First thing I want to say about Reticent is that i actually know this feeling very well, and I know the effect. After an emotional high, you basically <i>do</i> become effectively depressed, it sticks with you for a while. I even know some of the biological and psychological ideas and theories behind this, but that's not the point here. And to be honest, I think it's a fine consequence in and of itself. it keeps you from drinking from the same well over and over again(which is one problem I have had in games), and it also creates good consequences that's true to life without being horrific-even casually making someone feel good about themselves might ruin their week because they just aren't feeling it in bed with their spouse or some such.<br /> <br /> Now, enough people have brought up the ALL WILLPOWER GONE thing, and upon reflection, yeah, sure, that makes sense. Still, I would like someone having been nommed on to have some of the effects of listlessness and depression after it comes on, like a penalty to all actions based on how much of chimp you took. But Dave has already said he's gonna look at it, so there's that. For me, it's a good baseline. Do I think there's room in supplements for exploration on consequences? Hells yes, but that's for when I get me a big ol' book of sorcery to play with. Rites of Spring 2, I want it.<br /> <br /> As for the Scaling Meal sort of thing....Eh? I dunno.<br /> <br /> The thing of it as it applies to Satiety is to help encourage a certain level of predacity, or rather a different kind of predacity from lower levels. Well, okay, no, it's not just that, it's the mythic scale of Beast at work, the need for an epic figure to go onto bigger and bigger challenges. Changeling doesn't quite have that sense of need of escalation-folklore, as fairy tales often are, don't quite scale up the same way a myth does. I mean, it does, but consider that while stories like the Gallant Tailor, that inestimable bastard, might have his stakes increase, but his capabilities don't range up in similar fashion, at least not in the same image as the sort of stories Beast draws from.<br /> <br /> I get the desire to incentivize fae behavior from one angle, and on that I would honestly just add added success the more and more your harvest relates to your own personal myth(or put more simply ,that harvesting should idrectly relate to you and how permanent their emotional memory of you is like), or something like that, but the catch to that is I wouldn't want to <i>mandate</i> fae behavior for your magical gummi drop ammo, because Changeling has this weird tug of war going on with it's relationship to the fae that largely ends with someone deciding on their comfort level with the fae. Wyrd rising does enough of that as is. As is, creating the incentive should have rewards, but there should be rewards for leaving it the fuck alone too(Because Changeling can be a game about putting that thing back right where it came from or so help me, so help me, so help me, and cut, it's a musicial).<br /> <br /> So, finally, i just want to reiterate that there's this pervasive sense of changelings not being all that bad as a monster as the sets go, and I get that and the appeal of it, but it's always been something that bothered me. There's plenty of horror without, but sometimes I feel like we try to sugarcoat the effects of trauma with Changeling by only paying half as much attention to the horror within. In a lot of ways, Changeling has been too clear cut and squeaky clean for being the game that it's about, and that's something that needs to change. Hell, it's in the name. As changelings move away from their trauma, they should have legitimate reason to worry about what they are changing into. I think creating a consequence for harvesting emotions is not a bad way to go as one of several starts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-20-2016, 01:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T18:52:34-08:00","id":833643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=833637#post833637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, finally, i just want to reiterate that there's this pervasive sense of changelings not being all that bad as a monster as the sets go, and I get that and the appeal of it, but it's always been something that bothered me. There's plenty of horror without, but sometimes I feel like we try to sugarcoat the effects of trauma with Changeling by only paying half as much attention to the horror within. In a lot of ways, Changeling has been too clear cut and squeaky clean for being the game that it's about, and that's something that needs to change. Hell, it's in the name. As changelings move away from their trauma, they should have legitimate reason to worry about what they are changing into. I think creating a consequence for harvesting emotions is not a bad way to go as one of several starts.</div> </div> </div> </div>For what it's worth, I feel the exact opposite. I feel that Changeling was a ridiculously darker game when compared to its predecessor, The Dreaming, and while I really dug into the fluff, the mechanics and the way it was executed, I keep seeing that people think <i>it's not enough</i>. Like it just <i>has</i> to get darker and darker, often at the expense of subtlety and nuance. There already was a mechanic for changelings to become the abusers and victimisers. There were already Courts and Entitlements dedicated to doing shitty things to mortals. It was already assumed that most changelings killed their Fetches (repeatedly stated in several books), despite most Fetches having no clue what they did to deserve it (including the very opening fiction of the CtL corebook). There were already ways for changelings to fuck mortals over with pledges, fae trickery, using them as human shields against the True Fae (like Shivers, that girl from... Mortal Remains? The one that uses a Hunter to get her Keeper off her back). Even Loyalists and Privateers showed the ugly side of a victim willing to do anything to survive.<br /> <br /> The darkness, the dickery and the monstrosity were already there, subtle and nuanced as they might've been.<br /> <br /> It's entirely possible that what you're experiencing is a pushback against the &quot;Darker! I say darker!&quot; sentiment that's been cropping up for a long while now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T19:22:16-08:00","id":833659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tribute of a Dark Heart</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=833610#post833610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just want to say I LOVE the way dream interaction is being used in Changeling 2e!<br /> <br /> I was a bit curious about actually entering dreams though. When a changeling falls asleep he has the option of dissapearing from the world and going physically into his own dream. She can go to the hedge and find someone's dream bastion and insert herself that way (assuming you can find the right person's dream). There was also a contract that takes you instantly through a person's dream and into the hedge.<br /> <br /> Are there other ways to enter someone's dream for changelings? Can you enter a person's dream by touching their sleeping body in the real world as if going through a bastion? I didn't see anything about that, but I may have missed it.<br /> <br /> Once again, awesome work, and I can't wait to hold the actual book in my hands!</div> </div> </div> </div>I was hoping someone would answer my questions about dreamwalking, too, but no dice so far. =/","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T19:34:13-08:00","id":833662,"title":"","content":"A large part of this has to do with the fact of my experience with the world. Like, I've mentioned the closehand second experience with the consequence of emotional manipulation, and I'll say here and now I'm not comfortable with my own personal experiences with that aspect, but I want to kind of sum up my experience with a little bit of real talk.<br /> <br /> In many ways, I have been Lost. I'm not going to claim I have a landlock on this subject, because I know for a fact many other writers actually have it way worse than I've had, but I can say I've been there. I think the most pertinent one though, is that I <i>have</i> been both the abused <i>and</i> the abuser.<br /> <br /> I'll spare you the details, just, you need to know that I have done a few heinous things in my life. And for me, the biggest horror now was not that I did it, but the fact that I felt justified in my position because of what abuse I had received. Because of shit I had gone through, because woe was me, I had no qualms wrecking other people, physically, emotionally, mentally.<br /> <br /> Lost did a lot of things for me when I finally got it, so much so that I'm not even sure I can properly grasp it, but one of the biggest things it did was consolidate a lot of feelings and experiences for me into a clear understanding of a disdain for justification and unawareness of self. I don't truck well with things like nostalgia, short-sighted self assurance, and other such things. It's ironic that I stumble around with Clarity a little, because the big thing I got was the sense of rightness in always questioning whether you're in the right place or not, and if you're not, how to fix that, or at least turn it to good use, or even beyond that, just owning it. Either don't go beating up people for kicks, or own up to the fact that you beat up people for kicks, don't justify it me, and particularly not to yourself. The one thing I dislike most is when a person loses awareness of what they're doing and who they are. Know Where And Who You Are is a big ass commandment for me, shortly followed by Don't Rely On Your Own Judgment.*<br /> <br /> And this where this conversation comes in. Yes, Changeling is a dark game. But lots of people don't treat it that way. &quot;Bleakest game, my ass&quot; is something I've said so many times I wouldn't be surprised if that ended up the quote they put on my future TvTropes page, so it's not like I'm not guilty of it-but the responses for Lost Second Edition have largely seemed to lean towards this crazy ass notion of Heroic Changelings fight nobly against Evil Arcadian Forces while dealing with tragic elements. We talk about the horrors of the Lost, sure, but it feels so lightly brushed that it's infuriating. I don't need a &quot;EVERYONE IS AN EVIL MONSTER&quot; sort of thing, but I want some teeth to this.<br /> <br /> On a semi-related tangent, I want it on record that while I like the Becoming Nightmare mechanic, I also kind of hate it, particularly in relation to abused-abuser dialogue, because that has become our main way of talking about that part of the game....and I don't think that's actually what it's talking about, but nevermind that, the bigger problem is that by lumping all our thoughts of that dialogue onto that mechanic, we ignore the small, messy ways that changelings run the risk, the ones that <i>actually</i> <i>matter</i>. The broad picture of a changeling becoming a True Fae is nowhere near as terrifying to me as the moment when a changeling decides to make a person fall into lust with someone else to fill their battery without considering the consequence of how that makes them, in some ways, as bad as their Keeper. The fact that we're having this conversation shows how people sort of brush aside the notion.<br /> <br /> I'm all for subtlety. I really, really like subtlety. But if something is so subtle that I feel like it misses the point, as even my own experiences with Changeling First's mechanics have yielded, then I don't object to making it more overt. And following the fan community from it's inception, I have no problem saying that we lose sight of a lot of important shit(Hell, even I did for a while), and in the course of updating this game, it pays to bring it to light.<br /> <br /> Games are art. Art is about communication. If the message isn't strongly getting through, it's time to consider how you sell your message.<br /> <br /> *Overtly Rely, I should say<br /> <br /> PS: Inappropriate to this entire conversation, would you believe me if I told you my second favorite gameline after the Chronicles of Darkness is Golden Sky Stories?<br /> Edit: Semi-related to the inappropriate conversation as well as this, would you also believe me if I told you slice of life was my favorite mode of play?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-20-2016, 01:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T20:05:49-08:00","id":833675,"title":"","content":"As an aside from the tone discussion that's going on above, I think I'll ask what's potentially another aspect : Do people actually enjoy playing through &quot;feeding&quot; scenes at their tables? Like, I know from most of the games I've played in, a lot of the &quot;magic&quot; harvesting gets relegated to downtime, unless there's a dramatic scene and the group is out of juice, it often gets ignored. And the players I have played with basically go out of their way to minimise it in play.<br /> <br /> Like, to put it in perspective - every Vampire game I've ever played you do a feeding check at the start of the game to determine how much blood you have and basically nothing else happens unless you accidentally eat a person. And that's the blood you'd have for the session. And everyone was mostly happy with it because they saw it was far less interesting than the &quot;actual game&quot; so to speak.<br /> <br /> In changeling it was often similar - you'd do a thing and get Glamour. Interesting scenes only tended to happen when they crashed into the plot bus and something unusual happened.<br /> <br /> Heck, I had an ST for a while who simply didn't even bother and basically just gave half-Glamour to full Glamour at the start of every session depending on the local circumstances because they just felt like it was busywork. If something incidental came up during game (like Goblin Fruit or mortals or whatever) you could get more Glamour but you just ran with it.<br /> <br /> I know my experience isn't exhaustive (and I'm sure plenty of people hit the other end), but I've often felt like it was a bit of a distraction or it can create &quot;single player&quot; scenes very easily.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=833643#post833643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For what it's worth, I feel the exact opposite. I feel that Changeling was a ridiculously darker game when compared to its predecessor, The Dreaming, and while I really dug into the fluff, the mechanics and the way it was executed, I keep seeing that people think <i>it's not enough</i>. Like it just <i>has</i> to get darker and darker, often at the expense of subtlety and nuance. There already was a mechanic for changelings to become the abusers and victimisers. There were already Courts and Entitlements dedicated to doing shitty things to mortals. It was already assumed that most changelings killed their Fetches (repeatedly stated in several books), despite most Fetches having no clue what they did to deserve it (including the very opening fiction of the CtL corebook). There were already ways for changelings to fuck mortals over with pledges, fae trickery, using them as human shields against the True Fae (like Shivers, that girl from... Mortal Remains? The one that uses a Hunter to get her Keeper off her back). Even Loyalists and Privateers showed the ugly side of a victim willing to do anything to survive.<br /> <br /> The darkness, the dickery and the monstrosity were already there, subtle and nuanced as they might've been.<br /> <br /> It's entirely possible that what you're experiencing is a pushback against the &quot;Darker! I say darker!&quot; sentiment that's been cropping up for a long while now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well put.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T20:14:56-08:00","id":833680,"title":"","content":"It's hard for me to talk about this due to personal reasons, but part of the reason I was really against the idea of changelings as predators or having really obvious dangerous and monstrous facets, was because I find the idea a bit dehumanising towards victims. In my Changeling stories, I don't want to constantly deal with the way in which the changelings are similar to their Keepers. I don't want my themes of hope and growth and healing to be repeatedly derailed or made null by that sort of reminder. I feel that should be an optional issue to explore. For me, Changeling is about hope prevailing through despair and the guiding light in the darkness, same reason I love Geist and Promethean.<br /> <br /> The fact that I feel like I have to apologise for liking things that way IMO speaks volumes of the way I perceive the general community to be inclined towards.<br /> <br /> I want to see changelings overcome their flaws, conquer their fears, stand up to their Keepers, face the darkness and emerge scarred but victorious. I don't want those victories to be made hollow or Pyrrhic.<br /> <br /> Consequences are fine. But IMO the game should approach that aspect from a different angle. Instead of making it inescapable, intrinsic to the changeling condition, it should be a temptation. When you are a victim that lashes out or abuses others, you do it for a reason. It's a way for you, the disempowered, to empower yourself. It's a way for you to stop feeling helpless and scared. If I were to be charged with implementing that aspect into CtL 2e, I'd do it in the form of optional actions that give out rewards. Maybe have a mechanic where you can invoke some aspect of the Wyrd when performing an action (maybe it's doing an &quot;extra-strong harvesting&quot;, maybe it's invoking the power of Tales to set up a Wyrd-driven form of narrative mind-control to get them to act the way you want them to) against someone you feel strongly towards. Someone you truly hate, or are terrified of. Maybe someone you're madly in love with but doesn't want you. That way, the changeling is tempted to empower herself by doing something awful to another (not just mortals, but other changelings as well). It's not <i>mandatory</i>, but it's <i>tempting</i>. It's <i>empowering</i>. It gets you what you want... at a price. It sets you up perfectly for a moment of realisation about your own capability for victimisation.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=833675#post833675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do people actually enjoy playing through &quot;feeding&quot; scenes at their tables?</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually tend to gloss over it (abstracting it to an offscreen roll) as both a player and an ST unless the ST/player specifically wants to roleplay it.<br /> <br /> Also, thanks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":10056,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","user":"ShadowKnight1224","date":". 02-19-2016, 11:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T21:06:53-08:00","id":833696,"title":"","content":"Let's get in to Dreams and their mysteries...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Dreamwalking</b></span><ul><li><b>Hedge</b> \u2013 <b>So now the \u201cdream layer\u201d is just in the Hedge itself?</b> That all dreams and dreamers are \u201cphysically\u201d ( well, probably ephemerally more accurate ) in the Hedge?</li> <li><b>Dream Bastions </b>\u2013 <b>They are places/\u201dbubbles\u201d in the Hedge?</b> Like clearing, den, great flower buds with dreamers inside?</li> <li><b>The Gates of Horn and Ivory </b>\u2013 Do I get it correct \u2013 <b>Mortals, when they come asslep, are physically on Earth but their \u201cdreamselves\u201d are in Hedge\u2019s Dream Bastions, connected to one another, yes? </b>Changelings, on the other hand, can only by in one place at time \u2013 they can physically sleep in their beds OR be in the dreams of Hedge, leaving their bed empty in the night?</li> <li><b>Oneiromachy </b>\u2013 <b>Does it mean that I can kill mortal in his dream by sending him full box of Aggravated dream attacks, leading him to have full Lethal on \u201cwaking up\u201d?!</b></li> <li><b>Magic in Dream \u2013 If there could be ghosts in dreams, why not Shadows spirits?</b> I would rather go here with <b>Astral Realms </b>route and point that \u201cother realms\u201d exists only if dreamer is connected to them. If dreamer is Thyrsus mage or werewolf, Shadow could exists very much. But most mortals would not have those \u2013 they can have one or two ephemera in dreams if they are under it\u2019s Manifestation ( like being ghosts Anchors or Urged by spirit ). If dreamer is changeling, his Contracts dictates what is and what is not in the dream \u2013 Contract with Dead will probably mean that ghosts are very much possible in this dreams realities.</li> <li><b>Convince the Dreamer \u2013 Should not the Dicepool be more <i>Wits + Persuassion + Wyrd \u2013 Intensity</i>? </b>Socialize as Skill looks weird in here. Persuasion has more logic as you try too nudge dreamer to your point of view, is it not?</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T21:47:45-08:00","id":833712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=833503#post833503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, and in many ways, such a severe Reticent Condition leaves a victim <i>worse </i>off than if he had just been gnawed on by a Horror. You may have bad dreams for a while if a Tyrant utterly humiliates you to go high-Satiety, but with this? Being fed on by a changeling looks a lot like the changeling sending you through a depressive episode. That's kinda harsh, even from a purely rules perspective (it's a <i>very </i>potent debuff against anyone not on a <i>subset </i>of social interactions, and you just need to piss someone off enough to give off Anger Glamour to inflict it).<br /> <br /> I do like the idea of Reticent as a whole, it's just that it should be, yanno, the end of Willpower drain rather than the beginning, or much easier to cure and shorter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I second that.<br /> <br /> The Reticent Condition is a really nice concept. But I'm with Leliel's suggestion that it should happen <i>after</i> a person harvested of glamour has been drained of Willpower. Not on the spot.<br /> <br /> There was a House Rule I used, though, to handle this, inspired by Ennui from the Dreams of Delirium fan-supplement, and Glamour Rush mechanics from Rites of Spring. I'll probably dig up my old notes and see if I can scrape together a more up-to-date version which uses Conditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T21:57:12-08:00","id":833714,"title":"","content":"Kith interaction with Contracts, specifically Mirrorskins and Riddle-Kith and Skinmask.<br /> <br /> So, is the Mirrorskin blessing supposed to be a quick and free version of the two contracts, or are Mirrorskins expected to have to buy those 2 contracts as well to fulfill the &quot;shapechanger&quot; role?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T22:32:54-08:00","id":833719,"title":"","content":"My thoughts on reticent, in brief: it makes sense that if a changeling feeds on someone's emotions, that person would be left emotionally drained, or outright emotionless. Just like when a vampire feeds on someone's blood, that person is left drained of blood or exsanguinated. Just like when a human feeds on animal or plant matter, that animal or plant is left physically diminished or completely gone. You can't really consume something without leaving an absence of that thing where it used to be. I'm ok with Reticent as it is, though I wouldn't mind if it was tweaked. But I like the idea that harvesting emotions leaves an absence of emotion in the person who was harvested, and I hope that concept remains, what ever form it may take mechanically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T22:59:49-08:00","id":833721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=833719#post833719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My thoughts on reticent, in brief: it makes sense that if a changeling feeds on someone's emotions, that person would be left emotionally drained, or outright emotionless. Just like when a vampire feeds on someone's blood, that person is left drained of blood or exsanguinated. Just like when a human feeds on animal or plant matter, that animal or plant is left physically diminished or completely gone. You can't really consume something without leaving an absence of that thing where it used to be. I'm ok with Reticent as it is, though I wouldn't mind if it was tweaked. But I like the idea that harvesting emotions leaves an absence of emotion in the person who was harvested, and I hope that concept remains, what ever form it may take mechanically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except the ability says your not feed on the person, but by products created from a person feeling emotion. It shouldn't affect the target at all since... well your not actually feeding on that persons emotions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T23:31:20-08:00","id":833731,"title":"","content":"I always saw emotional feeding is closer to drinking someone's sweat, not their blood. Drinking is perfectly harmless, but you have to make them sweat first. Which can be harmless or even positive if done right, exercise is good for people, but if you go to far they could collapse or even have a heart attack.<br /> <br /> I'd much rather the Consiquences of emotional feeding are &quot;you've fanned the married guy's desire for his secretary; what did you think that was going to do to his marriage?&quot; rather than magically emotionally drained.<br /> <br /> Roll on Monday and the update.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=833680#post833680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that I feel like I have to apologise for liking things that way IMO speaks volumes of the way I perceive the general community to be inclined towards.<br /> <br /> I want to see changelings overcome their flaws, conquer their fears, stand up to their Keepers, face the darkness and emerge scarred but victorious. I don't want those victories to be made hollow or Pyrrhic.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not the only one. It the potential for success that makes failures meaningful, if the potential isn't there or a hundred to one shot then failures have no impact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 02-20-2016, 02:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T23:36:52-08:00","id":833732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=833721#post833721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except the ability says your not feed on the person, but by products created from a person feeling emotion. It shouldn't affect the target at all since... well your not actually feeding on that persons emotions.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a supernatural ability in a setting where the supernatural in general and fae magic in particular regularly treats abstractions as discrete objects. The Chronicles of Darkness take place in a world where in the spiritual reflection of a funeral parlor you can find a puddle of grief and using the least directly zero-sum magic in the setting to summon the psychic manifestation of someone's drive for self-improvement still means <i>they don't have it anymore</i>. If I rip the air out of your lungs or the fuzzy feeling off of your brain you're going to fucking feel it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T23:51:20-08:00","id":833734,"title":"","content":"I am having serious trouble believing no one here has had the experience of having an emotional high followed by a couple of days on an emotional low. Like, I am fairly sure this is an actual, regular, common thing, so my only course of belief here is that people here aren't experiencing emotional highs, and that sounds <i>insane</i>.<br /> <br /> I can think of at least five different instances this happened for me last year! Five separate times I got the Reticent condition without a changeling to blame! And I know I don't actually have emotional or mental issues!<br /> <br /> Like, seriously, this is the animal magnetism thing all over again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T00:50:10-08:00","id":833745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=833734#post833734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am having serious trouble believing no one here has had the experience of having an emotional high followed by a couple of days on an emotional low. Like, I am fairly sure this is an actual, regular, common thing, so my only course of belief here is that people here aren't experiencing emotional highs, and that sounds <i>insane</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a person who after an emotional high not only gets days of emotional low, but also gets physically ill... That's not the reason people are disagreeing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T00:58:34-08:00","id":833747,"title":"","content":"I think we need to be through with this line of discussion. I don't think there's anywhere productive we can go from here. I think we're bordering on some stuff that not only could hurt the discourse, but it's largely irrelevant because the harvest mechanic is going to change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T01:01:46-08:00","id":833748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=833734#post833734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am having serious trouble believing no one here has had the experience of having an emotional high followed by a couple of days on an emotional low. Like, I am fairly sure this is an actual, regular, common thing, so my only course of belief here is that people here aren't experiencing emotional highs, and that sounds <i>insane</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had episodes of hours of this kind burnout, maybe a day max. I heard about it from my psych buddies, but it's very individual thing. That's why I would rather left <b><i>Reticent Condition as Dramatic Fauilre </i></b>thing and do the Willpower sapping on this &quot;dead inside&quot; to represent it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T06:46:08-08:00","id":833806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=833731#post833731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're not the only one. It the potential for success that makes failures meaningful, if the potential isn't there or a hundred to one shot then failures have no impact.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel that Changeling doesn't need a greater failure condition, because it's not like most stories. You don't start on neutral ground and have to reach for the stars or fall in the Abyss. You start in the Abyss and are reaching for blissful, normal neutrality.<br /> <br /> The consequences of failure are staying where you are. In Changeling, I can think of scant few things worse than remaining trapped with your fears and nightmares.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T08:47:46-08:00","id":833862,"title":"","content":"So, on a different line of discourse, do dream bastions manifest in the same place, or are they just randomly located?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T09:50:31-08:00","id":833887,"title":"","content":"What the heck is the deal with Fading Magic?<br /> <br /> How Changelings do know it works? Murdering your Fetch after a year and a day of denial is not a very intuitive process.<br /> <br /> What are the thematic interests of such a thing? The big deal of Changeling 1e was &quot;you can never go home again&quot; what would that change?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T09:59:42-08:00","id":833892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=833887#post833887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The big deal of Changeling 1e was &quot;you can never go home again&quot; what would that change?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue the entire point of changeling 1e (and 2e, for that matter) was finding your way home.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T10:20:08-08:00","id":833906,"title":"","content":"I'm currently not digging the odd restriction on Oaths. I'm writting up a character for a game, an Ifrit/Fireheart Darkling of the Black Rose Court. I'm taking The Love as his first touchstone, a boyfriend that helped lead my character back from Hell. Jay there might just be my character's The One. There's these wishes for marriage.<br /> <br /> Oaths are real, they're solid, they're meaningful. They're invested with hope and emotion. Parts of what makes the changeling is invested into each other. It changes and shapes you. That's what an ideal marriage should do - completing each other. But... you can't. Oaths can only be made by changelings, for changelings and with changelings. You can't actually swear a Personal Oath with your lover. And I find that really, really odd and dissonant. No, you have to swear a Bargain, which is just about what you do. Not about the heart, the soul, or the blood. This is creating an odd situation where it feels like your relationship is only a shallow one. That the only way to have a deep, lasting relationship is with another changeling. I feel like its being told that no, you can't get married. <br /> <br /> Anyways, that's my impression from making up a new PC. Haven't actually gotten around to playing yet, but its something that crossed my mind, and I thought I would share.<br /> <br /> On a related matter, mostly because it crossed my mind while reading the pledge section, where would other supernaturals lie on this continuum? Generic hobs, crossover supers, Fae-touched humans, even some of the Gentry or stranger fae, or maybe some ghosts or spirits? We only have Huntsmen, mortals, and changelings mentioned. What about the others that might be involved here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T10:54:39-08:00","id":833917,"title":"","content":"How can Changelings find someone's Bastion in order to enter it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T11:36:46-08:00","id":833935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=833917#post833917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How can Changelings find someone's Bastion in order to enter it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have asked myself this question a lot. I think it was in my first draft notes.<br /> <br /> Also, someone brought up the home thing? Yeah, it's always been about the changeling making the long way home. It's a tough fight, but in the end, every changeling can make it home.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T11:46:22-08:00","id":833947,"title":"","content":"It mentions in the Glamour trait that you can get glamour from pledges, but the only mention I see of that is the redistrubition of glamour among ones motley.<br /> <br /> And ensorcelled mortals are mentioned in various places, but I don't see anything in pledges on that or an alternate mechanic for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T11:55:41-08:00","id":833955,"title":"","content":"Last two chapters I think need more clarification...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Pledges</b></span><ul><li><b>Sealing</b> \u2013 <b>As I understand, character can have any number of Sealings, she just need to pay in Glamour, yes? </b>No roof top limitation here on instances?</li> <li><b>Oaths</b> \u2013 <b>Do I get it right that character can have any number of Oaths also? </b>Wording seems implying that any time I can make Oath \u2013 for motley, freehold, personal or any other long term dedication \u2013 I just can have my Oath on this.</li> <li><b>Oathbreaker Conditon</b> \u2013 <b>The penalty of -1 on Social rolls with changelings is automatic? </b>So that other Lost just see your Mien and understand on Wyrd level \u201cOh, he broke the Oath, I see it on him\u201d? Or it\u2019s more a gossip things \u2013 \u201cYou heard, this new Darkling in town broke an Oath. \u2013 Typical Darkling...\u201d?</li> <li><b>Motley Oaths </b>\u2013 <b>We have <i>all </i>listed game effects or only one is chosen with the creation of Motley?</b></li> <li><b>Ensorcelled mortals</b> <b>\u2013 What happen to them? </b>In 1ED it was specific Plegde. Now I do not see this. Fae-Touched and Fetches are Minor Templates and bit more powerful than mortal seeing changeling for what it is.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T11:56:50-08:00","id":833956,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Dreamwalking</b></span><ul><li><b>Hedge</b> \u2013 <b>So now the \u201cdream layer\u201d is just in the Hedge itself?</b> That all dreams and dreamers are \u201cphysically\u201d ( well, probably ephemerally more accurate ) in the Hedge?</li> <li><b>Dream Bastions </b>\u2013 <b>They are places/\u201dbubbles\u201d in the Hedge?</b> Like clearing, den, great flower buds with dreamers inside?</li> <li><b>The Gates of Horn and Ivory </b>\u2013 Do I get it correct \u2013 <b>Mortals, when they come asleep, are physically on Earth but their \u201cdream selves\u201d are in Hedge\u2019s Dream Bastions, connected to one another, yes? </b>Changelings, on the other hand, can only by in one place at time \u2013 they can physically sleep in their beds OR be in the dreams of Hedge, leaving their bed empty in the night?</li> <li><b>Oneiromachy </b>\u2013 <b>Does it mean that I can kill mortal in his dream by sending him full box of Aggravated dream attacks, leading him to have full Lethal on \u201cwaking up\u201d?!</b></li> <li><b>Magic in Dream \u2013 If there could be ghosts in dreams, why not Shadows spirits?</b> I would rather go here with <b>Astral Realms </b>route and point that \u201cother realms\u201d exists only if dreamer is connected to them. If dreamer is Thyrsus mage or werewolf, Shadow could exists very much. But most mortals would not have those \u2013 they can have one or two ephemera in dreams if they are under it\u2019s Manifestation ( like being ghosts Anchors or Urged by spirit ). If dreamer is changeling, his Contracts dictates what is and what is not in the dream \u2013 Contract with Dead will probably mean that ghosts are very much possible in this dreams realities.</li> <li><b>Convince the Dreamer \u2013 Should not the Dicepool be more <i>Wits + Persuasion + Wyrd \u2013 Intensity</i>? </b>Socialize as Skill looks weird in here. Persuasion has more logic as you try too nudge dreamer to your point of view, is it not?</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T12:03:14-08:00","id":833964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=833917#post833917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How can Changelings find someone's Bastion in order to enter it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pathfinder contract lets you find dreams!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T12:40:55-08:00","id":833978,"title":"","content":"May I ask who is the one developing the Goblin Vows?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T12:50:52-08:00","id":833980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=833956#post833956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Dreamwalking</b></span><ul><li><b>Hedge</b> \u2013 <b>So now the \u201cdream layer\u201d is just in the Hedge itself?</b> That all dreams and dreamers are \u201cphysically\u201d ( well, probably ephemerally more accurate ) in the Hedge?</li> <li><b>Dream Bastions </b>\u2013 <b>They are places/\u201dbubbles\u201d in the Hedge?</b> Like clearing, den, great flower buds with dreamers inside?</li> <li><b>The Gates of Horn and Ivory </b>\u2013 Do I get it correct \u2013 <b>Mortals, when they come asleep, are physically on Earth but their \u201cdream selves\u201d are in Hedge\u2019s Dream Bastions, connected to one another, yes? </b>Changelings, on the other hand, can only by in one place at time \u2013 they can physically sleep in their beds OR be in the dreams of Hedge, leaving their bed empty in the night?</li> <li><b>Oneiromachy </b>\u2013 <b>Does it mean that I can kill mortal in his dream by sending him full box of Aggravated dream attacks, leading him to have full Lethal on \u201cwaking up\u201d?!</b></li> <li><b>Magic in Dream \u2013 If there could be ghosts in dreams, why not Shadows spirits?</b> I would rather go here with <b>Astral Realms </b>route and point that \u201cother realms\u201d exists only if dreamer is connected to them. If dreamer is Thyrsus mage or werewolf, Shadow could exists very much. But most mortals would not have those \u2013 they can have one or two ephemera in dreams if they are under it\u2019s Manifestation ( like being ghosts Anchors or Urged by spirit ). If dreamer is changeling, his Contracts dictates what is and what is not in the dream \u2013 Contract with Dead will probably mean that ghosts are very much possible in this dreams realities.</li> <li><b>Convince the Dreamer \u2013 Should not the Dicepool be more <i>Wits + Persuasion + Wyrd \u2013 Intensity</i>? </b>Socialize as Skill looks weird in here. Persuasion has more logic as you try too nudge dreamer to your point of view, is it not?</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div> I agree with you on that it should be persausion, not socialize, its a personal experience/connection, not an attempt to fit in to or understand a society, class, culture, or subculture.<br /> <br /> Bastions I think are portals into dream based pocket planes in the Hedge.<br /> <br /> Changeling mortal (or in some cases immortal) physical bodies and Dream bodies are merged, a single body. A Fae Touched's physical body and Dream body are still seperate. Changelings are now native creatures to the dream worlds (the hedge element of dreams), along with Onieroine, Gentry, Huntsmen, and possibly fetches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T14:23:30-08:00","id":834045,"title":"","content":"On Pledges: Yeah, Sealing penalties, especially ones you invested Glamor in/trick Huntsmen into making, need to be a little harsher in some areas. One Lethal isn't very much, especially for a Huntsman for whom death is &quot;back to respawn.&quot; Unless forcing them into breaking a Pledge is (the beginnings of) a way to permanently kill them...?<br /> <br /> Also, Bargains need to have a bit more mystical power than &quot;Whatever I, as a changeling can already do&quot;, because Huntsmen aren't around <i>all </i>the time (just enough to be justifiably paranoid, but rules should emphasize there's more than their mutual game of cat-and-mouse). If Goblin Vows are anything like the Rites of Spring version (ie, freeform magic based around a concept), perhaps a die bonus/effective Catch (no Glamor cost,in other words) to completing the Lost's end of the Bargain. It'd also fit with the &quot;Huntsman Cloak&quot; effect; according to the fluff they see changelings under a Bargain not as mortals, but fae who aren't changelings and are native to Earth, ergo seeing one using their powers to fulfill a pact isn't going to trip their &quot;wait a minute...&quot; instincts at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 02-20-2016, 05:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T14:28:54-08:00","id":834050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=833978#post833978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">May I ask who is the one developing the Goblin Vows?</div> </div> </div> </div>David Hill.<br /> <br /> Are you asking who wrote it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T17:07:05-08:00","id":834137,"title":"","content":"Could you maybe use \u201cMask\u201d for the illusion that muggles see and \u201cMasque\u201d for the Anchor, or vice versa? Something to visually distinguish these two concepts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T17:14:01-08:00","id":834143,"title":"","content":"So I know No seeming is a lot worse now than before but shouldn't there at least be something for them? It seems like a lot of drawbacks with no benefits other than you got lucky and look normal. At the very least when it was presented as a merit it as just a loss of a seeming contracts as most kiths weren't as developed as they are now. When I made the character it factored in and in 2e the character's going to get it rough in the transition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T19:29:08-08:00","id":834192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=833906#post833906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm currently not digging the odd restriction on Oaths. I'm writting up a character for a game, an Ifrit/Fireheart Darkling of the Black Rose Court. I'm taking The Love as his first touchstone, a boyfriend that helped lead my character back from Hell. Jay there might just be my character's The One. There's these wishes for marriage.<br /> <br /> Oaths are real, they're solid, they're meaningful. They're invested with hope and emotion. Parts of what makes the changeling is invested into each other. It changes and shapes you. That's what an ideal marriage should do - completing each other. But... you can't. Oaths can only be made by changelings, for changelings and with changelings. You can't actually swear a Personal Oath with your lover. And I find that really, really odd and dissonant. No, you have to swear a Bargain, which is just about what you do. Not about the heart, the soul, or the blood. This is creating an odd situation where it feels like your relationship is only a shallow one. That the only way to have a deep, lasting relationship is with another changeling. I feel like its being told that no, you can't get married.<br /> <br /> Anyways, that's my impression from making up a new PC. Haven't actually gotten around to playing yet, but its something that crossed my mind, and I thought I would share.<br /> <br /> On a related matter, mostly because it crossed my mind while reading the pledge section, where would other supernaturals lie on this continuum? Generic hobs, crossover supers, Fae-touched humans, even some of the Gentry or stranger fae, or maybe some ghosts or spirits? We only have Huntsmen, mortals, and changelings mentioned. What about the others that might be involved here?</div> </div> </div> </div>Very much agree on this - I was having the same doubts about that two things.<br /> <br /> <b>Oaths <i>should</i> be possible to integrate Ensorcelled other mortals ( like lovers or family ) and maybe it's <u>exactly</u> how it's making Ensorcellment?</b> Your Oath as changeling is opening their sensens to the Mask and sustaining their &quot;open&quot; status? They are (micro-minor) Template, just because changeling is marking them by this.<br /> <br /> Second question is always important - <b>How other supernatural are on the Pledges rules?</b> Does mages get something on having Bargin with Lost? Could werewolves be under personal Oaths?<br /> <br /> And last but not least - <b>Are there number limits on Plegdes - with Sealings, Oaths and Bargins - based on Wyrd?</b> This one is tricky to get from the text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-20-2016, 10:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T20:01:09-08:00","id":834207,"title":"","content":"First of all, WOOT, MCN's doing a Black Rose Courtier! I've won at life, I'm validated as a writer, I can die happy now.<br /> <br /> Second, I would need some time to articulate why exactly I get Oaths, but there is enough of a &quot;Huh?&quot; there, even for me, that I can definitely see some editing or expansion for it. I agree that there should at least be an Oath-like mechanic that can be used for mortals. I'm not sure if I would cross into Oaths for everyone, but I'm also not going to say no to it.<br /> <br /> I have got to stop talking like I have authority over these things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T11:52:10-08:00","id":834528,"title":"","content":"So Kiths, I'm not reviewing some stuff released a while ago. One of these things is not like the others. &quot;BlightBent&quot; seems cool, but I don't get how it's a kith. what did they do for their masters? all (most? only through the B's) of the other kiths seem to be related to a job. Maybe the job portion here could get cleaned up in the final version if it hasn't already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T12:02:56-08:00","id":834536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=834528#post834528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Kiths, I'm not reviewing some stuff released a while ago. One of these things is not like the others. &quot;BlightBent&quot; seems cool, but I don't get how it's a kith. what did they do for their masters? all (most? only through the B's) of the other kiths seem to be related to a job. Maybe the job portion here could get cleaned up in the final version if it hasn't already.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blightbents are like airtouched, snowskin, fireheart and metalflesh. They don't &quot;do&quot; something in particular, rather they're &quot;made&quot; of something in order to perform various miscellaneous tasks in a hostile environment. I'm sure you'll agree that extreme pollution and toxicity would qualify as a hostile environment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T12:06:55-08:00","id":834543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=834528#post834528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Kiths, I'm not reviewing some stuff released a while ago. One of these things is not like the others. &amp;quot;BlightBent&amp;quot; seems cool, but I don't get how it's a kith. what did they do for their masters? all (most? only through the B's) of the other kiths seem to be related to a job. Maybe the job portion here could get cleaned up in the final version if it hasn't already.</div> </div> </div> </div> The Blightbent job could have been to clean up pollution for its Keeper, with the pollution slowly being absorbed into Blightbent through its skin.<br /> <br /> Another Blightbent's job might have as a genuine pig for a curious gentry who strapped the power Blightbent to a bed and started infusing its with toxic chemicals to see what happens when it does so.<br /> <br /> Another Blightbent might simply have existed in a realms of pure pollution, her job could be anything, but she was changed into a Blightbent so that Realm wouldn't poison her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T12:22:41-08:00","id":834559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=834536#post834536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Blightbents are like airtouched, snowskin, fireheart and metalflesh. They don't &quot;do&quot; something in particular, rather they're &quot;made&quot; of something in order to perform various miscellaneous tasks in a hostile environment. I'm sure you'll agree that extreme pollution and toxicity would qualify as a hostile environment.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So I would expect blightbents, ifrit, and metalflesh to be a part of the same &quot;realm&quot;, the question that the descripition poses is why did you end up as a blightbent and not something else. Same could be said of airtouched and snowskin. Fireheart seems to be well explained. Airtouched I imagine are transports, couriers and floating platforms, this should perhaps be more spelled out. Snowskin probably ice scultptures... but it seems like there should be a beyond that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Blightbent job could have been to clean up pollution for its Keeper, with the pollution slowly being absorbed into Blightbent through its skin.<br /> <br /> Another Blightbent's job might have as a genuine pig for a curious gentry who strapped the power Blightbent to a bed and started infusing its with toxic chemicals to see what happens when it does so.<br /> <br /> Another Blightbent might simply have existed in a realms of pure pollution, her job could be anything, but she was changed into a Blightbent so that Realm wouldn't poison her</div> </div> </div> </div>this is actually a pretty good set of possibilites<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T12:35:16-08:00","id":834574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=834559#post834559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I would expect blightbents, ifrit, and metalflesh to be a part of the same &quot;realm&quot;, the question that the descripition poses is why did you end up as a blightbent and not something else. Same could be said of airtouched and snowskin. Fireheart seems to be well explained. Airtouched I imagine are transports, couriers and floating platforms, this should perhaps be more spelled out. Snowskin probably ice scultptures... but it seems like there should be a beyond that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would each kith only have one job? Even Miners can be tunneldiggers or sappers. Airtouched could literally do any job in an air-themed realm of Arcadia. Blightbent could be the same for pollution and toxicity, or they could be the result of spending too much time around pollution and waste. There's no hard and fast &quot;this kith only does this thing&quot; rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T12:44:31-08:00","id":834579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=834574#post834574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why would each kith only have one job? Even Miners can be tunneldiggers or sappers. Airtouched could literally do any job in an air-themed realm of Arcadia. Blightbent could be the same for pollution and toxicity, or they could be the result of spending too much time around pollution and waste. There's no hard and fast &quot;this kith only does this thing&quot; rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>no but most of the kiths suggest &quot;you probably did this&quot;, the Gremlin seems to have one job, make me laugh or I will eat you salacius crumb.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Gremlin is a mischievous dabbler who tends to like pulling mean pranks on others. She is <br /> small and seems harmless, which lets her get into a lot of trouble. A Gremlin is created solely for <br /> the amusement of her True Fae masters. The changeling served as a court jester and fool, <br /> making a mockery of guests and causing them pain and anguish in the name of her master. If <br /> she did not perform to whatever standards her master put to her each day, she was tortured <br /> until she performed better. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T12:49:16-08:00","id":834583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=834579#post834579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">no but most of the kiths suggest &quot;you probably did this&quot;, the Gremlin seems to have one job, make me laugh or I will eat you salacius crumb.</div> </div> </div> </div>Counterpoint: Chimera.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T12:50:11-08:00","id":834585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=834579#post834579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">no but most of the kiths suggest &quot;you probably did this&quot;, the Gremlin seems to have one job, make me laugh or I will eat you salacius crumb.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but that job goes from jester to fool to prankster to biting critic. You could probably play a Gremlin as a distinguished gentleman dressed in an impeccable attire, whose job was to make cutting remarks to his Keeper about the people in his court, at the exact appropriate times. Kiths have a flavour inspiration, but they're not hard and fast rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T12:53:31-08:00","id":834586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=834585#post834585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but that job goes from jester to fool to prankster to biting critic. You could probably play a Gremlin as a distinguished gentleman dressed in an impeccable attire, whose job was to make cutting remarks to his Keeper about the people in his court, at the exact appropriate times. Kiths have a flavour inspiration, but they're not hard and fast rules.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> yes I agree, I'm simply saying that while most of them have &quot;suggestions&quot; about what they might have been used for a few don't and it seems odd, in part because presumably other changeling kiths also come out of those environments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T12:58:38-08:00","id":834588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=834586#post834586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yes I agree, I'm simply saying that while most of them have &quot;suggestions&quot; about what they might have been used for a few don't and it seems odd, in part because presumably other changeling kiths also come out of those environments.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's probably because there's a word/page limit to each section and the writers tried to avoid any one kith from taking up too much space, so they opted to be more descriptive instead of prescriptive for some of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T14:31:13-08:00","id":834631,"title":"","content":"I haven't had the chance to run any 2e games, but I did take the time to update some of my former PCs and NPCs to 2e and wowee! Probably the most impressive is one of my player's PCs, a Dual Kith Dancer // Nightsinger of the Fairest Seeming with <i>Blessing of Perfection </i>and <i>Vainglory</i>. He was good at performance in 1e, but now he's got ~20 dice, Rote &amp; 8-again. And for a mere 3 Glamour can inflict Swooning, Obsessed, Inspired and one of Deprived, Guilty or Shaken. More importantly he averages a dozen or more successes every time he performs a musical number. In one test roll he pulled 20 successes which, after some discussion with his former player, was deemed roughly enough to make Angels fall, Huntsman abandon their hunt (for to finish would be to forget that sublime performance) or for the Wyrd to join in and set off broadway-esque musical numbers.<br /> <br /> Changeling 2e is splendid. Just splendid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T15:07:33-08:00","id":834649,"title":"","content":"Well, I've finally gotten to the end of the thread after reading the playtest and letting my mind wander off to wonderful and terrifying places. Got two of my players to fill out character sheets. Two more to go.<br /> <br /> Thinking about having a Krampus-inspired Hobgoblin show up in town for their first major antagonist. He'll be abducting &quot;naughty&quot; children, and if interrogated, be very confused about why the Changelings are protecting such ungrateful brats or why parents would want their disobedient, vice-ridden children back.<br /> <br /> &quot;The people want me to do this! Why else would I be so popular on that Internet thing? I even had a cameo on Venture Bros!&quot;<br /> &quot;The fat one spoiled his dinner with candy bars and didn't eat his vegetables! And the little girl was trying to commit matricide by hopping around on a cracked sidewalk! Worse, she tried to pretend to be all innocent by saying she was playing Hopscotch, but I could see the murderous intent in her eyes!&quot;<br /> <br /> I had one player who I needed to tell that you can't reason with the Gentry, and I figure that's one way to show the difficulty with trying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T16:51:38-08:00","id":834696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BronzeDog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=834649#post834649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And the little girl was trying to commit matricide by hopping around on a cracked sidewalk! Worse, she tried to pretend to be all innocent by saying she was playing Hopscotch, but I could see the murderous intent in her eyes!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This is beautiful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T18:32:35-08:00","id":834736,"title":"","content":"Im curious if when a changeling sleeps and chooces to go into her bastion, if the changling can leave the bastion and exit through the hedge to return to the mortal world, or if she must return to where she fell asleep<br /> <br /> also, if a changeling can choose to go to her bastion when knocked unconscious.<br /> <br /> adds another level to changeling being able to escape almost anything..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T23:22:16-08:00","id":834861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wrequis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=834736#post834736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im curious if when a changeling sleeps and chooces to go into her bastion, if the changling can leave the bastion and exit through the hedge to return to the mortal world, or if she must return to where she fell asleep<br /> <br /> also, if a changeling can choose to go to her bastion when knocked unconscious.<br /> <br /> adds another level to changeling being able to escape almost anything..</div> </div> </div> </div>The Dreamsteps contract let's you do that! The leaving a bastion for the hedge or mortal world bit anyways. <br /> <br /> Maybe someone with medical knowledge could speak up about whether people knocked unconscious can actually dream? I'd imagine the line between injury-unconscious and sleep is fairly fuzzy, with people being able to slip into regular sleep once their brain recovers from being whacked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T07:11:49-08:00","id":835015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LLegume</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=834861#post834861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Dreamsteps contract let's you do that! The leaving a bastion for the hedge or mortal world bit anyways.<br /> <br /> Maybe someone with medical knowledge could speak up about whether people knocked unconscious can actually dream? I'd imagine the line between injury-unconscious and sleep is fairly fuzzy, with people being able to slip into regular sleep once their brain recovers from being whacked.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, dreaming happens in REM sleep, which only happens after going through previous stages of sleep. Being knocked out doesn't start you down those stages, though (as you said) it is possible for you transition to dreaming after being knocked out without waking up in between. But it's not a given, and they're different states. It's like the difference between a computer's screensaver turning on (sleep) and having the power cord pulled out (knocked out).<br /> <br /> That said, medically, there's only a small portion of time spent asleep that is spend dreaming (REM sleep). Does this mean the Changeling only fades out during REM? Do they fade back in during other stages (these stages cycle through the night), or do they only come back when they wake up? Or is the science being overridden by magic and Changelings just fade out when asleep? Or is it (as many things) GM discretion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T07:33:13-08:00","id":835034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=834631#post834631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't had the chance to run any 2e games, but I did take the time to update some of my former PCs and NPCs to 2e and wowee! Probably the most impressive is one of my player's PCs, a Dual Kith Dancer // Nightsinger of the Fairest Seeming with <i>Blessing of Perfection </i>and <i>Vainglory</i>. He was good at performance in 1e, but now he's got ~20 dice, Rote &amp; 8-again. And for a mere 3 Glamour can inflict Swooning, Obsessed, Inspired and one of Deprived, Guilty or Shaken. More importantly he averages a dozen or more successes every time he performs a musical number. In one test roll he pulled 20 successes which, after some discussion with his former player, was deemed roughly enough to make Angels fall, Huntsman abandon their hunt (for to finish would be to forget that sublime performance) or for the Wyrd to join in and set off broadway-esque musical numbers.<br /> <br /> Changeling 2e is splendid. Just splendid.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my experience, this has been my favourite way to do Changeling. Changelings are powerful, and often frighteningly, exceptionally so, but usually only in very narrow circumstances. The kind of concentration of power that makes a Changeling a stunning performer deprives them of power elsewhere; they might be good, even formidable, in other areas, but they're not as staggeringly grand as in this example here. Changeling is a really fun game to hyper-focus in, because it breeds the kinds of astounding strengths and extreme weaknesses you see in fairy tales.<br /> <br /> As far as using rolls like that, I think my way to use it would be to have the player take a very significant penalty (-5 or even -10, to represent a task normally considered beyond impossible), but, as you might notice, that doesn't really ding the dice pool much; you're still pretty much guaranteed not just a success but an exceptional one. At that level, the Huntsman is moved by the one and only thing that alleviates the pain of its existence and might even start reconsidering its loyalties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T11:11:43-08:00","id":835192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=835015#post835015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, dreaming happens in REM sleep, which only happens after going through previous stages of sleep. Being knocked out doesn't start you down those stages, though (as you said) it is possible for you transition to dreaming after being knocked out without waking up in between. But it's not a given, and they're different states. It's like the difference between a computer's screensaver turning on (sleep) and having the power cord pulled out (knocked out).<br /> <br /> That said, medically, there's only a small portion of time spent asleep that is spend dreaming (REM sleep). Does this mean the Changeling only fades out during REM? Do they fade back in during other stages (these stages cycle through the night), or do they only come back when they wake up? Or is the science being overridden by magic and Changelings just fade out when asleep? Or is it (as many things) GM discretion?</div> </div> </div> </div> In human sleep REM is a small part, but in Changeling's unique sleep most of it could REM sleep, Changelings likely would have their own","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T11:39:27-08:00","id":835230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=835034#post835034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my experience, this has been my favourite way to do Changeling. Changelings are powerful, and often frighteningly, exceptionally so, but usually only in very narrow circumstances. The kind of concentration of power that makes a Changeling a stunning performer deprives them of power elsewhere; they might be good, even formidable, in other areas, but they're not as staggeringly grand as in this example here. Changeling is a really fun game to hyper-focus in, because it breeds the kinds of astounding strengths and extreme weaknesses you see in fairy tales.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed 100%. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=835034#post835034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as using rolls like that, I think my way to use it would be to have the player take a very significant penalty (-5 or even -10, to represent a task normally considered beyond impossible), but, as you might notice, that doesn't really ding the dice pool much; you're still pretty much guaranteed not just a success but an exceptional one. At that level, the Huntsman is moved by the one and only thing that alleviates the pain of its existence and might even start reconsidering its loyalties.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, this is the point at which a storyteller should just throw out dice altogether (One of them, I'm quite fond of throwing out dice). The Changeling essentially cannot fail, or even succeed mundanely. Everytime they dance the world dances with them. The only reason to throw dice is to have a hearty laugh at how ridiculous the final number is.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T12:29:18-08:00","id":835272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=834207#post834207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all, WOOT, MCN's doing a Black Rose Courtier! I've won at life, I'm validated as a writer, I can die happy now.</div> </div> </div> </div>You did a good job with them. My group likes the idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second, I would need some time to articulate why exactly I get Oaths, but there is enough of a &quot;Huh?&quot; there, even for me, that I can definitely see some editing or expansion for it. I agree that there should at least be an Oath-like mechanic that can be used for mortals. I'm not sure if I would cross into Oaths for everyone, but I'm also not going to say no to it.<br /> <br /> I have got to stop talking like I have authority over these things. </div> </div> </div> Well, I kinda get what they were going for too; it wasn't until I was sitting down and wanted to make a character that it struck me as off.<br /> <br /> Oaths should mean -something-. They're major. You shouldn't use them casually. Everyone and their brother shouldn't be involved But why that means only changelings is where I'm floundering. Sure, you'll likely be closer (or hateful) to the fellow Lost than you will others, but the exceptions is where I catch myself. I mean, even Werewolf is accepting of mortals and other supernaturals into their packs. And what's wrong with an oath of vengence against hobs or other fae creatures?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=834192#post834192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And last but not least - <b>Are there number limits on Plegdes - with Sealings, Oaths and Bargins - based on Wyrd?</b> This one is tricky to get from the text.</div> </div> </div> </div>As for the limits? I don't know. Unlike Mage, who used the limit on spells as a major factor, limits on pledges quickly proved to be meaningless in many games. I don't know anyone that really pushed the cap. It never felt like it was necessary or needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-22-2016, 03:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T12:43:35-08:00","id":835284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=834207#post834207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all, WOOT, MCN's doing a Black Rose Courtier! I've won at life, I'm validated as a writer, I can die happy now.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=835272#post835272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You did a good job with them. My group likes the idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you share this court? It sounds really interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T12:55:39-08:00","id":835296,"title":"","content":"The original, messy but fuller version of them is in the Court Creation thread-I'll get links and bring them here.<br /> <br /> The Rosiere Freehold is making it's way into the corebook. It's not as detailed as what you have in the thread, but it has more mechanics and some much better polish. Once it gets to second draft form, I'll toss it up so you have a city other than Toronto to look at.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=559072#post559072\">The Rose Courts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=572106#post572106\">La Maison Du Regret</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=572920#post572920\">l'Egare, the Wayward</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=573070#post573070\">Into The Depths</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=573370#post573370\">la Duel Final and les Marries</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=575415#post575415\">The Sovereigns of Paris and the Score of the Spheres</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=576033#post576033\">The Duels and the Paramours, plus sidebars</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=577649#post577649\">1001 Problems, but a Belle Ain't One of Them</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-22-2016, 07:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T14:04:25-08:00","id":835352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=835230#post835230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, this is the point at which a storyteller should just throw out dice altogether (One of them, I'm quite fond of throwing out dice). The Changeling essentially cannot fail, or even succeed mundanely. Everytime they dance the world dances with them. The only reason to throw dice is to have a hearty laugh at how ridiculous the final number is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have trouble bringing myself to throw out the dice. Even when characters are superhumanly skilled, I like to keep a <i>hint</i> of possibility for their failure; it adds tension, and causes big, dramatic moments to feel like the character pulled off a miracle rather than simply being a fiat force of nature. Plus, extreme dice penalties can help make extreme dice pools and successes have some meaning. Huge penalties put some heft behind the idea of extreme skill being a form of magic in its own right.<br /> <br /> Ostensibly, for example, the rules at present say that you need some manner of Cover to hide, but, if I had, say, a stealth-focused Changeling, I might just say that lack of cover merely imposes an extreme penalty (say, a -15). The most absolutely skilled person in the world can field, barring equipment and Willpower, twelve dice. If they're wearing a sound-dampening suit and spend Willpower, they'd have 1-3 dice after the penalty, depending on equipment quality. That is, mind you, the best human being on the planet wearing specialty equipment; someone who would make James Bond look like a chump.<br /> <br /> A Changeling, meanwhile, can theoretically bump up their Stealth to ludicrous proportions with a mixture of Kith blessings, Merits, and Contracts, on top of natural skill. That means a Changeling doesn't need to be invisible; they can do Bugs-Bunny-esque things of sneaking behind someone and mimicking their motions exactly. When players pull that off, it gives weight to those little numbers on the sheet and tell you exactly how good this character is at what they do.<br /> <br /> There's benefits to doing it both ways, since failure in a dramatic moment in a way that <i>isn't</i> fun can really bunk up a chronicle, and fudging the roll after takes away from the sense of immersion far more than just not having it to begin with does, but such is life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T14:09:04-08:00","id":835359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=835352#post835352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have trouble bringing myself to throw out the dice. Even when characters are superhumanly skilled, I like to keep a <i>hint</i> of possibility for their failure; it adds tension, and causes big, dramatic moments to feel like the character pulled off a miracle rather than simply being a fiat force of nature. Plus, extreme dice penalties can help make extreme dice pools and successes have some meaning. Huge penalties put some heft behind the idea of extreme skill being a form of magic in its own right.<br /> <br /> Ostensibly, for example, the rules at present say that you need some manner of Cover to hide, but, if I had, say, a stealth-focused Changeling, I might just say that lack of cover merely imposes an extreme penalty (say, a -15). The most absolutely skilled person in the world can field, barring equipment and Willpower, twelve dice. If they're wearing a sound-dampening suit and spend Willpower, they'd have 1-3 dice after the penalty, depending on equipment quality. That is, mind you, the best human being on the planet wearing specialty equipment; someone who would make James Bond look like a chump.<br /> <br /> A Changeling, meanwhile, can theoretically bump up their Stealth to ludicrous proportions with a mixture of Kith blessings, Merits, and Contracts, on top of natural skill. That means a Changeling doesn't need to be invisible; they can do Bugs-Bunny-esque things of sneaking behind someone and mimicking their motions exactly. When players pull that off, it gives weight to those little numbers on the sheet and tell you exactly how good this character is at what they do.<br /> <br /> There's benefits to doing it both ways, since failure in a dramatic moment in a way that <i>isn't</i> fun can really bunk up a chronicle, and fudging the roll after takes away from the sense of immersion far more than just not having it to begin with does, but such is life.</div> </div> </div> </div>As with all things tabletop it really depends on the group. I run with a bunch of actors, writers, and comedians, all used to Improve Theater, so I find that quite often there is simply no need for dice. The players create drama, tension and excitement all on their own. But I've also run groups where the dice are, as you said, essential to tension. And the players would otherwise drift off, lose focus, or just go way out of control. Of course, dice can cause that as well, which all folds back to &quot;it really depends on the group&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T04:12:38-08:00","id":835671,"title":"","content":"With a fae mount's actor mask, does it increase the fae mounts speed to that of the vehicle it pretends to be if the mask is of a vehicle?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T06:17:19-08:00","id":835702,"title":"","content":"I figured it would just make it look like a vehicle of an appropriate speed. It's supposed to be identical to a horse, which in the public animal stats has speed 20 (if you go by it's actual stats) which can potentially be doubled to 40. That gives it a running speed of about 54 mph.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T06:40:50-08:00","id":835714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=835702#post835702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I figured it would just make it look like a vehicle of an appropriate speed. It's supposed to be identical to a horse, which in the public animal stats has speed 20 (if you go by it's actual stats) which can potentially be doubled to 40. That gives it a running speed of about 54 mph.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which means you cannot use it to have a motorbike form (which have speeds of 100), despite the fact the actor mask ability specifcally uses a motorbike as one of it's examples. If you look at the vehicle rules, none have speeds of 40 or less. Lowest is 60.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T07:23:38-08:00","id":835751,"title":"","content":"A Speed of 40 equals a running speed of 80, So a fae mount can go as fast as a car small, which is faster than the speed limit in a lot of cities. If you still think that's too slow just let Manyleague stack. 3 of those and it'll be able to outpace a sports car with no trouble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T13:39:20-08:00","id":835994,"title":"","content":"I have a question about &quot;Caging a Dream&quot;:<br /> It can be used to escape from powers like: Dominate(Vampire), Vinculum(Vampire), Mind(Mage), Possession(Numina), etc?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T13:48:21-08:00","id":836000,"title":"","content":"Um. no. Why would it work like that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T13:54:40-08:00","id":836006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=835994#post835994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question about &quot;Caging a Dream&quot;:<br /> It can be used to escape from powers like: Dominate(Vampire), Vinculum(Vampire), Mind(Mage), Possession(Numina), etc?</div> </div> </div> </div>My reading of it is that it's physical, not mental. Escaping from mental powers like that would be WAY too powerful, I think, as an innate template ability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T14:18:14-08:00","id":836026,"title":"","content":"On the subject of Oaths: could you maybe expand the scope from \u201cother changelings\u201d to something like \u201cfae (including changelings, hobgoblins, huntsmen, and fetches), fae-touched, and your Touchstone\u201d? I get where MCN is coming from; while Oaths should be reserved for characters with whom you're emotionally invested (i.e., you don't swear Oaths with random strangers), you shouldn't assume that the only people that warrant such attention should be other changelings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T14:28:20-08:00","id":836031,"title":"","content":"'Til the Stars Do (Not) Bind Us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T16:49:12-08:00","id":836099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=836006#post836006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My reading of it is that it's physical, not mental. Escaping from mental powers like that would be WAY too powerful, I think, as an innate template ability.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Besdies, the Clarity bonuses should already apply to such magics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T09:30:54-08:00","id":836476,"title":"","content":"Okay, having now taken the time to read through the entirety of the previewed Contracts I have some more in depth thoughts.<br /> <br /> First off, I really love these. I love how they've been streamlined to eliminate wasted design space. No more of 1st edition's rigid five dot progression, no more dud clauses padding the actually interesting stuff, no more splitting powers up so that you need two clauses to use a power effectively. Every dot in here is worthwhile and it's glorious. There are so many cases where two similar contracts have been folded into one, taking advantage of exceptional or seeming effects.<br /> <br /> Unmaker's Destructive Gaze was always just a ranged Touch of the Workman's Wrath, and it fits perfectly as a Wizened specific enhancement. Light Shy was functionally an enhanced Shadow Patch and now it squeezes both mechanics into the base effect and the exceptional.<br /> <br /> The one that caught me most by surprise was Become the Primal Foundation sneaking in as the Elemental variant of Phantom Glory. It makes sense when I think about it, and it combines what were already two of my favorite capstone powers.<br /> <br /> Also, I cannot overstate how pleased I am that Might of the Terrible Brute has a dex option now. Dex builds are a lot of fun and have some great opportunities for interesting synergy, but the lack of abilities to boost dex made them prohibitively expensive.<br /> <br /> <br /> My one major concern is Changeling Hours; it has some incredibly broad leeway to cause trouble, especially the Fairest effect. With all the ways to boost dice pools it's not too hard to get an exceptional, and freezing something in time permanently feels rather beyond the scope of what Changelings should be easily capable of. Especially applied to people, this contract gets weird fast. I'm not comfortable with the possibility of freezing an enemy in time permanently. Also, what does &quot;newly made&quot; mean applied to people? Do they turn into babies? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T10:01:16-08:00","id":836501,"title":"","content":"For living things ageing and growing are technically different processes. Since Changeling Hours specifies that it reverses damage though <i>ageing</i> the first power should only revert a human to the point where they stopped growing, around their mid-twenties. It could be argued that before that point they weren't quite &quot;finished&quot; in a strictly material sense.<br /> <br /> It might be worth a line banning the exceptional success effect from living beings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 02-24-2016, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T11:03:31-08:00","id":836534,"title":"","content":"I posted this earlier but I think it got overlooked.<br /> <br /> I think Tying the Knots of Fate and Glimpse of a Distant Mirror could use a bit of a boost, because neither of them can match the most famous faerie tale equivalent.<br /> <br /> For Tying the Knots of Fate that's Sleeping Beauty. Tying the Knots explicitly says that you can't dictate the outcome of the event, but in Sleeping Beauty the curse was &quot;prick your finger on a spinning wheel, and die&quot;.<br /> <br /> A simple solution would be to boost the Fariest and Ogre variants. Fairest can specify a positive outcome, Ogres can specify a negative outcome. I'd also suggest adding a Wizened which variant lets you add a loophole to existing fates (if you know they're there). The changeling thus specifies a loophole that will prevent the fate, or a situation which will reverse the fate depending on what's more suitable.<br /> <br /> <br /> For Glimpse of a Distant Mirror it's Snow White. The Contract has no ability to perform the &quot;Who's the Fairest of them All&quot;. A simple solution would be to add a Fairest varient that lets you find who's the best at something in a chosen area.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T11:10:57-08:00","id":836538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=836501#post836501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For living things ageing and growing are technically different processes. Since Changeling Hours specifies that it reverses damage though <i>ageing</i> the first power should only revert a human to the point where they stopped growing, around their mid-twenties. It could be argued that before that point they weren't quite &quot;finished&quot; in a strictly material sense.<br /> <br /> It might be worth a line banning the exceptional success effect from living beings.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Unfortunately the way the actual chemistry works it is that we age because we grow...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T11:16:53-08:00","id":836542,"title":"","content":"Slowly burning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T11:18:06-08:00","id":836543,"title":"","content":"Well, either way the extra abilities for that contract could do with a bit of clarification as to what exactly they mean. How many years is one point of damage worth, anyway?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T12:46:30-08:00","id":836600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=836534#post836534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I posted this earlier but I think it got overlooked.<br /> <br /> I think Tying the Knots of Fate and Glimpse of a Distant Mirror could use a bit of a boost, because neither of them can match the most famous faerie tale equivalent.<br /> <br /> For Tying the Knots of Fate that's Sleeping Beauty. Tying the Knots explicitly says that you can't dictate the outcome of the event, but in Sleeping Beauty the curse was &amp;quot;prick your finger on a spinning wheel, and die&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> A simple solution would be to boost the Fariest and Ogre variants. Fairest can specify a positive outcome, Ogres can specify a negative outcome. I'd also suggest adding a Wizened which variant lets you add a loophole to existing fates (if you know they're there). The changeling thus specifies a loophole that will prevent the fate, or a situation which will reverse the fate depending on what's more suitable.<br /> <br /> <br /> For Glimpse of a Distant Mirror it's Snow White. The Contract has no ability to perform the &amp;quot;Who's the Fairest of them All&amp;quot;. A simple solution would be to add a Fairest varient that lets you find who's the best at something in a chosen area.</div> </div> </div> </div> That Fairest idea is great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T12:50:36-08:00","id":836603,"title":"","content":"Thanks.<br /> <br /> (You mean the Glimpse of a Distant Mirror idea right?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T12:57:54-08:00","id":836611,"title":"","content":"Reposting this here from the other thread (think I made a mistake).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the Skin Mask Contract, does the Catch work only if you're trying to become an exact copy of the person whose clothes you have, or does it accep