quot;no werewolf mating&quot; idea, did the changeling crew do similar to changelings being infertile? I mean, sure, there are goblin fruits, probably goblin contracts, marketplace tokens,etc and thats not counting Mummies or Mages. I am still curious though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T17:06:36-08:00","id":836751,"title":"","content":"I was really looking through all the different kiths and I think it would be really cool to have something like a Wizard kith that could learn mortal supernatural merits at a dot discount but i dont know if that would be over powered. I just think there seems to be so many opitions for a front line or a survival kind of character but there only seems to be a few really occult focused kiths for example the gravekeeper and witchtooth kiths<br /> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11277-hyperspacewizard","name":"hyperspacewizard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T17:12:28-08:00","id":836755,"title":"","content":"If ya wanna play a wizard, go play Mage. Fae are magical in a different way, and it'd be weird to put them in those shoes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T17:25:35-08:00","id":836759,"title":"","content":"Its not so much that i want to play a wizard as i think there should be more options for a changeling who was taken by the fae for his occult interest in his mortal life like a wiccan or ceremonial magician did something to attract a fae's attention or even the classic old man wise woman style kith that gives out wisdom","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11277-hyperspacewizard","name":"hyperspacewizard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T17:53:30-08:00","id":836767,"title":"","content":"Well there is the Witchtooth, Gravewright, Ifrit, Greys, The German one with telekenic powers, Oni, Anqiarious, Fireheart (goes well with Goblin vows), just off the top of my head.<br /> <br /> If you want a strong Occult feel I'd go with say Witchtooth/ Ifrit Dual Kith Darkling or Wizened, and join the Autumn Court and get some more Goblin Vows based on occult typics.<br /> <br /> Goblin Vows Demon Summoning, Goblin Vows Undead, Goblin Vows Divination, Goblin Vows Grimiores, Goblin Vows Pagan Gods, Goblin Vows Bearded Wizards, Goblin Vows Wicca are some possiblities.<br /> <br /> I think I read somewhere that the Kiths might end up orginized by type. I could be wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T18:01:25-08:00","id":836768,"title":"","content":"Undead is likely too vague for Goblin Vows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T18:02:33-08:00","id":836770,"title":"","content":"I am fairly certain you cannot Goblin Vow with Bearded Wizards.<br /> <br /> But I completely forgot about Kiths like Witchtooth, so what do I know?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T18:18:13-08:00","id":836777,"title":"","content":"So does anyone know what supernatural effect hedgespun items are going to be able to have or is that going to be left up to storyteller judgement also thanks for the ideals a moonborn/author would be a good cthulhu style mad investigator. AHA I was looking through the supernatural merits for the hurt locker spoilers and something like the Phantasmagoria merit would be amazing for a kith blessing or even just translating it to a changeling contract maybe a Darkling addition that would allow you to cause more serious conditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11277,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11277-hyperspacewizard","user":"hyperspacewizard","date":". 02-24-2016, 09:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11277-hyperspacewizard","name":"hyperspacewizard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T18:41:32-08:00","id":836786,"title":"","content":"Here I've put the Kiths into catagories, some in multiple catagories. Many aren't a perfect fit, but it gives you an idea of how many Kith blessing lean towards a particular use.<br /> <br /> I think doing this has made it easier for me to plan future Characters.<br /> <br /> Movement/Survival (Air Touched, Farwalker, Levinquick, Nix, Runnerswift, Sandharrow, Tunnelgrub, Waterborn, Woodwalker, Lurkglider, Windwing, Swimmerskin, Steepscrambler)<br /> <br /> Occult (Antiquarian, Blightbent, Brightone, Chimera, Fireheart, Gravewright, Grey, Ifrit, Waterborn, Leechfinger, Moonborn, Oni, Oracle, Telluric, Witchtooth, Weisse Frau)<br /> <br /> Knowledge/Science (Author, Chirurgeon, Antiquarian, Fireheart, Gameplayer, Riddleseeker, Slewfoot, Cleareyes)<br /> <br /> Fighters (Bloodbrute, Coldscales, Draconic, Earthbones, Gargantuan, Gristlegrinder, Hunterheart, Jeweleyes, Leechfinger, Levinquick, Metalflesh, Razorhand, Render, Roteater, Sandharrow, Skitterskulk, Venombite, Soldier, Corpseginder, Lurkglider)<br /> <br /> Social (Brollachan, Broadback, Chatelain, Chimera, Coyote, Draconic, Flowering, Illes, Larcenist, Mirrorskin, Muse, Nix, Playmate, Polychromatic, Snowskin, Thusser, Troll, Truefriend, Whisperwisp, Flamesiren, Shadowsoul, Dearheart)<br /> <br /> Creators/Artists/Proformance (Artist, Author, Brewer, Cyclopean, Dancer, Gremlin (anticreator), Maker, Manikin, Minstrel, Muse, Nightsinger, Smith, Thusser, Miner)<br /> <br /> Stealth/Thief (Brollachan, Larcanist, Lurker, Palewraith, Skogsra, Whisperwisp, Shadowsoul, Woodblood).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T18:50:24-08:00","id":836790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hyperspacewizard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=836777#post836777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So does anyone know what supernatural effect hedgespun items are going to be able to have or is that going to be left up to storyteller judgement also thanks for the ideals a moonborn/author would be a good cthulhu style mad investigator. AHA I was looking through the supernatural merits for the hurt locker spoilers and something like the Phantasmagoria merit would be amazing for a kith blessing or even just translating it to a changeling contract maybe a Darkling addition that would allow you to cause more serious conditions.</div> </div> </div> </div> Luna's Bedlam Contract + Moonborn already allow you to give someone a whole bunch of mental health conditions, such as Lunacy, Madness, Obsession, Fugue, Lost, Amniasa, and with the Fairest &amp; Ogre Effects Swooning, Wanton, Broken, and couple of others. You can just destroy someones sanity like that, and there is few more contracts that can add Clarity Breaking points, and more conditions like Shaken and Spooked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T19:05:24-08:00","id":836800,"title":"","content":"Its more the fact that you can make illusions that attracted me to the phantasmagoria merit the darkling addition was just an ideal off the top of my head a more well thought out ideal would be a contract that allowed you to make harmless illusions but with a wizened addition that you can program an item to show the person who touches it a pre made one kinda like a waking world version of the dream vessels","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11277-hyperspacewizard","name":"hyperspacewizard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T20:00:11-08:00","id":836821,"title":"","content":"I would guess Hedgespun is mechanically similar to first edition, but it's something I'm definitely curious about because it's been one of my favorite parts of the game since I first read Rites of Spring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T21:28:44-08:00","id":836845,"title":"","content":"Does anyone know if Entitlements are still going to exist in 2nd?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11277-hyperspacewizard","name":"hyperspacewizard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T21:47:14-08:00","id":836851,"title":"","content":"Yes, they will. We have the write up for them and everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T21:47:32-08:00","id":836852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hyperspacewizard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=836845#post836845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone know if Entitlements are still going to exist in 2nd?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I managed to fit them in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T00:01:44-08:00","id":836888,"title":"","content":"A check re: Hollow: Am I reading it correctly that the single baseline entrance is a gate from the mortal world to the Hollow's chunk of the Hedge, and thus that there isn't any particular worry about East Access leading to unexpected guests trying to find their suit jacket in the closet you last ducked in from?<br /> <br /> Similarly, does the exit available through Escape Route come out in the Hedge, the mortal realm, or either?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T08:12:02-08:00","id":837033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=836852#post836852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes. I managed to fit them in.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, you rock.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T13:19:13-08:00","id":837734,"title":"","content":"Based on our initial character creation efforts, here is the feedback we've got on some of the kiths that we've been considering. Most of them are quite excellent, and we wouldn't change a thing about them. We did have a couple thoughts on some of them, though.<br /> <br /> Brewers have always been popular for our games. I was disappointed to see that they've lost their resistance to poisons, though. It seems like that would still be fitting for them, given that the rest of their Blessing requires them to spend Glamour.<br /> <br /> I could see Coyotes being able to spend a point of Glamour to add Wyrd to Subterfuge rolls made to lie or inspire trust.<br /> <br /> Since Gremlins are treated as pranksters and jesters rather than merely destroyers, it would be nice if they didn't require a complex machine to be used in order to use their Blessing. After all, a jester making a mockery of someone for tripping over their own two feet would be quite appropriate in one of the Keeper's lands that lacked complicated machinery. Even if the object was still required, perhaps it could be any object rather than a complex one, such as a walking stick that breaks at the worst moment. At the very least, it would be nice to see their Blessing being able to be used more than once per scene. A bonus to rolls attempting to humiliate others could also take care of the jester angle in the absence of machinery.<br /> <br /> Playmates seem like they could use a little bit of a boost, given that the entirety of their Blessing is reliant upon them engaging in teamwork efforts. I could see giving them some sort of benefit to either Socialize or Empathy rolls, giving them an easier time finding companions. <br /> <br /> Does the Render's ability to ignore armor function only against material armor, or would it work just as well against armor created by magical effects?<br /> <br /> Are the Thussers able to choose some people to be immune to their performance? If they're not, their Blessing's mechanics don't seem to fit with the flavor text. The implication I'd gotten from it was that they could distract with their performance while either the changeling or someone connected to them stole from the entranced audience, but the mechanics seem to indicate that nobody could act at all unless they first managed to resist the effects.<br /> <br /> Airtouched and Lurkgliders both have Blessings that protect them from falls until terminal velocity. At that point, do they suffer the same damage anyone else would suffer, or does their falling damage begin like they were a normal mortal suffering a fall starting at that point?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T12:08:34-08:00","id":838164,"title":"","content":"I have been absolutely delighted at the dreaming systems. They have all been excellent, and I can't wait to see the Merits that relate to them.<br /> <br /> The only thing that stands out as odd to me is that a changeling is unable to dream without vanishing from the physical world, and that to maintain their presence there they must hide their supernatural nature at the cost of their Willpower. I think that I would prefer it if choosing the Gate of Ivory resulted in them having shallow dreams that function as ordinary dreams like a mortal would experience. They would still gain their Willpower for slumbering, but while doing so, they would be just as vulnerable as mortals in their dreams to those that would seek to meddle with them. This would still give them a good reason to choose the Gate of Horn, but it would make the Gate of Ivory a valid option for changelings that wished to maintain the illusion of normalcy without it proving to be untenable for those that did return to their mortal lives.<br /> <br /> Are Hedgespun items permanent creations, capable of being taken out of the Hedge?<br /> <br /> The Succubi are delightfully insidious, and interesting problems that really require helpful changelings to solve. I assume that the damage that they deal after the Willpower is gone takes the form of extreme fatigue rather than actual wounds. Do their victims start to realize something is wrong, or do these Wish Fulfillment dreams keep them coming back for more even though they haven't gained the Willpower from it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T12:38:53-08:00","id":838170,"title":"","content":"I'd imagine that the drained mortals would be losing perspective, finding the waking world harder and harder to deal with, only thinking about their next fix of pleasant dreams.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T23:19:50-08:00","id":838992,"title":"","content":"Small random question: Will there be Contracts that let you manipulate the weather? If not, I have some Homebrewing to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T23:22:03-08:00","id":838993,"title":"","content":"A glance at the Seasonal Contracts says yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T23:25:00-08:00","id":838995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=838993#post838993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A glance at the Seasonal Contracts says yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does that mean there are some previews out on the forums?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T00:10:58-08:00","id":839002,"title":"","content":"That's a nope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T05:31:05-08:00","id":839079,"title":"","content":"According to my highly scientific sample pool of &quot;one&quot;, if you engage Arc in mild yet friendly snark whilst effectively begging for a spoiler, DaveH will post said spoiler the next day.<br /> <br /> What could go wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T07:31:16-08:00","id":839154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=839079#post839079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to my highly scientific sample pool of &amp;quot;one&amp;quot;, if you engage Arc in mild yet friendly snark whilst effectively begging for a spoiler, DaveH will post said spoiler the next day.<br /> <br /> What could go wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div> LMFAO, very amusing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T08:57:21-08:00","id":839221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=839079#post839079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to my highly scientific sample pool of &quot;one&quot;, if you engage Arc in mild yet friendly snark whilst effectively begging for a spoiler, DaveH will post said spoiler the next day.<br /> <br /> What could go wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a ritual, really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T09:07:17-08:00","id":839230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=838993#post838993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A glance at the Seasonal Contracts says yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that seasonal as in the Seasonal Courts, or is that a separate thing? If so, I hope they're more generally available than before. Nature is such a powerful Changeling theme, being able to control the weather feels like it ought to be more... Universal. Darklings should be able to call storms at night to cover their approach; Snowskins should be able to call up chilly winds and snowstorms to waylay their prey. That sort of junk.<br /> <br /> It'd also be neat if said Contracts could apply benefits to Hollows, like, say, allowing a character to create a persistent weather effect in the Hedge surrounding the Hollow, but I babble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T13:38:05-08:00","id":839398,"title":"","content":"I could easily imagine that just being part of the Hollow merit: I'd absolutely let them spend a dot of said merit (assuming it functions the same) via the Amenities &quot;sub-merit&quot; for weather patterns.<br /> <br /> For the Seasonal contracts, I believe they're talking about the Seasonal Court's contracts. . .and since there are no &quot;true&quot; official Courts, that means that should mean that said Contracts are made via some &quot;build-a-Contract&quot; rule, or perhaps even &quot;build-a-Court-Contract&quot; rule if Court Contracts are supposed to be even better than normal Contracts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T13:49:05-08:00","id":839407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=839398#post839398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could easily imagine that just being part of the Hollow merit: I'd absolutely let them spend a dot of said merit (assuming it functions the same) via the Amenities &quot;sub-merit&quot; for weather patterns.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2K8R3qXyDyoN3MxVEhfNWxPb2s/view\" target=\"_blank\">\u2026Hollow's been spoiled.</a> There is no &quot;sub-Merit,&quot; it works like Bolthole now where you just apply dots toward effects. The &quot;Home Turf&quot; effect could probably be fluffed as a weather effect, but &quot;persistent weather effect&quot; and &quot;the Hedge&quot; are kind of already mutually inclusive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T14:20:11-08:00","id":839425,"title":"","content":"I don't think they're any more mutually exclusive than Hollows are, or any other persistent feature of the Hedge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T14:29:31-08:00","id":839436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=839425#post839425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think they're any more mutually exclusive than Hollows are, or any other persistent feature of the Hedge.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026Read the word again, Axel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T15:02:20-08:00","id":839453,"title":"","content":"Pleasant Weather should fall under the Luxury option of the Hollow Merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T15:14:34-08:00","id":839466,"title":"","content":"... Right. In my defense, I didn't get to eat until about 4 PM today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T17:44:23-08:00","id":839562,"title":"","content":"Contracts of the Wild had one of the better weather control contracts in first edition, and it was universal (well, Beast/Elemental affinity, strictly speaking) so there's definitely precedent for weather control outside the Seasonal Court contracts<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T18:05:08-08:00","id":839578,"title":"","content":"I figure this might not be important enough to mention in the core, but can supernaturals or mortals not connected to the Wyrd possess dots in Hollow?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T18:29:43-08:00","id":839591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=839407#post839407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2K8R3qXyDyoN3MxVEhfNWxPb2s/view\" target=\"_blank\">\u2026Hollow's been spoiled.</a> There is no &quot;sub-Merit,&quot; it works like Bolthole now where you just apply dots toward effects. The &quot;Home Turf&quot; effect could probably be fluffed as a weather effect, but &quot;persistent weather effect&quot; and &quot;the Hedge&quot; are kind of already mutually inclusive.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The &quot;applying dots towards affects&quot; was what I meant by sub-merit. Tremendously unclear, but I couldn't do the brain&gt;fingers&gt;words thing correctly.<br /> <br /> And awesome, completely missed Hollows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T03:23:49-08:00","id":839776,"title":"","content":"Just for knowing, is the Blessing of Forgetfulness Goblin Contract from Rites of Spring going to make it to the core book of this new edition? Or something similar? Arcadia seems so likely to produce a Contract specifically connected with the fleeting quality of memories ('cause you know, it's always difficult to remember dreams and stuffs like that).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/822-daemonchrno","name":"DaemonChrno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar822_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T05:28:10-08:00","id":839819,"title":"","content":"It is defiantly slated to be put in. I'm sure they won't forget about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T09:03:49-08:00","id":839948,"title":"","content":"Question. Some contracts create an environmental tilt or something that has a variable intensity. Most notable is control elements. However, there are no listed guidelines for how powerful to make these effects. What should we doing for the playtest?<br /> <br /> Offhand... (round up when applicable)<br /> Heavy Winds Severity = Wyrd/2<br /> Inferno = This isn't a tilt. Elements that cause damage deal (Wyrd)B or (Wyrd/2)L damage.<br /> Blizzard = Penalty for depth is equal to Wyrd<br /> Earthquake = Penalty equal to Wyrd/2. Lethal damage equal to half the penalty.<br /> Flooded = As is. Unsure if flooded can ever take water above the person's head. If yes. Penalty equals Wyrd.<br /> <br /> In the case of using an element to attack someone, do you add any skill to the element's strength? How do you determine the damage value?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Maybe a better guideline is... if the element creates a penalty, that penalty is equal to the changeling's Wyrd (max 5). If the element deals damage just by existing, such as through fire or lightning, it deals (Wyrd)B or (Wyrd/2)L rounded up. If the tilt does more than one thing, halve the Changeling's Wyrd before determining it's effrcts. The penalty given by this contract may not exceed -5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 03-01-2016, 12:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T10:12:35-08:00","id":839998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=839398#post839398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could easily imagine that just being part of the Hollow merit: I'd absolutely let them spend a dot of said merit (assuming it functions the same) via the Amenities &amp;quot;sub-merit&amp;quot; for weather patterns.<br /> <br /> For the Seasonal contracts, I believe they're talking about the Seasonal Court's contracts. . .and since there are no &amp;quot;true&amp;quot; official Courts, that means that should mean that said Contracts are made via some &amp;quot;build-a-Contract&amp;quot; rule, or perhaps even &amp;quot;build-a-Court-Contract&amp;quot; rule if Court Contracts are supposed to be even better than normal Contracts.</div> </div> </div> </div> Are Court Contracts better then regular contracts? Or are Court Contracts just cheaper? Or are they regular Contracts that have been altered like a Court effect, simular to Seeming effects?<br /> <br /> I don't know, only the names of the Talespinning Contract and Emotional Contract have been revealed, we still don't know HOW 2e court contracts work in practice compared to universal and Goblin Contracts. Do they have seeming effects, heck do Goblin Contracts have Seeming Effects, I don't know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T10:38:08-08:00","id":840013,"title":"","content":"Actually looking at the platest document we know alittle bit about how Court Contracts work.<br /> <br /> You much be a member (or possibly Court Goodwill), and they are shaped by your Mantle Instead of your Wyrd.<br /> <br /> So where a Universal or Goblin Contract would be Attribute + Skill + Wyrd for activation, a Court Contract is Attribute + Skill + Mantle for activation.<br /> <br /> We also know every court gets an Emotional Contract keyed to the court's emotion and the Talespinning Contract (since its universally available to every court I'm not sure why its not just a universal contract, but I suspect that the contract ties into the Courts individual story some how), and a third contract unique to the Court.<br /> <br /> Also Contracts change your Changeling, likely for Mien some how, and this is likely true for Court Contracts.<br /> <br /> They cost a 1 experience per dot, so they no more expensive then merits.<br /> <br /> That's all we know so far about Court Contracts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T17:22:04-08:00","id":843701,"title":"","content":"Is Hidden Reality's dicepool supposed to not have an attached Skill?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T04:23:39-08:00","id":843894,"title":"","content":"For clarity's sake... Caging a Dream. In earlier reveals, it sounded like you could spend a glamour to shake off handcuffs, escape rope, unlock a prison door, escape a locked safe, cracl open the car trunk youre stuck in, etc. Now, in the playest stuff, it sounds like to escape a place, you can turn a locked door into a door into the Hedge--you cant actually get to where the door physically leads to, you cant unlock the door, but you can escape into the Hedge and use your talents to get from there to somewhere safe (and if your hedge navigation skills are good, maybe you CAN exit on the other side of that exact door). this also contradict's 1e's idea that you cant open a hedge gate using a locked door. Has the locked door limit been changed? do you only escaped locked rooms/cells by entering the hedge? Is this the right way to read it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T06:51:03-08:00","id":843928,"title":"","content":"seems weird that escaping handcuffs, or a grapple would result in you entering the hedge...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T07:31:56-08:00","id":843948,"title":"","content":"Ha, I think its just escaping locked rooms and stuff that uses the hedge, not escaping handcuffs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T09:55:38-08:00","id":844018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> 