darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=973123#post973123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What... What did I just walk in on!?!</div> </div> </div> </div> i had the same thought, but deleted it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T20:23:25-07:00","id":981241,"title":"","content":"By nature of the question I don't know if this is better suited for the errata pass, so I'm asking it here:<br /> <br /> Is Portents and Visions <i>supposed</i> to have the dicepool it does? Only it's identical to that of the next Contract on the list (Riddle-Kith) and its 1e precedents are Wits- and Empathy-based and I'm having some trouble building a coherent rationale for a &quot;see the past or future&quot; Contract using a core roll of Manipulation and Subterfuge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T14:43:12-07:00","id":991129,"title":"","content":"Honestly 2e would have me excited even if it was just Embracing the Wyrd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-21-2016, 05:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T06:28:17-07:00","id":992352,"title":"","content":"I have to say that overall, the second edition is really doing a good job of emphasizing the otherness of Changelings. In the first edition, they didn't really do enough to emphasize how being a Changeling affected just the way a person lived day by day, at least in my opinion. There was mention of it, but 2e really tries and makes it clear that Changelings don't experience the world the same way normal humans do, that their experiences have fundamentally changed the way they think about and interact with things. For example, the Changeling breaking points do a much better job than the original Clarity meter of showing that the Durance means that even something people find insignificant, like a romantic comedy, suddenly means something wholly different to a Changeling. <br /> <br /> Also, I love that there's still room for happy endings. In my opinion 2e makes it harder to get those, but it's still very possible for a character that tries hard enough and works at it to be able to build a life among mortals that, while never the same as the life they had before, can still be just as deep and fulfilling. That's one of the reasons I loved Changeling in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7372-lady-gray","name":"Lady Gray","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7372_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T01:01:53-07:00","id":995545,"title":"","content":"This is kind of a strange thing, but I was just watching the X-Files and the Huntsmen really reminded me of the alien bounty hunters from season 2, both of them being shapeshifting, deceptive, difficult to harm beings from another world who are used by alien beings as enforcers and hunters. I know it could very well be a coincidence, and I acknowledge that they probably weren't based on an X-Files antagonist, but it's one hell of a cool coincidence, since changeling is already ChroD's take on UFO lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T18:01:57-07:00","id":995887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=995545#post995545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is kind of a strange thing, but I was just watching the X-Files and the Huntsmen really reminded me of the alien bounty hunters from season 2, both of them being shapeshifting, deceptive, difficult to harm beings from another world who are used by alien beings as enforcers and hunters. I know it could very well be a coincidence, and I acknowledge that they probably weren't based on an X-Files antagonist, but it's one hell of a cool coincidence, since changeling is already ChroD's take on UFO lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good catch.<br /> <br /> It's partly coincidental, partly not. <br /> <br /> It was a really oblique parallel to alien abduction stories, because that was a thing that was touched on in 1e, but never really explored much. I didn't want to call it out explicitly, but I did like the idea of allowing for that type of story. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T19:09:40-07:00","id":995909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=995887#post995887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good catch.<br /> <br /> It's partly coincidental, partly not. <br /> <br /> It was a really oblique parallel to alien abduction stories, because that was a thing that was touched on in 1e, but never really explored much. I didn't want to call it out explicitly, but I did like the idea of allowing for that type of story. </div> </div> </div> </div>That's really cool! I've always loved the alien abduction connection Changeling had, and I'm glad to see 2e is keeping with it (the Grey kith is super cool). The way 1e drew parallels between folklore and mythology surrounding the Fae and modern UFO and alien lore was one of my favorite things about the game. It's an especially deft move considering the controversy over including aliens in ChroD- changeling provides a way to do that, but in a completely optional fashion that works for both sides. Changeling is pretty much the reason I've been with people who don't think ChroD needs an &quot;aliens&quot; game- because Changeling covers pretty much all of the bases of UFOs and alien folklore and its paranormal connections. It has pod people, UFOs, psychic powers...and you can use the Kith system to make any of the &quot;classic&quot; alien types: Greys, little green men, reptilians, bug people, cyborgs, energy beings, shapeshifters... Watching the X-Files actually made me love Changeling even more, because you can perfectly fit any kind of alien abduction story into it. That CtL can work perfectly as a &quot;dark fairytale&quot; game or an &quot;alien abduction&quot; game, that it reveals some really fascinating cultural parallels while doing so, is a really major achievement. <br /> <br /> And I just realized, the alien bounty hunters are part of the wider &quot;men in black&quot; archetype, where people who investigated or witnessed alien encounters were supposedly harassed and intimidated by strange individuals with anachronistic mannerisms and strange habits, which fits perfectly as a role huntsmen could play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-30-2016, 10:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}